ect letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A complete bilateral cleft palate involves failure of fusion between the palatine processes (from the maxillary prominences) and the nasal septum (derived from the frontonasal process).  \nThe correct combination is the palatine processes and the frontonasal process.  \nThus, the matching option is **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 293}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5209", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With respect to marital satisfaction, most long lasting marriages\n\nOptions: \nA. Show lower levels during the years when children are present\nB. Show constant low satisfaction throughout the marriage\nC. Show high satisfaction through all the years of marriage\nD. Show a steady increase in satisfaction throughout the marriage, regardless of children's presence\nE. Show ups and downs throughout the marriage\nF. Show low satisfaction in the early years, which increases as the years pass\nG. Show high satisfaction only during the years when children are present\nH. Show high satisfaction that steadily declines as the years pass\nI. Show high satisfaction only after children have left the home\nJ. Show high satisfaction in the early years, which gradually increases over time\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Research in marital satisfaction suggests that the presence of children often reduces marital satisfaction due to increased demands, and satisfaction tends to increase again after children leave home. Therefore, the most likely correct answer is that most long-lasting marriages show lower levels during the years when children are present.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 268}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4990", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Men are more likely than women to die from\n\nOptions: \nA. Breast Cancer\nB. Influenza\nC. Stroke\nD. Suicide\nE. Asthma\nF. Heart Disease\nG. Septicemia\nH. Lung Cancer\nI. Osteoporosis\nJ. Alzheimer's Disease\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on mortality statistics, men have a higher death rate than women for **heart disease**, which is the leading cause of death for both genders but disproportionately affects men.  \nWhile men also have higher mortality for some other options (like lung cancer or suicide), heart disease accounts for the greatest overall number of excess male deaths.  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 213}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4938", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With respect to job training, younger workers\n\nOptions: \nA. Have less experience and therefore need more training\nB. Do not benefit from training as much as older workers do\nC. Are less open to feedback than older workers\nD. Prefer to have classes by themselves\nE. Always learn faster than older workers\nF. Always perform worse on the job than trained older workers\nG. Receive more opportunities than older workers\nH. Are not interested in job training\nI. Perform better on the job than trained older workers\nJ. Prefer online training over traditional classroom learning\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on typical findings in workplace training research, younger workers often have less experience and thus require more initial training to build foundational skills.  \n\nThe most likely correct answer is:  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 270}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5539", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An ileostomy opening should be:\n\nOptions: \nA. less than 1cm in length.\nB. invisible to the naked eye.\nC. 3-5cm in length.\nD. below skin level.\nE. protruding 10cm from the skin.\nF. over 10cm in length.\nG. over 5cm in length.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C** because an ileostomy is typically constructed to protrude 2\u20133 cm, and a length of 3\u20135 cm helps prevent skin irritation and ensures proper appliance fit.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 176}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5134", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The WHO made a strong recommendation that the maximum intake of free sugars by individuals within populations should be\n\n\nOptions: \nA. 10-15%\nB. >20%\nC. <10%\nD. >15%\nE. <5%\nF. >10%\nG. <15%\nH. 15-20%\nI. <20%\nJ. 5-10%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The WHO recommends that free sugars should make up **less than 10%** of total energy intake, with a conditional recommendation of further reduction to below 5% for additional health benefits.  \nAmong the options, **<10%** matches the strong recommendation.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5037", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Public health ethics is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Primarily concerned with the health of healthcare workers\nB. Subject-centered\nC. Patient-centered\nD. Population-centered\nE. Centered around the health of the elderly population\nF. Based on the principle of \"first do no harm\"\nG. Concerned with the health of individual families\nH. Solely focused on the prevention of disease\nI. Focused on the health of animals\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Public health ethics is fundamentally concerned with the health of communities and populations, not just individuals. Among the options, the one that best captures this focus is \"population-centered.\"  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 172, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 225}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4857", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Poliovirus can most easily become more virulent by which of the following processes?\n\nOptions: \nA. Altering its mode of transmission\nB. Increasing its replication speed\nC. Recombining with another enterovirus\nD. Multiple nucleotide deletions and substitutions\nE. Developing resistance to antiviral medications\nF. Mutation of the RNA genome at only a few positions\nG. Developing a secondary protein coat\nH. Increasing the complexity of its RNA genome\nI. Altering its protein coat\nJ. Merging with a bacteriophage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **F. Mutation of the RNA genome at only a few positions** because poliovirus has an RNA genome with high mutation rates, and small changes in key genomic regions can significantly increase virulence without requiring major genomic restructuring.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 175, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 230}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4868", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The patient's self-report of pain is important because health care staff:\n\nOptions: \nA. can determine the patient's pain threshold.\nB. can overestimate the intensity of the patient's pain.\nC. can compare it with other patients' pain levels.\nD. do not possess an objective way of assessing pain.\nE. can use the information to prescribe and administer the maximum possible amount of pain relief.\nF. underestimate the intensity of the patient's pain.\nG. are able to visually assess the patient's pain level.\nH. can measure the patient's pain with medical instruments.\nI. can use the information to prescribe and administer the least possible amount of pain relief.\nJ. can ignore the patient's pain.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because pain is subjective, and there is no reliable objective measure or instrument to assess it directly.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 246, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 283}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4869", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The docility hypothesis is that\n\nOptions: \nA. Those who experience low environmental demands become less docile\nB. Those with less capability are less vulnerable to environmental demands\nC. Those with low capabilities are more vulnerable to environmental demands\nD. Those with high capabilities become less vulnerable to environmental demands\nE. Those with high capabilities are more vulnerable to environmental demands\nF. Those who experience high environmental demands become less docile\nG. Those with high capability become less docile in low environmental demands\nH. Those who experience low environmental demands become more docile\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The docility hypothesis in lifespan developmental psychology states that individuals with lower capabilities are more susceptible to the influence of their environment, making them more vulnerable to its demands. This matches option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 231, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 292}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4908", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following rules regarding the interconversion of fuels are central to the integration of metabolic pathways?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Fatty acids can be made from and converted to carbohydrates and amino acids\nB. Carbohydrates can be made from and converted to amino acids and fatty acids\nC. Fatty acids can be made from but not converted to carbohydrates and amino acids\nD. Amino acids can be made from and converted to fatty acids\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**C** \u2014 Fatty acids cannot be converted back to carbohydrates in humans because acetyl-CoA cannot be reconverted to pyruvate, and most amino acids are glucogenic but cannot be synthesized from fatty acids.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 199}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4926", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The World Systems Theory divides the world as a unit into three subcategories: core countries, periphery countries, and semi-periphery countries. Which of the following answers correlates best with semi-periphery countries?\n\nOptions: \nA. Small percentage of very high class individuals.\nB. Highly industrialized and technologically advanced nations.\nC. Countries with a high rate of population growth.\nD. Strong central government.\nE. High rates of urbanization.\nF. Economies dependent on foreign aid.\nG. Low income, agrarian societies.\nH. Countries with no natural resources.\nI. A diversified and developed economy.\nJ. An economy centralized around one natural resource.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on World Systems Theory, semi-periphery countries are intermediate in development, having both core-like and periphery-like characteristics. The best match from the options is **I. A diversified and developed economy**, as they often have more diversified economies than periphery countries but are not as advanced as core countries.  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 190, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 257}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4936", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The perspective that development is embedded in history means that\n\nOptions: \nA. Only physical development is influenced by age\nB. Some characteristics change with age while others do not\nC. All individuals experience development at the same pace\nD. Development is dependent solely on genetic factors\nE. Developmental changes are always positive\nF. Sociocultural conditions must always be considered\nG. Development in any particular areas (e.g., social) is tied to development in other areas (e.g., cognitive)\nH. Development is unaffected by external influences\nI. Change can always occur regardless of age\nJ. History has no impact on individual development\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **F**, because the statement that development is embedded in history emphasizes that sociocultural and historical contexts shape developmental pathways.  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 236, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 282}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4962", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has been observed that a reduction in family size and improved sanitary condition have led to an increase in allergic conditions. The 'hygiene hypothesis' suggests that\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Living on a working farm will increase the development of atopic diseases\nB. Particular care must be taken during breast feeding in high risk infants\nC. Living on a working farm will help reducing the development of atopic diseases\nD. Using antibiotics frequently will reduce allergies\nE. Living in urban areas will help reduce the development of atopic diseases\nF. The frequent use of antiseptic swipes will reduce allergies\nG. Exposure to allergens in early childhood will increase the risk of developing allergies\nH. Staying in highly sanitized environments will reduce the development of atopic diseases\nI. Breastfeeding should be avoided in high risk infants to prevent allergies\nJ. The use of probiotics in infants will increase the development of atopic diseases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The hygiene hypothesis proposes that reduced early childhood exposure to microbes (as in smaller families and highly sanitized environments) increases the risk of allergic/atopic diseases.  \nTherefore, increased microbial exposure, such as living on a working farm, is thought to protect against atopic diseases.  \n\nCorrect choice: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 311, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 396}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4969", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following could lead to iodine deficiency?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Living at high altitudes\nB. Excessive consumption of fast food\nC. Intake only of locally grown food in central Africa\nD. Low intake of dairy products\nE. Drinking too much water\nF. Lack of physical activity\nG. Low intake of fruits and vegetables\nH. Inadequate sunlight exposure\nI. Insufficient caloric intake\nJ. Overconsumption of caffeinated beverages\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **C. Intake only of locally grown food in central Africa** because iodine deficiency often occurs in regions with iodine-poor soil, and relying solely on local food from such areas (like parts of central Africa) can lead to insufficient iodine intake.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 178, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 252}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4980", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient comes into the hospital after being bit by a dog who he stated was \u201cacting crazy\u201d. The wound is open and bleeding. Animal control captured the dog and said that it was foaming at the mouth and extremely aggressive. Suspecting a rabies infection, the patient is given a serum that contains rabies antibodies that were grown inside a horse. This is an example of what kind of immunity?\n\nOptions: \nA. Passive\nB. Acquired\nC. Passive natural\nD. Natural\nE. Active artificial\nF. Passive artificial\nG. Active natural\nH. Artificial\nI. Innate\nJ. Active\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient is receiving pre-formed antibodies from another species (horse), which provides immediate but temporary protection without stimulating the patient\u2019s own immune system. This is an example of **passive artificial immunity**.  \n\nCorrect choice: \\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 275}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4984", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true regarding the complications of a large goitre?\n\nOptions: \nA. It causes tinnitus due to compression of the auditory canal\nB. It causes severe headaches due to increased pressure in the neck area\nC. It causes shortness of breath due to compression of the lungs\nD. It causes hoarseness due to compression of the trachea\nE. It causes a more florid thyrotoxicosis than a smaller goitre\nF. It can cause hyperthyroidism due to overproduction of thyroid hormones\nG. It causes stridor due to compression of the oesophagus\nH. It leads to a decreased production of thyroid hormones causing hypothyroidism\nI. It increases the risk of thyroid cancer\nJ. Dysphagia is an indication for surgery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **J**, because dysphagia from esophageal compression is a recognized complication of a large goiter and a common indication for surgical intervention. Other options are incorrect: stridor arises from tracheal (not esophageal) compression, hoarseness is from recurrent laryngeal nerve compression, and goiter size does not inherently correlate with more severe thyrotoxicosis or cause hypothyroidism solely due to size.\n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 249, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 364}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4987", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The reaction time difference between younger and older adults is reduced when older adults\n\nOptions: \nA. Practice regular aerobic exercise\nB. Lift weights on a regular schedule\nC. Read for at least an hour every day\nD. Consume large quantities of vitamins\nE. Consume high protein diet\nF. Take regular afternoon naps\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on research in cognitive aging, regular aerobic exercise has been shown to improve cognitive function and processing speed in older adults, which can help reduce reaction time differences compared to younger adults.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 151, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 212}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5026", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true about dietary calcium:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Typical calcium intake in most adults is between 0.5mg and 2.0mg per day\nB. Activated Vitamin D decreases absorption of dietary calcium\nC. There is clear evidence that people who consume more than the average amount of calcium have a lower risk of bone fractures.\nD. Absorption efficiency is inversely related to calcium intake, so that a higher proportion is absorbed when calcium intake is low\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because the body adapts to low calcium intake by increasing the fractional absorption in the intestines.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 156, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 186}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5046", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One line of evidence against antagonistic pleiotropy is that\n\nOptions: \nA. Exercise increases rather than decreases longevity\nB. Senescence can also be observed in cells with short telomere strands\nC. Women who have more children tend to live longer\nD. Certain species have shown no signs of aging\nE. The genetic mutation rate increases with age\nF. Even tissue cells with longer telomere strands can show senescence\nG. Senescence is observed in all living organisms\nH. Caloric restriction extends lifespan in many species\nI. Some animals show little or no senescence\nJ. Organisms with fewer offspring have a longer lifespan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **I. Some animals show little or no senescence**, because if aging is due to antagonistic pleiotropy (genes with early-life benefits but late-life costs), we would expect senescence to be universal, but its absence in some species contradicts that.  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 193, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 254}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5054", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mutations that cause achondroplasia exert an effect which can be classified as:\n\nOptions: \nA. recessive negative.\nB. haplosufficiency.\nC. neutral mutation.\nD. loss-of-function.\nE. recessive positive.\nF. gain-of-function.\nG. dominant negative.\nH. gain-of-regulation.\nI. haploinsufficiency.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Most cases of achondroplasia are caused by a specific mutation in the FGFR3 gene that leads to overactive signaling, which inhibits bone growth. This is best described as a **gain-of-function** mutation.  \nThe correct choice is: \\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5081", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which single statement about fat digestion and absorption is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Absorption of fatty acids in the intestine occurs mainly through FABP and FAT/CD36 transport proteins in the enterocytes of the distal duodenum\nB. After absorption, medium chain triglycerides (MCT) enter the lymphatic system, whereas long chain triglycerides enter the portal blood system.\nC. The products of partial digestion of triglycerides (triacylglycerols) can form mixed micelles with pancreatic cholesterol and phospholipids and this increases absorption\nD. Triglycerides (triacylglycerols) must be emulsified and digested before the fatty acids can be transported\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Correct answer:** D  \n**Reasoning:** Triglycerides are insoluble in water and must be emulsified (by bile salts) and enzymatically digested (by lipases) before their fatty acids can be efficiently transported into enterocytes.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 236, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 296}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5101", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the risk if water is used for bladder washout in secondary care?\n\nOptions: \nA. The medical staff may be unhappy.\nB. The patient may experience discomfort.\nC. Fluid may bypass when the washout is carried out.\nD. Using water may cause a urinary tract infection.\nE. There is no risk in using water for bladder washout.\nF. It may lead to kidney damage.\nG. The procedure may need to be repeated.\nH. Using water may cause electrolyte imbalance.\nI. Bladder washout may be unsuccessful.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **H**, as sterile water (unlike saline) can cause hemolysis and fluid absorption leading to electrolyte imbalance, especially during bladder irrigation in patients with open mucosal surfaces.\n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 171, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 221}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5104", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One reason that older adults show high levels of optimism is that\n\nOptions: \nA. Our measures have low validity\nB. Many pessimists die at a younger age\nC. Their cognitive abilities decline with age\nD. They do not really know what is going on\nE. They tend to focus on the past rather than the future\nF. This may be a warning sign for dementia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **B**, as selective mortality (where individuals with lower optimism may have higher mortality rates earlier in life) is a documented factor in aging research.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 180}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5105", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bu is often late for appointments but says it's because she had more important things on her mind. This is an example of which coping strategy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Projection\nB. Regression\nC. Immunization\nD. Assimilation\nE. Avoidance\nF. Displacement\nG. Denial\nH. Accommodation\nI. Sublimation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The behavior described involves justifying lateness by focusing on other priorities, which is a way of avoiding responsibility for being late. This aligns with **avoidance** as a coping strategy.\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5110", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One reason that older adults may have difficulty in retrieving memories is that\n\nOptions: \nA. There are many more memories to search through to find the one that is sought\nB. The aging brain is less capable of accessing long-term memory\nC. Memory is less well organized as we grow older and finding a memory can be quite difficult\nD. Older adults intentionally suppress certain memories\nE. Memory retrieval is physically tiring for older adults\nF. Older adults are less capable of forming new memories\nG. Long-term memory often discards older and unused memories\nH. Memory retrieval is often affected by external distractions faced by older adults\nI. The process of memory retrieval slows down significantly with age\nJ. Older adults quit searching because they have more important things to do\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **I**, as research on cognitive aging consistently shows that processing speed, including memory retrieval, slows with age.\n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 257}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5113", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With which of the following relatives is an individual most likely to share a common HLA haplotype?\n\nOptions: \nA. Son\nB. Nephew\nC. Aunt\nD. Sister\nE. Cousin\nF. Grandmother\nG. Uncle\nH. Grandfather\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An individual shares a **complete HLA haplotype** most reliably with a **sibling** who inherited the same two haplotypes from their parents.  \n\nAmong the options, **sister** is the only sibling, while others (son, aunt, cousin, etc.) have a lower probability of sharing an entire haplotype.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5120", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Laryngeal oedema is usually confined to the larynx above the vocal folds because\n\nOptions: \nA. laryngeal oedema is not confined to any particular area of the larynx\nB. fluid will drain rapidly into the thorax below the vocal folds.\nC. there are numerous mucous glands in the vestibular folds.\nD. the vocal folds have a protective layer that prevents oedema\nE. the larynx below the vocal folds is more susceptible to inflammation\nF. the mucosa below the vocal folds absorbs fluid more rapidly\nG. the mucosa covering the vocal folds is tightly attached to underlying tissues.\nH. there are fewer blood vessels in the area below the vocal folds\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G** because the mucosa of the vocal folds is tightly bound to the underlying vocal ligament, limiting edema formation there, while the supraglottic tissues are looser and allow fluid accumulation.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 232, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 289}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5132", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Intestinal motility is a complex process, orchestrated by nerves, hormones and the presence of food in the stomach. Which statement about this process is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. At the start of a meal, the stomach increases its \"tone\" in order to develop pressure which will lead to expulsion of its contents, via the pylorus\nB. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum, speeds up intestinal motility\nC. The migrating motor complex is chiefly responsible for the absorption of nutrients after a meal has been consumed\nD. The migrating motor complex is chiefly responsible for peristaltic movement of food after a meal has been consumed\nE. The release of glucagon after eating a meal will speed up the emptying of the stomach\nF. The stomach decreases its \"tone\" at the end of a meal to develop pressure which will lead to expulsion of its contents, via the pylorus\nG. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum, slows intestinal motility\nH. The release of insulin after eating a meal will speed up the emptying of the stomach\nI. The presence of partially digested protein and fiber in the duodenum, speeds up intestinal motility\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on physiology, the presence of nutrients like fat and carbohydrates in the duodenum triggers inhibitory feedback (via hormones like CCK and GLP-1) to slow gastric emptying and intestinal motility to allow adequate time for digestion and absorption.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:  \n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 306, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 367}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5136", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When using bioelectrical impedance for measuring body composition, why does an electrical current travel faster through muscle than it does through fat?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Fat conducts electricity better than muscle\nB. Fat is denser than muscle\nC. Fat contains less water than muscle\nD. Muscle weighs more than fat\nE. Muscle contains less water than fat\nF. Muscle is denser than fat\nG. Muscle contains more water than fat\nH. Fat contains more electrolytes than muscle\nI. Muscle contains more electrolytes than fat\nJ. Muscle weighs less than fat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G. Muscle contains more water than fat**.  \nBioelectrical impedance relies on the conductivity of tissues, and since muscle has a higher water and electrolyte content, it conducts electricity faster than fat, which is less hydrated.  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 274}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5140", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does the papilloma family of viruses cause cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. Alters the host's immune response to cancer cells\nB. Mutates the host's DNA, leading to uncontrolled cell growth\nC. Stimulates cell division, leading to overgrowth and cancer formation\nD. Acts as a co factor for a cellular oncogene\nE. Produces toxins that damage cellular DNA\nF. Causes inflammation and cell death, leading to cancer\nG. Integrates viral genome into cellular DNA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C** because human papillomaviruses (HPV) produce proteins like E6 and E7 that stimulate continuous cell division, overriding normal growth controls and leading to cancerous overgrowth.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 184, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 238}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5144", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Muscle lactate production increases when:\n\nOptions: \nA. the muscle is fully hydrated.\nB. oxygen levels in the muscle are low.\nC. glucose levels in the muscle are low.\nD. oxygen is readily available.\nE. the pH of the muscle falls.\nF. the muscle is at rest.\nG. pyruvate cannot be formed from glucose breakdown.\nH. glycolysis is activated at the onset of exercise.\nI. the muscle experiences a sudden drop in temperature.\nJ. the muscle is in a state of relaxation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because lactate production increases under anaerobic conditions when oxygen levels are low, allowing glycolysis to continue by regenerating NAD\u207a.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 164, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5152", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Social support is most likely to have a positive influence on health and well being when it is\n\nOptions: \nA. Provided only in a crisis situation\nB. Very emotional\nC. Unexpected\nD. Perceived as support\nE. Given without the recipient's knowledge\nF. External rather than internal\nG. Constant and unwavering regardless of circumstances\nH. Financial in nature\nI. Provided solely through online platforms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**, because perceived support is what actually reduces stress and improves well-being, regardless of the objective amount or type of support given.  \nIf support is not seen as helpful or caring by the recipient, it may not benefit health.  \nThus, the perception of being supported matters more than the support\u2019s form or timing.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 172, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 263}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5202", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true about an abdominal mass?\n\nOptions: \nA. An indentible mass is caused by faecal loading of the colon\nB. A non-tender mass is always indicative of a benign tumor\nC. A hard mass is always a symptom of colorectal cancer\nD. An enlarged kidney is dull to percussion\nE. A movable mass is a definite sign of a hernia\nF. A large mass arising out of the pelvis which disappears following urethral catheterization is caused by an ovarian cyst\nG. A mass that changes size is always due to a bladder infection\nH. A mass that disappears after eating is caused by a stomach ulcer\nI. A pulsatile mass is always due to an aortic aneurysm\nJ. A painful mass is always a symptom of gallstones\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D. An enlarged kidney is dull to percussion** because kidneys are solid organs located retroperitoneally, and solid organs typically produce dullness on percussion.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 263}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5264", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true about rectal bleeding?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hemorrhoids are never a cause of rectal bleeding\nB. A painful digital examination suggests an anal fissure\nC. A colonoscopy is not necessary if rectal bleeding is present\nD. Rectal cancer is the commonest cause of rectal bleeding\nE. Bright red blood on the finger usually signifies a caecal lesion\nF. Rectal bleeding is always a sign of cancer\nG. Proctoscopy is of no value in the assessment of rectal bleeding\nH. Rectal bleeding is not a symptom of diverticulosis\nI. Rectal bleeding is always accompanied by pain\nJ. A negative colonoscopy rules out all causes of rectal bleeding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**, as a painful digital rectal exam is characteristic of an anal fissure due to the associated tenderness.  \n\nOther options are incorrect: hemorrhoids are a common cause (A false), colonoscopy is often needed (C false), rectal cancer is not the commonest cause (D false), and bright red blood usually indicates a distal source, not cecal (E false).  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 300}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5309", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How are antibody producing cells stimulated?\n\nOptions: \nA. Interacting with a virus short peptide\nB. Interacting with a T helper cell.\nC. Interacting with a plasma cell\nD. Interacting with a virus infected cell\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because antibody-producing B cells require activation by helper T cells, which occurs after antigen presentation and co-stimulatory signals.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5322", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Do traits change with age?\n\nOptions: \nA. They change a little\nB. They only change due to major life events\nC. Only after the age of 60\nD. Only in childhood\nE. Only for women\nF. They change drastically\nG. No\nH. Only for men\nI. They change quite a lot\nJ. They don't change at all\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on psychological research, personality traits show some stability but also gradual change across the lifespan, with the most significant shifts occurring in young adulthood and continuing at a slower pace later. This means traits generally change a little over time rather than remaining completely fixed or changing drastically.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 231}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5354", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best explains the antioxidant action of vitamin E?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. It is lipid soluble and can react with free radicals in the bloodstream resulting from nitric oxide formation by vascular epithelium\nB. It forms an unstable radical that can be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with vitamin C\nC. It is lipid soluble and can react with free radicals in the bloodstream resulting from carbon dioxide formation by vascular epithelium\nD. It is converted to an unstable radical by reaction with vitamin C\nE. It is water soluble and can react with free radicals in the bloodstream resulting from nitric oxide formation by vascular epithelium\nF. It forms a stable radical that can be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with vitamin B12.\nG. It forms a stable radical that can be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with vitamin C\nH. It forms a stable radical that cannot be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with glutathione and glutathione peroxidase\nI. It is converted to a stable radical by reaction with vitamin C\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G** because vitamin E (\u03b1-tocopherol) acts as a lipid-soluble antioxidant by forming a relatively stable tocopheroxyl radical after scavenging free radicals, and this radical can be regenerated back to active vitamin E by vitamin C (ascorbate).  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 340, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 410}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5405", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Endurance type exercise training modulates fuel storage and substrate use. Adaptive responses include:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. lowering intramuscular lipid storage\nB. Increasing liver glycogen content\nC. Increasing muscle glycogen use during exercise\nD. Increasing intramuscular lipid use during exercise\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Endurance training enhances the ability to use fat as a fuel source, which includes increasing the utilization of intramuscular lipids during exercise to spare glycogen. This matches option D, while the other options are either opposite to typical adaptations (A and C) or not a primary direct adaptation of endurance training in muscle (B).\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 234}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5413", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The amount and composition of dietary fat are important factors for influencing blood lipid metabolism. Which of the following statements is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids is associated with an increase in plasma triglyceride concentrations\nB. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated fatty acids is associated with a decrease in HDL cholesterol\nC. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with large amounts of carbohydrate is associated with decreased LDL and increased plasma triglyceride concentrations\nD. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated fatty acids is associated with an increase in LDL cholesterol\nE. Consumption of soluble dietary fibre and plant stanols/sterols is associated with a significant increases in LDL cholesterol\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on nutritional science, replacing saturated fat with high amounts of carbohydrates can lower LDL cholesterol but often raises triglycerides.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 236}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5427", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Measuring the blood pressure in an arm that is above the level of the heart will:\n\nOptions: \nA. cause an auscultatory gap.\nB. accurately estimate the blood pressure.\nC. lead to a misleading diastolic reading.\nD. underestimate the blood pressure.\nE. cause a spike in the blood pressure.\nF. overestimate the blood pressure.\nG. cause a false high reading.\nH. have no effect on the blood pressure reading.\nI. result in an inaccurate pulse reading.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When the arm is above heart level, gravity reduces the effective pressure, leading to a lower reading than the actual blood pressure. Therefore, the measurement would **underestimate** the blood pressure.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 183, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 237}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5433", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you believe that we are mostly in control of our own development and that our behaviors, good or bad, determine how successful our aging with be, you would be said to have which of the following perspectives?\n\nOptions: \nA. Continuity\nB. Discontinuity\nC. Organismic\nD. Nurture\nE. Dynamic Systems\nF. Stochastic\nG. Nature\nH. Mechanistic\nI. Evolutionary\nJ. Contextual\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This perspective emphasizes personal agency and behavior as drivers of development, aligning most closely with a **mechanistic** view, which sees individuals as proactive controllers of their outcomes.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 153, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 195}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5437", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A baby born with pulmonary hypoplasia secondary to oligohydramnios caused by renal agenesis would be classified as having:\n\nOptions: \nA. an association.\nB. a disruption.\nC. a syndrome.\nD. a deformation.\nE. a dysplasia.\nF. a sequence.\nG. a phenotype.\nH. a spectrum.\nI. a malformation.\nJ. a complex.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **F. a sequence** because renal agenesis leads to oligohydramnios, which in turn causes pulmonary hypoplasia\u2014a cascade of events initiated by a single anomaly. This fits the definition of a sequence, where one primary defect results in secondary structural changes. The other terms do not accurately describe this chain of causation.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 237}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5472", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Toxicity and dose-response data from animal studies, together with data of which of the following types, are used to evaluate the safety of a food substance?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The price of the food to which the substance is added\nB. The concentration of the substance in food\nC. The amount of the substance that is excreted by the human body\nD. The amount of the substance that is naturally present in the human body\nE. The quantity of the substance sold in supermarkets\nF. The yearly intake of the substance by animals consuming the food\nG. The daily intake of the substance by humans consuming the food\nH. The total amount of the substance a person will consume over a lifetime\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G** because safety evaluations for food substances rely on estimated human exposure levels, which are based on daily intake from the diet.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 241, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 284}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5473", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The pancreas secretes a large amount of digestive enzymes after a meal. Which statement about this process is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Bile is needed to activate all pancreatic enzymes\nB. All pancreatic enzymes are produced in an active form and can start digestion immediately\nC. Enzymes are produced in the pancreas but released in the stomach for digestion\nD. Pepsinogen is the chief enzyme which digests protein and requires removal of a peptide sequence from the active cleft before it can work\nE. Pancreatic secretion of hydrochloric acid is required to provide the correct pH for maximal pancreatic enzyme in the duodenum\nF. Enteropeptidase converts trypsinogen to trypsin by cleavage of a peptide sequence that blocks the active site of trypsin.\nG. Pancreatic enzymes are needed to break down carbohydrates only.\nH. Pancreatic \u00e1-amylase will hydrolyse starch to free glucose\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **F**, because enteropeptidase (an intestinal brush-border enzyme) cleaves trypsinogen to its active form trypsin by removing an inhibitory peptide, initiating the pancreatic protease cascade.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 292, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 348}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5477", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What happens during the 'incubation period'?\n\nOptions: \nA. The virus mutates and becomes more virulent\nB. This period commonly lasts for a few hours\nC. Virus replication happens at an intracellular level\nD. Symptoms of the disease start appearing in the host\nE. The virus is spread to others without any symptoms in the host\nF. The host's body becomes immune to the virus\nG. The virus is cleared from the body by the immune system\nH. This period commonly lasts for a few years\nI. The virus is dormant and does not replicate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C**, because during the incubation period, the virus replicates inside host cells, but symptoms are not yet apparent.\n\nOther options are incorrect: symptoms appear after incubation (D), transmission often occurs during incubation in some diseases (E) but isn't a definition of the period itself, and the duration is variable but not typically just a few hours or years (B, H).\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 180, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 265}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5497", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Those more likely to experience depression after a loss are those who\n\nOptions: \nA. Have a strong social support network\nB. Have no previous history of mental health issues\nC. Have not previously experienced depression\nD. Have a high income\nE. Have been married less than a year\nF. Are young survivors\nG. Are in good health\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **F. Are young survivors**, as younger individuals often have less coping experience and are more vulnerable to prolonged grief and depression after a loss.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Older adults are able to improve their memories and reduce their anxiety about declining memory when\n\nOptions: \nA. They engage in social activities and interact with peers\nB. They practice mindfulness and meditation to reduce stress levels\nC. They engage in physical activity regularly\nD. They regularly solve puzzles and engage in brain-stimulating activities\nE. They learn that many aspects of memory do not decline and some even get better\nF. They simply learn a number of memory improvement techniques\nG. They take memory-enhancing medications\nH. They learn about memory and aging and learn some techniques\nI. They consume a diet rich in antioxidants and omega-3 fatty acids\nJ. Older adults cannot do either of these\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **H**, as research shows that education about normal memory changes with age combined with practical techniques reduces anxiety and can improve performance.\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 238}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5546", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Loss of stomach lining can lead to symptoms that resemble\n\nOptions: \nA. Diabetes\nB. Dementia\nC. Osteoporosis\nD. Tuberculosis\nE. Hepatitis\nF. Senescence\nG. Leukemia\nH. Anorexia\nI. Parkinson's disease\nJ. Hypertension\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Loss of stomach lining can impair vitamin B12 absorption, leading to pernicious anemia and neurological symptoms such as memory loss or confusion, which may resemble dementia. Among the options, dementia is the condition most closely associated with these neurological effects.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 198}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5572", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about the protein requirement is correct\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The protein requirement can be less than the demand.\nB. The protein requirement is equal to the demand minus the efficiency of utilization.\nC. The protein requirement is equal to the demand divided by the efficiency of utilization.\nD. The protein requirement is always higher than the demand.\nE. The protein requirement is the same for all individuals regardless of age or health status.\nF. The protein requirement is equal to the demand multiplied by the efficiency of utilization.\nG. The protein requirement is always the same as the demand.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C** because protein requirement accounts for how efficiently the body uses protein, so requirement = demand / efficiency of utilization.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 230, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 273}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5574", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The effects of iron on certain aspects of socio-emotional development (shyness, orientation/engagement and response to unfamiliar pictures) is due to:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The role of iron in serotonin production\nB. None of the above\nC. The role of iron in neurochemistry\nD. The role of iron in maintaining blood sugar levels\nE. The role of iron in muscle function\nF. The role of iron in energy metabolism\nG. The role of iron in dopamine production\nH. The role of iron in myelination\nI. The role of iron in cognitive development\nJ. The role of iron in red blood cell production\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks about iron\u2019s role in socio-emotional development aspects like shyness and engagement.  \nResearch links iron to neurotransmitter synthesis, particularly dopamine, which affects reward, motivation, and social behavior.  \nThus, the most likely direct mechanism here is iron\u2019s involvement in dopamine production.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 193, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 261}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4977", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A team of engineers constructing signal lights for airplanes that they can use to guide them to runways are attempting to determine the brightness needed for the pilot to be able to detect the tower at 1 mile away. They set the light to a test brightness and establish communication with an inbound pilot. When the pilot is 1 mile away from the tower, he says he cannot see the light. In terms of Signal Detection Theory, what would this be called?\n\nOptions: \nA. True negative\nB. False positive\nC. Incorrect rejection\nD. Correct hit\nE. False alarm\nF. Hit\nG. False negative\nH. Miss\nI. True positive\nJ. Correct rejection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Signal Detection Theory, when a signal (the light) is present but the observer (the pilot) reports not seeing it, that is called a **miss**.  \n\nAmong the options, both \u201cmiss\u201d and \u201cfalse negative\u201d describe this, but \u201cmiss\u201d is the more standard SDT term for this outcome.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 283}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5157", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What would be the frequency of AABBCC individuals from a mating of two AaBbCc individuals?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.0/4\nB. 1.0/512\nC. 1.0/1024\nD. 1.0/32\nE. 1.0/2\nF. 1.0/64\nG. 1.0/8\nH. 1.0/16\nI. 1.0/128\nJ. 1.0/256\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For a cross between two triple heterozygotes (AaBbCc \u00d7 AaBbCc), the probability of a homozygous recessive genotype (aa) at one locus is 1/4.  \nSince the loci are independent, the probability of AABBCC (homozygous dominant at all three loci) is also (1/4)\u00b3 = 1/64.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 197}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4861", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using this formula, if a reaction was provided with 84g of ethane and unlimited oxygen, how many grams of carbon dioxide would result (Carbon atomic weight: 12amu, Hydrogen atomic weight: 1amu, Oxygen atomic weight: 16amu)?\n\ufeff\nThe unbalanced reaction of ethane gas to carbon dioxide and water is as follows:\n\n C2H4 + O2 \u2014> CO2 + H2O\n\nOptions: \nA. 78g\nB. 210g\nC. 312g\nD. 528g\nE. 156g\nF. 44g\nG. 264g\nH. 180g\nI. 132g\nJ. 396g\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "First, balance the combustion reaction:  \nC\u2082H\u2084 + 3 O\u2082 \u2192 2 CO\u2082 + 2 H\u2082O.  \n\nMolar mass of C\u2082H\u2084 = (2 \u00d7 12) + (4 \u00d7 1) = 28 g/mol.  \nMoles of C\u2082H\u2084 in 84 g = 84 / 28 = 3 mol.  \n\nFrom the balanced equation, 1 mol C\u2082H\u2084 produces 2 mol CO\u2082, so 3 mol C\u2082H\u2084 produces 6 mol CO\u2082.  \nMolar mass of CO\u2082 = 12 + (2 \u00d7 16) = 44 g/mol.  \nMass of CO\u2082 = 6 \u00d7 44 = 264 g.  \n\nThat matches option **G**.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 176, "total_tokens": 385}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4919", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a very weak base, the pKb of a solution would likely be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Near 14 at 25\u00baC\nB. Lower than the pOH\nC. Lower than the pH\nD. Equal to the pOH\nE. Near 0 at 25\u00baC\nF. Higher than the pH\nG. Near 7 at 25\u00baC\nH. Higher than the pOH\nI. Equal to the pKa\nJ. Equal to the pH\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For a very weak base, \\(K_b\\) is very small, so \\(pK_b = -\\log K_b\\) is large. At 25\u00b0C, a large \\(pK_b\\) means a value close to 14.  \n\nCorrect choice: \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 168, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 227}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5360", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following cannot be a substrate for gluconeogenesis?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Palmitic acid\nB. Pyruvate\nC. Galactose\nD. Glycerol\nE. Propionic acid\nF. Lactic acid\nG. Aspartic acid\nH. Alanine\nI. Glutamic acid\nJ. Oxaloacetate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Palmitic acid cannot be a substrate for gluconeogenesis because fatty acids with an even number of carbon atoms (like palmitic acid, a 16-carbon saturated fatty acid) yield acetyl-CoA, which cannot be converted to glucose in animals. All other listed molecules can be converted to glucose via gluconeogenic pathways.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 210}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4912", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Newborn infants in countries with limited access to safe water and low levels of education should be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Exclusively formula fed for six months\nB. Exclusively breast fed for six months\nC. Should receive both breast milk and other foods as tolerated in the first 6\nD. months\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on global health guidelines, the safest and most recommended practice in such settings is exclusive breastfeeding to reduce infection risks and ensure adequate nutrition.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 195}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5421", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A race car attempting to jump a series of 8 buses is set up on a flat track with a ramp at the end. Engineers assigned to the project have determined that, in order to jump the buses, the car must reach a velocity of 130 km/h. If the distance of the track is 50m, at what rate must the car accelerate to reach this velocity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 26 m/s^2\nB. 22 m/s^2\nC. 10 m/s^2\nD. 20 m/s^2\nE. 17 m/s^2\nF. 15 m/s^2\nG. 7 m/s^2\nH. 13 m/s^2\nI. 18 m/s^2\nJ. 30 m/s^2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We can use the kinematic equation \\( v^2 = u^2 + 2 a s \\), with initial velocity \\( u = 0 \\), final velocity \\( v = 130 \\, \\text{km/h} \\), and distance \\( s = 50 \\, \\text{m} \\).  \nFirst convert \\( v \\) to m/s: \\( 130 \\, \\text{km/h} = 130 \\times \\frac{1000}{3600} \\approx 36.11 \\, \\text{m/s} \\).  \nThen \\( a = \\frac{v^2}{2s} = \\frac{(36.11)^2}{100} \\approx 13.04 \\, \\text{m/s}^2 \\), which is closest to **13 m/s\u00b2**.\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 235, "output_tokens": 166, "total_tokens": 401}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5253", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On an average daily basis, the gross energy intake of a healthy woman is 9279 kJ, the energy content of her faeces and urine are 647 kJ and 318 kJ, respectively. Her average daily digestible energy intake and metabolisable energy intake would be, respectively,:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nB. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-318 kJ\nC. 9279-(318+647) kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nD. 9279+647 kJ and 9279-(318+647) kJ\nE. 9279+318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nF. 9279-647 kJ and 9279-(647+318) kJ\nG. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nH. 9279+318 kJ and 9279+647 kJ\nI. 9279 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nJ. 647 kJ and 318 kJ\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Digestible energy** = Gross intake \u2212 Fecal energy = 9279 \u2212 647 kJ.  \n**Metabolisable energy** = Digestible energy \u2212 Urinary energy = (9279 \u2212 647) \u2212 318 = 9279 \u2212 (647 + 318) kJ.  \nThat matches option **F**.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 277}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Walking down a street late at night, an adult male pedestrian notices a young female on the ground, not moving. The female is on the opposite side of the street. Crossing the street, the pedestrian notices that the young woman appears both much wealthier than he is and is of a different ethnicity. Seeing no one else present, the pedestrian renders aid. According to the bystander effect, which of the following would change how the pedestrian reacts?\n\nOptions: \nA. The presence of a security camera on the street\nB. The presence of one other person who is already approaching the girl\nC. The person requiring aid appearing to be of a lower socioeconomic class rather than a higher one\nD. The presence of a large, intimidating dog near the girl\nE. The person requiring aid appearing to be the same ethnicity rather than a different one\nF. The person requiring aid appearing to be less wealthy than initially thought\nG. The person requiring aid appearing to be older rather than younger\nH. The person requiring aid appearing to be of the same gender rather than a different one\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The bystander effect primarily involves the presence or absence of other people affecting an individual\u2019s likelihood to help, so the key factor is whether others are available to share responsibility.  \n\nThe correct choice is **B** because the presence of another person already helping could either increase helping (modeling behavior) or reduce the individual\u2019s perceived need to act, both of which are changes predicted by theories related to the bystander effect.  \n\nOther options involve characteristics of the victim or environment that are less directly tied to the core diffusion-of-responsibility mechanism.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 341, "output_tokens": 156, "total_tokens": 497}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4997", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The likelihood of an individual in a population carrying two specific alleles of a human DNA marker, each of which has a frequency of 0.2, will be:\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.24\nB. 0.4\nC. 0.32\nD. 0.1\nE. 0.16\nF. 0.12\nG. 0.02\nH. 0.04\nI. 0.08\nJ. 0.06\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for the probability of carrying **two specific alleles** each with frequency 0.2.  \nAssuming Hardy\u2013Weinberg equilibrium, the chance of having both copies of that specific allele (homozygosity) is \\(0.2 \\times 0.2 = 0.04\\).  \n\nThat matches option **H**.\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 241}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4921", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A segment of DNA from a lab mouse is determined to be 5\u2019 \u2013 GGATCCTCATG \u2013 3\u2019. Which of the following DNA segments would be the result of this original DNA sequence experiencing both a point mutation and a deletion?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5' - GGATCCTCA - 3'\nB. 5\u2019 \u2013 TGATCCCAG \u2013 3\u2019\nC. 5\u2019 \u2013 GGATCCATG \u2013 3\u2019\nD. 5' - GGATCCTCGT - 3'\nE. 5\u2019 \u2013 GGTCCTCATC \u2013 3\u2019\nF. 5' - GGATCCGCATG - 3'\nG. 5' - GGATCTCATG - 3'\nH. 5' - GGATCCTCAT - 3'\nI. 5' - GGATCCTCAG - 3'\nJ. 5\u2019 \u2013 GCATCCTCATG \u2013 3\u2019\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The original sequence is **5'\u2013GGATCCTCATG\u20133'**.  \nA **point mutation** changes one base, and a **deletion** removes at least one base.  \nOption **G** (5'\u2013GGATCTCATG\u20133') has a point mutation (C\u2192T in bold) and a deletion (missing the C that was originally after GATC), fitting both requirements.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 256, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 347}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5258", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the mean rate of oxygen consumption of a male athlete during a training session is 2 l/min, then his rate of energy expenditure is approximately:\n\nOptions: \nA. 20 kJ/min.\nB. 500 kJ/min.\nC. 30 kJ/min.\nD. 40 kJ/min.\nE. 400 kJ/min.\nF. 60 kJ/min.\nG. 200 kJ/min.\nH. 100 kJ/min.\nI. 80 kJ/min.\nJ. 120 kJ/min.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The energy equivalent of oxygen is about 20 kJ per liter. At 2 l/min, that gives 40 kJ/min.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5203", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Under which circumstances would you not use a catheter valve?\n\nOptions: \nA. If the patient chooses it.\nB. If the patient is bedridden.\nC. If urine does not need to be measured.\nD. If the patient has bladder sensation.\nE. If the patient suffers from urinary incontinence.\nF. If the patient is post-operative.\nG. If the patient is in the late stages of pregnancy.\nH. If the patient has a history of bladder spasms.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A catheter valve is generally not used when the patient is bedridden (B) because it requires the patient to be mobile enough to access a toilet to drain the bladder regularly. It is also contraindicated in cases of urinary incontinence (E) because the valve relies on the patient\u2019s ability to sense bladder fullness and control voiding.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B} and \\boxed{E} (both are valid contraindications, but if only one is required, B is the most direct contraindication in typical clinical guidelines).", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 161, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 271}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5272", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If both parents are affected with the same autosomal recessive disorder then the probability that each of their children will be affected equals ___.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3 in 4\nB. 1 in 3\nC. 2 in 3\nD. 2 in 4\nE. 1 in 10\nF. 1\nG. 3 in 3\nH. 4 in 4\nI. 1 in 4\nJ. 1 in 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "If both parents are affected by the same autosomal recessive disorder, they are both homozygous recessive (genotype **aa**).  \nAll their children will therefore inherit one recessive allele from each parent, so all children will be **aa** and affected.  \nThe probability that each child will be affected is **1** (100%).  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 164, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 236}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5434", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the frequency of males affected with an X-linked recessive condition in a human population is .10 (one in ten), what will be the expected frequency of affected females?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.001\nB. 0.01\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.15\nE. 0.0011\nF. 0.02\nG. 0.0001\nH. 0.0002\nI. 0.05\nJ. 0.2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For an X-linked recessive condition, the frequency of affected males equals the allele frequency \\( q \\) because males have only one X chromosome. Given that the frequency of affected males is 0.10, we have \\( q = 0.10 \\). Affected females require two copies of the recessive allele, so their expected frequency is \\( q^2 = (0.10)^2 = 0.01 \\).\n\nThe correct answer is **B**.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 139, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 235}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4934", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Your first action following confirmation of cardiac arrest is to:\n\nOptions: \nA. ensure the emergency team/services are called.\nB. administer an electric shock using a defibrillator.\nC. give 30 chest compressions.\nD. check the notes to see if the patient has a DNAR order.\nE. rush the patient to the emergency room.\nF. administer adrenaline.\nG. lay the patient down and elevate the legs.\nH. perform mouth-to-mouth resuscitation.\nI. check the patient's blood pressure.\nJ. give two rescue breaths.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In a confirmed cardiac arrest, the immediate priority is to call for help to activate the emergency response and ensure advanced resources arrive quickly.\n\nThe correct choice is **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 171, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5548", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If an X-linked recessive disorder is in Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium and the incidence in males equals 1 in 100, then the expected incidence of affected homozygous females would be _______.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 in 10 000\nB. 1 in 50 000\nC. 1 in 5000\nD. 1 in 8000\nE. 1 in 1000\nF. 1 in 40 000\nG. 1 in 200\nH. 1 in 100 000\nI. 1 in 20 000\nJ. 1 in 4000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For an X-linked recessive disorder, the incidence in males equals the allele frequency \\( q \\) because males have only one X chromosome.  \nGiven that incidence in males is \\( 1/100 \\), we have \\( q = 0.01 \\).  \nHomozygous affected females occur with frequency \\( q^2 = (0.01)^2 = 0.0001 = 1/10\\,000 \\).\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 157, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 238}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5394", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 68-year-old female has a history of breast cancer that has recurred twice in the past 5\u00a0years. She has undergone both radiation and chemotherapy for metastatic carcinoma to the bone. She presents to the office today to ask for help in dealing with midthoracic back pain to enable her to use less analgesic agents. The most appropriate osteopathic manipulative technique to treat this patient's spine is\n\nOptions: \nA. direct soft tissue technique\nB. high velocity, low amplitude\nC. high velocity, high amplitude\nD. indirect myofascial release\nE. low velocity, low amplitude\nF. isotonic exercise therapy\nG. mid velocity, mid amplitude\nH. static stretching technique\nI. direct myofascial release\nJ. isotonic resistance therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Given the history of metastatic bone disease, any forceful or direct technique is contraindicated due to risk of pathological fracture. The safest approach is an indirect, gentle method that does not load the spine.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 253, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 313}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5245", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 44-year-old female presents to the office for evaluation of a lump on her neck that she noted 1\u00a0week ago. She denies any tenderness, fever, weight loss, or fatigue. Physical examination reveals a\u00a02-cm\u00a0freely movable mass in the lower left lobe of the thyroid. In addition to thyroid-stimulating hormone and free thyroxine levels, the most appropriate initial method to investigate this lesion is\n\nOptions: \nA. Thyroid biopsy\nB. Positron emission tomography (PET) scan\nC. Lymph node biopsy\nD. Computed tomography (CT) scan\nE. an iodine131\u00a0scan\nF. a nuclear thyroid scan\nG. Endoscopic examination of the throat\nH. fine-needle aspiration\nI. Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)\nJ. ultrasonography of the thyroid gland\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate initial method is thyroid ultrasonography to characterize the nodule before considering biopsy.\n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 250, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 281}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5261", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a blood unit has been out of refrigeration for longer than the accepted time limit, you should:\n\nOptions: \nA. Use it for non-human transfusion purposes.\nB. Leave it to reach room temperature before administering.\nC. refrigerate for a minimum of 12 hours and then administer it.\nD. return it to the blood bank and inform them of why you have done so.\nE. dispose of the contents in the sluice area, keeping the bag for record purposes.\nF. Use it immediately for the most critical patient.\nG. Discard it without notifying the blood bank.\nH. Freeze it to preserve it for later use.\nI. Return it to the refrigerator and use it within the next 24 hours.\nJ. transfuse it as soon as possible and annotate the patient's notes with the time of administration.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on standard blood bank protocols, a unit that has been out of refrigeration beyond the time limit should be returned to the blood bank with documentation of the reason so it can be properly assessed and discarded if necessary.  \n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{D}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 260, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 327}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4982", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person is prescribed Ropinirole 1.5 mg divided into three doses. How many micrograms is each dose? Choose one answer from the following:\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 5000\nC. 0.05\nD. 500\nE. 50,000\nF. 0.005\nG. 50\nH. 5,000,000\nI. 500,000\nJ. 0.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "First, convert 1.5 mg to micrograms:  \n1.5 mg \u00d7 1000 = 1500 \u00b5g total.  \nDivided into three doses: 1500 \u00b5g \u00f7 3 = 500 \u00b5g per dose.  \n\nThat matches option D (500).  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 130, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5227", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which muscle is the most active during a right lateral excursion of the mandible?\n\nOptions: \nA. Left masseter muscle\nB. Right buccinator muscle\nC. Right temporalis muscle\nD. Right masseter muscle\nE. Right lateral pterygoid muscle\nF. Left medial pterygoid muscle\nG. Left temporalis muscle\nH. Left buccinator muscle\nI. Left lateral pterygoid muscle\nJ. Right medial pterygoid muscle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "During a right lateral excursion of the mandible, the left lateral pterygoid muscle is primarily responsible for pulling the mandible to the right side. The right lateral pterygoid is relatively inactive during this contralateral movement.  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 167, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 230}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5128", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A couple comes for preconceptional genetic counseling because they both have a family history of \u03b1-thalassemia. The woman has a minimally decreased hemoglobin concentration. Genetic studies show a single gene deletion. The man has microcytic anemia and a two-gene deletion. If the two-gene deletion is in trans (one deletion on the maternal gene and one deletion on the paternal gene), which of the following percentages of their offspring will have a two-gene deletion?\n\nOptions: \nA. 75%\nB. 50%\nC. 20%\nD. 80%\nE. 10%\nF. 0%\nG. 66%\nH. 33%\nI. 25%\nJ. 100%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man has a two-gene deletion in *trans* (one deletion from each parent), so his genotype is \u03b1\u03b1/--. The woman has a single gene deletion, so her genotype is \u03b1\u03b1/\u03b1-.  \nTheir offspring can inherit either \u03b1 or - from each parent, and the only way to get a two-gene deletion is if the child inherits the - from the mother and the - from the father.  \nThat probability is 25%.\n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 305}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4910", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Food supplements, including trace minerals and vitamins are frequently advertised with promising health benefits. Which of the following substance could be consumed in excess, i.e. well above the recommended daily requirement?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Vitamin C\nB. Vitamin D\nC. Zinc\nD. Vitamin A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**D. Vitamin A**  \nVitamin A is fat-soluble and can accumulate in the body, causing toxicity if consumed well above recommended amounts. In contrast, excess water-soluble vitamin C is excreted, and while vitamins like D and minerals like zinc can also be harmful in high doses, vitamin A toxicity is particularly well-documented from excessive intake (e.g., through supplements or liver).  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 203}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5552", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A randomized controlled trial is conducted to assess the effectiveness of a new combination-drug antihypertensive therapy (Drug X) compared with a standard antihypertensive single-drug therapy. Study participants include 140 women (70%) and 60 men (30%) ages 30 to 60 years, with baseline blood pressure measurements of 150/95 mm Hg or higher. The investigators defined antihypertensive therapy as effective if the treatment resulted in a blood pressure measurement below 140/90 mm Hg. When designing the study, the investigators set the probability of wrongly finding that Drug X is more effective than the standard therapy as 1%; they set the probability of wrongly finding that the effectiveness of the two drugs is the same as 10%. Which of the following is the most accurate estimate of the statistical power in this study?\n\nOptions: \nA. 90%\nB. 80%\nC. 1%\nD. 60%\nE. 20%\nF. 40%\nG. 70%\nH. 50%\nI. 10%\nJ. 30%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statistical power is defined as 1 minus the probability of a type II error (wrongly finding no difference when one exists).  \nHere, the probability of wrongly finding the two drugs equally effective (type II error) is given as 10%, so power = 1 \u2212 0.10 = 0.90 = 90%.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 299, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 369}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4929", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 960 mg of the antibacterial drug Cotrimoxazole is prescribed every 12 hours. What is the daily dose in grams? Choose one answer from the following:\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.92\nB. 0.192\nC. 0.96\nD. 0.0192\nE. 19.2\nF. 3.84\nG. 1920\nH. 960\nI. 2.88\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The dose is 960 mg every 12 hours, so the daily dose is \\(960 \\, \\text{mg} \\times 2 = 1920 \\, \\text{mg}\\).  \nConverting mg to grams: \\(1920 \\, \\text{mg} = 1.92 \\, \\text{g}\\).  \nFrom the options, this corresponds to choice A.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 130, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5243", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 15-year-old male presents to the office with the complaint of painless swelling in the left testicle that has varied in size over the past several months. There is no history of trauma. The lesion transilluminates well, and no inguinal nodes are palpable. Findings from a testicular scan are normal. The most appropriate management includes\n\nOptions: \nA. ultrasonic therapy\nB. cryotherapy\nC. needle biopsy\nD. radiation therapy\nE. laser therapy\nF. chemotherapy\nG. needle aspiration\nH. injection with a sclerosing agent\nI. surgical repair\nJ. oral medication\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The presentation is most consistent with a hydrocele, which transilluminates and has normal testicular scan findings. The appropriate management for a symptomatic or persistent hydrocele in an adolescent is surgical repair (hydrocelectomy).  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 274}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5489", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Under what circumstances would you use antibiotics prior to catheterization?\n\nOptions: \nA. If the patient requests them.\nB. If the patient has a broken bone.\nC. If patient has an artificial heart valve.\nD. If the patient has a skin infection.\nE. If the patient is allergic to antibiotics.\nF. If the patient has had a catheter in situ for a week.\nG. If the patient does not have urinary tract infection.\nH. If the patient has a common cold.\nI. If the patient has a history of urinary tract infections.\nJ. If the patient has a high fever.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **C. If the patient has an artificial heart valve**, because antibiotic prophylaxis is often recommended before invasive procedures like catheterization for patients with certain cardiac conditions to prevent infective endocarditis.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 275}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4931", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Blood clots are responsible for repeatedly blocking a catheter. What should you do?\n\nOptions: \nA. Use a syringe to remove the clot.\nB. Remove the catheter and recatheterize.\nC. Replace the catheter with a new one without informing medical staff.\nD. Inform the patient's family.\nE. Inform the patient.\nF. Ignore it and continue with the procedure.\nG. Flush the catheter with saline.\nH. Inform medical staff.\nI. Repeatedly press the catheter to remove the clot.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct action is to inform medical staff, as they can assess and manage the catheter appropriately, which may include flushing or replacement.  \n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 170, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 203}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5015", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new blood test to detect prostate cancer is evaluated in 300 male volunteers. A needle biopsy of the prostate gland is done on all men with serum prostate-specific antigen concentrations greater than 5 ng/mL (N<4). One hundred men undergo biopsy procedures; 90 are found to have prostate cancer, and five are found to have chronic prostatitis. Which of the following is necessary to calculate the sensitivity of this test?\n\nOptions: \nA. Prevalence of chronic prostatitis in the general population\nB. Prevalence of prostate cancer in the general population\nC. Prostate biopsies of men with test results greater than 5 ng/mL\nD. Prostate biopsies of men with test results equal to or below 5 ng/mL\nE. Number of men with test results greater than 5 ng/mL and chronic prostatitis\nF. Incidence of prostate cancer in the general population\nG. Number of men with test results greater than 5 ng/mL and a normal biopsy specimen\nH. Number of men with test results equal to or below 5 ng/mL and a normal biopsy specimen\nI. Number of men with test results equal to or below 5 ng/mL and chronic prostatitis\nJ. Incidence of chronic prostatitis in the general population\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To calculate sensitivity, we need the number of true positives (men with prostate cancer who tested positive) and false negatives (men with prostate cancer who tested negative).  \nWe already have data on men with test results >5 ng/mL (positive tests) who underwent biopsy, but we lack information on men with test results \u22645 ng/mL (negative tests) who may still have prostate cancer.  \nTherefore, we need **prostate biopsies of men with test results equal to or below 5 ng/mL** to identify false negatives.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 361, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 490}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5070", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 31-year-old man with a 5-year history of HIV infection comes to the office because of anal pain, particularly on defecation, for the past 4 months. He says he has seen spots of blood on the toilet tissue but has not had any other noticeable bleeding. He reports no change in bowel habits and has not had recent fever, chills, or rectal drainage. He says he and his partner engage in anal-receptive intercourse. His most recent CD4+ T-lymphocyte count 2 months ago was 350/mm3 ; HIV viral load at that time was undetectable. He currently is being treated with antiretroviral therapy. He has had no opportunistic infections. Medical history is also significant for syphilis and genital herpes treated with penicillin and acyclovir, respectively. He does not smoke cigarettes or drink alcoholic beverages. Vital signs are normal. Physical examination shows small bilateral inguinal lymph nodes, but respiratory, cardiac, and abdominal examinations disclose no abnormalities. There are several tender fleshy lesions around the perianal area. Rectal examination produces tenderness, but there is no rectal discharge. Test of the stool for occult blood is trace positive. Which of the following is the most appropriate pharmacotherapy at this time?\n\nOptions: \nA. Acyclovir\nB. Imiquimod\nC. Levofloxacin\nD. Metronidazole\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient's history of anal-receptive intercourse and perianal fleshy lesions suggests human papillomavirus (HPV)-related anal warts, which are common in HIV patients. Imiquimod is a topical immune response modifier used to treat external anogenital warts. The other options treat infections not indicated by the presentation.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 401, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 485}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5146", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person weighs 62 kg. Their drug dose is 15 mg/kg. How many grams is their dose? Choose one answer from the following:\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.186\nB. 0.93\nC. 18.6 x 10^-3\nD. 0.0186\nE. 186\nF. 9.3\nG. 18.6\nH. 1.86\nI. 93\nJ. 930\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "First, calculate the dose in milligrams:  \n\\( 62 \\, \\text{kg} \\times 15 \\, \\text{mg/kg} = 930 \\, \\text{mg} \\).  \n\nConvert milligrams to grams:  \n\\( 930 \\, \\text{mg} = 0.93 \\, \\text{g} \\).  \n\nThis matches option **B**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5112", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a condition such as schizophrenia the recurrence risk will be greatest for which of the following relatives of an affected individual?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aunt\nB. Nephew\nC. Brother\nD. Grandchild\nE. Great-grandchild\nF. Second cousin\nG. Cousin\nH. Uncle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The recurrence risk for a genetic disorder like schizophrenia is highest in closest relatives. Among the listed options, a **brother** (first-degree relative) has the highest genetic relatedness to the affected individual.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 134, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 195}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5297", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 35-year-old female develops nausea and vomiting after she underwent a cholecystectomy for protracted ileus. Her body mass index was 23\u00a0kg/m2\u00a0before surgery, and, except for the cholecystitis, she was in good health. The patient remains unable to eat 6\u00a0days after surgery. Which of the following forms of nutritional support is most appropriate for this patient?\n\nOptions: \nA. oral protein-rich diet\nB. feeding through a nasogastric feeding tube\nC. feeding through a jejunostomy tube\nD. central hyperalimentation\nE. intravenous saline solution\nF. peripheral hyperalimentation\nG. oral carbohydrate-rich diet\nH. feeding through a gastrostomy tube\nI. oral fat-free modular diet\nJ. intravenous dextrose solution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has a protracted ileus, so enteral nutrition (especially gastric) is likely not tolerated; central hyperalimentation (total parenteral nutrition) is indicated when oral/enteral intake is not expected for >7 days and she is already on day 6.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 286}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5448", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 26-year-old woman is brought to the emergency department because of an 8-hour history of severe back and abdominal pain and mild but persistent vaginal bleeding. Ultrasonography of the abdomen shows a 2-cm ectopic pregnancy in the ampulla. The ampulla has ruptured into the surrounding tissue. Fluid from this rupture will most likely be found in which of the following locations?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lesser peritoneal cavity\nB. Mesometrium\nC. Pouch of Douglas\nD. Uterine cavity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The rupture of an ampullary ectopic pregnancy typically releases blood and fluid into the peritoneal cavity, where it often collects in the most dependent pelvic space, the **pouch of Douglas** (rectouterine pouch). This is a common site for fluid accumulation in cases of hemoperitoneum from a ruptured ectopic pregnancy. The other locations are not the primary dependent pelvic space where such fluid would collect.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 191, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 298}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5071", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 7-year-old male is brought to the office for evaluation of school problems. The mother says that the teacher has told her that the patient is inattentive, has difficulty following sequential instructions, and often seems to drift off to sleep during class. A polysomnogram reveals obstructive sleep apnea. The most appropriate management is\n\nOptions: \nA. referral to a psychiatrist\nB. heart rate and apnea monitoring\nC. imipramine\nD. elevation of the head of the bed\nE. speech therapy\nF. prescription of stimulant medication\nG. prescription of sleeping pills\nH. surgical evaluation\nI. administration of caffeine\nJ. use of a humidifier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate management for obstructive sleep apnea in a child is surgical evaluation, typically for adenotonsillectomy, which is the first-line treatment.  \n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 231, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 275}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5126", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 64-year-old male presents to the emergency room with a bloody nose that has been dripping out his nares for the past 2\u00a0hours. He denies any trauma, recent upper respiratory illness, or history of prior bloody nose. Past medical history is unremarkable, and he takes no medications. He has a blood pressure of 180/90\u00a0mmHg. Examination of the nasal passages reveals that the site of the bleeding is on the septal mucosa of the right naris. The most appropriate next step in management includes\n\nOptions: \nA. anterior packing\nB. placing an ice compress over the nose\nC. catheter balloon tamponade\nD. pinching the nares together for 5 minutes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has active epistaxis from an anterior source (septal mucosa), so initial management should be direct pressure by pinching the nares.  \nAnterior packing or balloon tamponade would be considered if direct pressure fails.  \nIce compresses are less effective than direct pressure for active bleeding.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 279}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4948", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient cuts a peripheral motor nerve in their wrist when they fall through a plate glass window. If the nerve does not regenerate, after about 6 months the muscles it normally innervates will show signs of which of the four options below?\n\nOptions: \nA. spastic paralysis\nB. contracture\nC. fasciculations\nD. muscle stiffness\nE. atrophy\nF. hypertrophy\nG. muscle rigidity\nH. flaccid paralysis\nI. muscle spasms\nJ. hyperreflexia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "After 6 months without regeneration, the denervated muscles will undergo **atrophy** and exhibit **flaccid paralysis**.  \nThe correct answer is a combination of E and H, but since only one letter can be chosen and atrophy is the primary degenerative change, the most direct answer is **E**.  \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 233}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5059", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Examination of a patient indicates that they have a medially directed strabismus (squint). This could be due to damage to the\n\nOptions: \nA. oculomotor nerve.\nB. accessory nerve.\nC. trochlear nerve.\nD. ophthalmic trigeminal nerve.\nE. optic nerve.\nF. vestibulocochlear nerve.\nG. facial nerve.\nH. hypoglossal nerve.\nI. glossopharyngeal nerve.\nJ. abducens nerve.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A **medially directed strabismus** (esotropia) results from a weakened lateral rectus muscle, which is innervated by the **abducens nerve (CN VI)**. Damage to this nerve impairs abduction of the eye, causing unopposed medial pull.  \n\nAnswer: \\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 160, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 227}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5341", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A physician is conducting a retrospective review of a trial involving the use of Drug X in patients with a specific disease. It is known that Drug X is associated with an increased probability of cancer in patients who use the drug. A total of 600 individuals with a specific disease were included in the trial. Of the participants, 200 individuals received Drug X and 400 individuals did not receive it. One hundred individuals who received Drug X died of a particular type of cancer and 100 individuals who did not receive the drug died of the same type of cancer. Based on these data, which of the following is the relative risk of death from this type of cancer in individuals who take Drug X as compared with individuals who do not take Drug X?\n\nOptions: \nA. Individuals who take Drug X have two times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nB. Individuals who take Drug X have four times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nC. Individuals who take Drug X have three times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nD. Individuals who take Drug X have six times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nE. Individuals who do not take Drug X have three times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nF. Individuals who take Drug X have half the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nG. Individuals who take Drug X have an equal risk of dying from this type of cancer\nH. Individuals who do not take Drug X have two times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nI. Individuals who take Drug X have five times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nJ. Individuals who take Drug X have zero risk of dying from this type of cancer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Relative risk = (risk in exposed group) / (risk in unexposed group) = (100/200) / (100/400) = (0.5) / (0.25) = 2.  \nThis means individuals who take Drug X have twice the risk of dying from this cancer compared to those who do not take it.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 485, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 547}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4953", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 30-year-old woman, gravida 2, para 0, aborta 1, at 28 weeks' gestation comes to the office for a prenatal visit. She has had one previous pregnancy resulting in a spontaneous abortion at 12 weeks' gestation. Today, her vital signs are within normal limits. Physical examination shows a uterus consistent in size with a 28-week gestation. Fetal ultrasonography shows a male fetus with no abnormalities. Her blood group is O, Rh-negative. The father's blood group is B, Rh-positive. The physician recommends administration of Rho\n\nOptions: \nA. Development of polycythemia\nB. Formation of antibodies to RhB\nC. Development of lymphocytosis\nD. Formation of antibodies to RhO\nE. immune globulin to the patient. This treatment is most likely to prevent which of the following in this mother?\nF. Development of leukocytosis\nG. Formation of antibodies to RhD\nH. Development of anemia\nI. Formation of antibodies to RhC\nJ. Development of natural killer cells\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The physician is recommending Rho(D) immune globulin to an Rh-negative mother to prevent anti-D alloimmunization from fetal Rh-positive blood exposure.\n\nThe most direct effect is preventing antibody formation against the RhD antigen.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 277, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 329}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5514", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 2-year-old boy is brought to the emergency department by his babysitter because of a 30-minute history of respiratory distress. The babysitter reports that she is 15 years old and has cared for the patient on numerous occasions during the past year. The child's mother, who is a single parent, is currently out of town for business but will return later tonight. The babysitter says, \"He has had a runny nose since I started babysitting yesterday, but this afternoon he awoke from a nap with a barking sound and he was breathing real heavy.\" She does not know the child's prior health history, nor does she know if the boy takes any medications on a regular basis. The child looks tired and sits upright on the babysitter's lap. He is obviously comfortable with his caregiver. Vital signs are temperature 38.7\u00b0C (101.7\u00b0F), pulse 110/min, respirations 28/min and labored, and blood pressure 85/50 mm Hg. Pulse oximetry on room air shows an oxygen saturation of 89%. Physical examination discloses inspiratory stridor. Neck is supple, tympanic membranes are normal, and there is a profuse nasal discharge. Examination of the pharynx discloses no abnormalities. Auscultation of the chest discloses equal air entry on both sides and no crackles. The remainder of the examination shows no abnormalities. Treatment with 40% oxygen via venturi mask and intravenous fluids is initiated. Despite continued supplemental oxygen and hydration, the child remains tachypneic and stridorous at rest. Oxygen saturation is now 93%. In addition to administering racemic epinephrine by nebulizer, which of the following is the most appropriate next step?\n\nOptions: \nA. Intravenous aminophylline therapy\nB. Intravenous antibiotic therapy\nC. Intubation\nD. Oral dexamethasone therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The child\u2019s presentation is consistent with moderate to severe croup, and after initial nebulized epinephrine, steroids such as dexamethasone are standard to reduce inflammation and prevent relapse.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 441, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 483}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5023", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An 18-year-old primigravid woman comes for her initial prenatal visit at 16 weeks' gestation. She is not sure about the date of her last menstrual period but says that the pregnancy probably occurred immediately after she stopped taking oral contraceptives 5 months ago. Maternal serum \u03b1-fetoprotein (MSAFP) concentration is increased to 3 multiples of the median. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Amniocentesis for measurement of \u03b1-fetoprotein concentration\nB. Immediate cesarean section\nC. Hormone therapy to balance MSAFP levels\nD. Monitor patient without taking action\nE. Triple screening for MSAFP, serum \u03b2-hCG, and serum estriol concentrations\nF. Administer a pregnancy test\nG. Prescribe oral contraceptives\nH. Ultrasonography\nI. Repeat measurement of MSAFP concentration\nJ. Conduct a pelvic exam\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate next step is to confirm gestational age and assess for possible anomalies, as an elevated MSAFP can be due to incorrect dating or fetal abnormalities. Ultrasonography is used first to verify dates and check for structural issues before considering invasive testing like amniocentesis.\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 286, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 365}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5224", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient is stabbed in the neck. You suspect damage to the accessory nerve in the posterior triangle. You would test nerve function by asking the patient to\n\nOptions: \nA. turn their head to the side without impairment.\nB. lift their shoulders against resistance.\nC. extend their neck against resistance.\nD. extend their neck without impairment.\nE. rotate their head against resistance.\nF. shrug their shoulders without resistance.\nG. lift their shoulders without impairment.\nH. rotate their head without impairment.\nI. turn their head to the side against resistance.\nJ. extend their arm against resistance.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The accessory nerve (CN XI) primarily innervates the sternocleidomastoid and trapezius muscles. In the posterior triangle, it is most associated with motor function of the trapezius, which is tested by having the patient shrug their shoulders against resistance.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 179, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 243}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5288", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Three weeks ago a 45-year-old man was admitted to the hospital because of frostbite of both feet. He was treated by rapid rewarming and protective care of the feet. All the toes on the right foot have turned black. He has become slightly febrile and progressively more confused during the past few days. Examination discloses cellulitis in the midfoot. Which of the following is the most appropriate treatment?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hyperbaric oxygen\nB. Skin grafting\nC. Intravenous fluids and electrolytes\nD. Application of topical collagenase\nE. Application of silver sulfadiazine\nF. Amputation\nG. Antibiotic therapy\nH. Application of warm compresses\nI. Placement of a wound VAC\nJ. Debridement of necrotic skin over the toes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has signs of infection (fever, confusion, cellulitis) complicating frostbite necrosis, so systemic antibiotic therapy is the most urgent initial step to control sepsis before definitive surgical management.  \nWhile debridement or amputation may eventually be needed, antibiotics address the immediate life-threatening infection.  \nOther options like topical treatments or hyperbaric oxygen are not first-line for this acute infectious presentation.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 316}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5518", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 13-month-old child is brought to the emergency department because of urticaria, swelling of the lips, and difficulty breathing immediately after eating an egg. A potential risk for hypersensitivity reaction is posed by vaccination against which of the following illnesses?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hepatitis\nB. Influenza\nC. Pertussis\nD. Poliomyelitis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The child\u2019s symptoms suggest an IgE-mediated allergy to egg protein. Some influenza vaccines are produced in chicken eggs and may contain residual egg protein, posing a risk of hypersensitivity in those with egg allergy.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 157, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 220}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4958", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 2-month-old female is brought to the office for her first routine health maintenance examination and for her immunization update. In order to determine whether or not any contraindications exist for diphtheria, tetanus, pertussis (DtaP) immunization, the parents should be questioned regarding\n\nOptions: \nA. allergy to eggs\nB. previous seizures\nC. dietary habits\nD. gestational age at birth\nE. family history of diabetes\nF. any chronic conditions\nG. history of heart disease\nH. Apgar scores at birth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most important contraindication to assess for DTaP vaccination in an infant is a history of seizures or neurological reaction to a previous dose, as it may indicate increased risk of adverse events.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 255}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5182", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 43-year-old man with a history of self-mutilation comes to the emergency department because of pain in his right thigh and shaking chills during the past 3 days. He says he intentionally burned his right thigh several times with a cigarette lighter 6 days ago. This morning he soaked his thigh in a tub of hot water and massaged it, after which a large amount of \"greenish fluid\" drained from the wound sites. The patient normally takes lithium carbonate but stopped 3 months ago after he lost his job. Medical history is otherwise unremarkable. Vital signs are temperature 39.2\u00b0C (102.5\u00b0F), pulse 170/min, respirations 18/min, and blood pressure 120/60 mm Hg. Physical examination shows an edematous right lateral thigh with multiple burn sites with a white exudative appearance. There is erythema surrounding the burn areas with red streaks extending up the thigh. Palpation of the burn sites discloses fluctuance. Results of laboratory studies show a hemoglobin concentration of 14 g/dL and a leukocyte count of 19,000/mm3 . In addition to beginning antibiotic therapy, which of the following is the most appropriate next step?\n\nOptions: \nA. Application of a pressure bandage\nB. Intravenous fluid resuscitation\nC. Recommencement of lithium carbonate treatment\nD. Transfer to a burn center\nE. Thrombolytic therapy\nF. Immediate surgical amputation\nG. Physical therapy consultation\nH. Psychiatric consultation\nI. Topical silver sulfadiazine\nJ. Incision and drainage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has signs of a severe soft tissue infection (cellulitis with possible abscess, fever, leukocytosis) following self-inflicted burns, and fluctuance indicates an abscess requiring drainage. Incision and drainage is the appropriate next step in addition to antibiotics. \n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 439, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 511}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5490", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not necessary when examining the jugular venous pulse?\n\nOptions: \nA. Checking the pulse on both sides of the neck\nB. Using a magnifying glass\nC. Using a stethoscope\nD. Patient should be in a standing position\nE. Patient holding their breath\nF. Good lighting\nG. Turning the patient's head to the right\nH. Timing the pulsation with the radial pulse\nI. Patient's neck muscles should be relaxed\nJ. Patient lying at 45 degree angle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because examining the jugular venous pulse is typically done with the patient reclining, not standing, to make the venous pulsations visible.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 174, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 215}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5007", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When you examine a patient who has suffered an unfavourable fracture of the body of the mandible, you would expect the\n\nOptions: \nA. anterior fragment to be displaced anteriorly by the action of the lateral pterygoid muscle.\nB. posterior fragment to be displaced downwards by the action of the digastric muscle.\nC. anterior fragment to be displaced backwards by action of the temporalis muscle.\nD. posterior fragment to be displaced laterally by the action of the medial pterygoid muscle.\nE. anterior fragment to be displaced medially by the action of the medial pterygoid muscle.\nF. posterior fragment to be displaced upwards by the action of the masseter muscle.\nG. posterior fragment to be displaced anteriorly by the action of the lateral pterygoid muscle.\nH. anterior fragment to be displaced upwards by the action of the masseter muscle.\nI. anterior fragment to be displaced downwards by the action of the digastric muscle.\nJ. posterior fragment to be displaced medially by action of the medial pterygoid muscle.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **H** because in an unfavorable fracture of the mandibular body, the anterior fragment is typically displaced downward by the digastric and mylohyoid muscles, while the posterior fragment is displaced upward by the masseter, temporalis, and medial pterygoid muscles.  \n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 275, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 343}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5236", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 51-year-old man comes to the office because of a 6-month history of a lump on his tongue that is interfering with his speech and eating; he also has had a 6.8-kg (15-lb) weight loss during this period. He has smoked 1 pack of cigarettes daily and has consumed six 12-oz bottles of beer on weekend nights during the past 30 years. His vital signs are within normal limits. Physical examination shows a 1.5-cm mass on the apex of the tongue. Further evaluation of the mass confirms squamous cell carcinoma. It is most appropriate to evaluate which of the following lymph nodes first for evidence of metastasis in this patient?\n\nOptions: \nA. Parotid\nB. Retropharyngeal\nC. Subclavian\nD. Submental\nE. Supraclavicular\nF. Popliteal\nG. Inferior deep cervical\nH. Preauricular\nI. Axillary\nJ. Inguinal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The tongue apex drains first to the submental lymph nodes, which are part of the primary lymphatic drainage pathway for this area.  \nGiven the location of the squamous cell carcinoma, checking these nodes is the appropriate initial step in evaluating for metastasis.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 269, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 324}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5185", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 40-year-old man with paranoid schizophrenia is transferred to the emergency department from the residential facility where he lives 2 hours after having swallowed a nail. The patient says he does not have any symptoms. Medical history is otherwise unremarkable. His only current medication is haloperidol. The patient is not in acute distress. Vital signs are normal. Physical examination shows no abnormalities. Mental status examination discloses a flat affect, distractibility, and derailment of thoughts. X-ray of the abdomen is obtained and shows a 4-cm nail in the left upper quadrant. No free air is visible. After admitting the patient to the hospital, which of the following is the most appropriate management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Open laparotomy and removal of the nail through a gastrotomy incision\nB. Insertion of a nasogastric tube to suction out the nail\nC. Administration of activated charcoal to bind the nail and facilitate its removal\nD. Removal of the nail through endoscopic esophagogastroscopy\nE. Administration of a barium swallow to track the nail's passage\nF. Administration of ipecac to induce vomiting and expectoration of the nail\nG. Administering a laxative to expedite the passage of the nail\nH. Observation to allow passage of the nail via normal peristalsis\nI. Use of a magnet to draw out the nail\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient is asymptomatic with a smooth, blunt object already in the stomach, and endoscopic removal is indicated for objects >2.5\u20133 cm to prevent complications like perforation or obstruction.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 342, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 389}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5049", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A problem in comparing older adults' memory for recent events and events that happened a long time ago is that recent events\n\nOptions: \nA. Can be verified while older events often cannot\nB. Are influenced by current mental state\nC. May be very well rehearsed\nD. Are more likely to be distorted or embellished\nE. Are often less significant than older events\nF. Have a different emotional impact\nG. Have no denominator to help in computing an average\nH. Can be easily confused with older events\nI. Are more likely to be forgotten\nJ. Are far more meaningful\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **A**, because in memory research, verifying the accuracy of recent events is often easier than for distant past events, which introduces a methodological challenge when comparing them.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 189, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 234}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5038", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A source emits a sound from one medium with a certain velocity, intensity, frequency and wavelength. When the sound exits the first medium and enters a denser medium, all of the following changes EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. tone\nB. amplitude\nC. wavelength\nD. direction\nE. pitch\nF. frequency\nG. resonance\nH. volume\nI. intensity\nJ. velocity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The properties that do not change when sound enters a different medium are **frequency** (and thus pitch/tone, which depend on frequency).  \nThe correct answer is the one that does **not** change, so it is frequency, which corresponds to **F**.  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 202}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5255", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The group that permits analysis of the entire natural history of HIV/AIDS is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Non-seroconverters\nB. Seroconverters\nC. Short-term survivors with low levels of CD4+ cells\nD. Long-term survivors\nE. Long-term survivors with high levels of CD4+ cells\nF. Persistent seronegatives\nG. Short-term survivors\nH. Seroconverters with fluctuating levels of CD4+ cells\nI. Persistent seropositives\nJ. Long-term survivors with low levels of CD4+ cells\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The group that allows analysis of the entire natural history of HIV/AIDS would be those who have been infected and followed from initial infection through all stages, which is best represented by **seroconverters** (those who convert from HIV-negative to HIV-positive). This group can be monitored from seroconversion through progression, including possible long-term survival.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 182, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 261}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4924", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best accounts for the negative slope of the liquid-solid equilibrium line in the phase diagram for water?\n\nOptions: \nA. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which is the result of the van der Waals forces between water molecules.\nB. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l) which results from the crystalline framework that forms due to hydrogen bonds.\nC. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l) which causes the solid to form liquid under low pressure conditions.\nD. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l), this is caused by the metallic bonds formed between water molecules.\nE. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l), which causes the solid to form liquid under high pressure conditions.\nF. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l), which is a result of the covalent bonds formed between water molecules.\nG. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which results from the hydrogen bonds formed between water molecules.\nH. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which results in the solid forming liquid under low pressure conditions.\nI. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which is due to the ionic bonds formed between water molecules.\nJ. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which causes the solid to form liquid under high pressure conditions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The negative slope of the solid-liquid line in water\u2019s phase diagram occurs because ice is less dense than liquid water, due to hydrogen bonding creating an open crystalline structure. This lower density means increasing pressure favors the denser liquid phase, lowering the melting point.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 385, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 447}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5142", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A police officer carries out hundreds of traffic stops every year. When his supervisor is reviewing the officer\u2019s records for the past year, he notices that the officer is equally likely to stop people of various genders, ages, and races. However, he is significantly more likely to write tickets for middle-aged white males with dark hair and eyes. When confronted with this fact, the officer truthfully states that he has no idea why that is, and that it must simply be a coincidence. Unbeknownst to the officer, this behavior is tied to the fact that these men look like his father, with whom he had an abusive relationship as a child. What psychological framework would directly address the unconscious bias in his behavior? \n\nOptions: \nA. Gestalt\nB. Developmental\nC. Biopsychological\nD. Humanistic\nE. Cognitive behavioral\nF. Positive psychology\nG. Evolutionary\nH. Behaviorist\nI. Social cognitive\nJ. Psychoanalytic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The scenario describes an unconscious bias rooted in early childhood experiences, which aligns with the **psychoanalytic** framework\u2019s focus on how repressed memories and unresolved conflicts can influence behavior without conscious awareness.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 302, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 371}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4991", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Grandparents with grandchildren in college report feeling especially loved when such grandchildren\n\nOptions: \nA. Buy them college merchandise as a token of love and appreciation\nB. Pay a surprise visit and ask for advice\nC. Dedicate a social media post to them\nD. Ask them to attend college events and introduce them to friends\nE. Visit during the holidays and bring gifts\nF. Send a text message every day\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question emphasizes grandparents feeling **especially loved**, which suggests a meaningful, personal interaction rather than a routine or material gesture.  \nOption **D** (asking them to attend college events and introducing them to friends) involves inclusion and pride in a significant part of the grandchild\u2019s life, likely creating a strong emotional connection.  \n\n**\\boxed{D}**", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 145, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 218}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4966", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What nutritional strategies will not improve performance during prolonged endurance type exercise?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Tapering\nB. The classic glycogen loading regime\nC. Hydration during exercise\nD. Exogenous carbohydrate ingestion during exercise\nE. Carbohydrate loading\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**A. Tapering**  \nWhile tapering reduces training load before competition to enhance performance, it is a training strategy\u2014not a nutritional one. The question asks for nutritional strategies that do **not** improve performance, and tapering does not directly involve nutrient intake or timing.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5052", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A cross between two true breeding lines one with dark blue flowers and one with bright white flowers produces F1 offspring that are light blue. When the F1 progeny are selfed a 1:2:1 ratio of dark blue to light blue to white flowers is observed. What genetic phenomenon is consistent with these results?\n\nOptions: \nA. overdominance\nB. polygenic inheritance\nC. epistasis\nD. pleiotropy\nE. lethal alleles\nF. genetic drift\nG. genetic linkage\nH. codominance\nI. incomplete dominance\nJ. inbreeding depression\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The F1 offspring show an intermediate phenotype (light blue) between the two parental true-breeding types (dark blue and white), and the F2 generation shows a 1:2:1 phenotypic ratio matching the genotypic ratio. This pattern is characteristic of **incomplete dominance**, where heterozygotes exhibit a blended or intermediate phenotype.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 289}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5303", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In terms of price per calorie, which of the following foods is the cheapest and most nutritious?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Bag of chips\nB. Chicken breast\nC. Banana\nD. Slice of bread\nE. Pasta\nF. Slice of pizza\nG. Apple\nH. Broccoli\nI. Can of soda\nJ. Cheese burger\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on typical cost and nutritional value per calorie, **pasta** is generally the cheapest source of calories while also providing carbohydrates and some protein. Compared to the other options, it offers more sustained energy and nutrients per unit cost than items like chips, soda, or pizza. Therefore, the best choice from the list is pasta.\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 142, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 214}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5484", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the following are true regarding the function of neurons EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The refractory period prevents the neuron from initiating a new action potential.\nB. The transmitting neuron secretes neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from its dendrites.\nC. An action potential is initiated when the axon hillock reaches the threshold potential.\nD. The action potential travels along the axon away from the cell body.\nE. Hyperpolarization occurs when the membrane potential becomes more negative than the resting potential.\nF. The flow of sodium into the neuron depolarizes the membrane in the first phase of an action potential.\nG. Hyperpolarization at the end of an action potential is one mechanism by which neurons limit the rate at which action potentials may fire.\nH. The neuron releases neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from the axon terminals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because neurotransmitters are released from axon terminals, not dendrites.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 25, "total_tokens": 254}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5199", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Each of the following are aspects of the McDonaldization of Society EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The extensive use of technology in everyday life\nB. Rationalization of decisions into cost/benefit analysis structures and away from traditional modes of thinking\nC. A focus on efficiency and predictability in all aspects of society\nD. An intense effort on achieving sameness across diverse markets\nE. Increased emphasis on quantity over quality\nF. The prioritization of profit over societal well-being\nG. Bureaucratic organization that formalizes well-establish division of labor and impersonal structures\nH. The standardization of societal norms and practices\nI. A shift from individual craftsmanship to mass production\nJ. A dissolution of hierarchical modes of authority into collaborative teambased decision protocols\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **J**, because McDonaldization involves increased control and hierarchical systems, not a dissolution of hierarchy into collaborative teams.\n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 275, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 318}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5198", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why do vigorous CD8 cell responses in chronically infected HIV-positive individuals fail to eliminate the virus?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inadequate MHC Class I presentation\nB. Suboptimal CTL\nC. Overproduction of interferon gamma\nD. Overactive T-helper cells\nE. Absence of dendritic cells\nF. CTL exhaustion\nG. Presence of neutralizing antibodies\nH. Epitope escape\nI. Insufficient natural killer cell activity\nJ. Lack of B cell response\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **F. CTL exhaustion**, because in chronic HIV infection, persistent antigen exposure leads to T-cell dysfunction and loss of cytotoxic capacity. **H. Epitope escape** is also a key mechanism, but CTL exhaustion is a broader, well-established cause of failed viral clearance in chronic infections.  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 159, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 231}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4923", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A certain molecule acts by binding to cytochrome oxidase A3, the final enzyme in the electron transport chain. Administration of a large dose of this substance to a human would likely:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decrease the rate of glycolysis, leading to a drop in ATP production.\nB. Have no effect as cells would switch which macronutrient they metabolize to circumvent the blocked biochemical pathway.\nC. Stimulate the cell to increase its production of cytochrome oxidase A3 to compensate for the blocked enzyme.\nD. Lead to the overproduction of NADH, causing a buildup of toxic metabolites in the cell.\nE. Increase the cell\u2019s ATP production as negative feedback would cause the cell to up-regulate anaerobic pathways.\nF. Increase the efficiency of the electron transport chain by providing an alternative pathway for electron transfer.\nG. Have no effect as the cells would increase their reliance on fatty acid oxidation for energy production.\nH. Lead to death due to an inability of the cell to pass electrons to oxygen, thus stopping aerobic respiration and asphyxiating the cells.\nI. Lead to death due to an inadequate supply of ADP to accept a phosphate group at the ATP synthase enzyme.\nJ. Cause a rapid increase in the production of reactive oxygen species, leading to oxidative stress and cell death.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The molecule described inhibits cytochrome oxidase (complex IV), which prevents the final transfer of electrons to oxygen, halting the electron transport chain and aerobic ATP production. This would rapidly cause severe cellular energy failure, ultimately leading to death.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 323, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 379}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4873", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A problem for immune system theories of senescence is\n\nOptions: \nA. Determining what first causes the senescence in the immune system\nB. The immune system theories do not explain the role of lifestyle in senescence\nC. Immune system theories do not explain the role of genetic factors in senescence\nD. Immune system theories are too complex to test effectively\nE. The lack of information about senescence in general\nF. That the immune system improves with age\nG. Immune system theories cannot account for the environmental factors in senescence\nH. That the immune system does not decline with age\nI. The difficulty of isolating the immune system from other bodily systems\nJ. Auto-immune disorders are far too rare\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **H**, as it directly states a problem: if the theory claims immune decline causes aging, but the immune system does not actually decline with age (or improves), that would undermine the theory.\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 252}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4955", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A phase 2, multicenter trial was conducted to determine the efficacy of a new vaccine for prevention of HIV infection. The study enrolled 4000 subjects, aged 20 to 65 years. Of these subjects, 2100 were men and 1900 were women; 2500 were white, 1000 were African American, 300 were Hispanic, and 200 were Asian/Pacific Islanders. Results of the trial showed no overall benefit of the vaccine. However, post hoc analysis disclosed a small but statistically significant vaccine protection among African American subjects. Which of the following is the most accurate rationale for questioning the validity of efficacy analysis of the HIV vaccine among the African American study subjects?\n\nOptions: \nA. HIV infection is more prevalent among African American populations\nB. The vaccine had no overall benefit\nC. The study was not blinded\nD. The age of the subjects could have affected the results\nE. The study did not disclose the number of subjects who were actually infected with HIV\nF. There was a Type II error\nG. Vaccine response among African American subjects was not the primary outcome measure\nH. The vaccine response varied across different ethnicities\nI. There was a Type I error\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **I** because the post hoc subgroup analysis showing a statistically significant benefit only in African American subjects is highly susceptible to a Type I error (false positive) due to multiple comparisons without prior hypothesis.  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 312, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 364}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5141", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the human norovirus cannot be cultured in cell cultures how can it best be studied?\n\nOptions: \nA. Volunteer studies\nB. Animal studies using non-human primates\nC. Through computer simulation models of the virus\nD. By studying the virus's effect on plant cells\nE. In cells using replicon systems\nF. Animal models\nG. By isolating the virus in a laboratory setting\nH. In cells using non-replicon systems\nI. Deductions from the 3 human ORF's of the virus genome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most effective current method for studying human norovirus in vitro is through replicon systems, which allow for viral RNA replication and protein expression without producing infectious virus particles. This approach overcomes the lack of a robust cell culture system.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 175, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 230}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5212", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which level of personality description appears to show the most change with age?\n\nOptions: \nA. Values\nB. Communication skills\nC. Identity\nD. Traits\nE. Self-esteem\nF. Interests\nG. Social roles\nH. Emotional responses\nI. Coping strategies\nJ. Personal concerns\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Research suggests that traits (temperament and dispositional characteristics) tend to be relatively stable over adulthood, while personal concerns (goals, values, and life tasks) are more responsive to changing life contexts and age-related shifts.  \n\nTherefore, **J. Personal concerns** shows the most change with age.  \n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Over 1 year, a study is conducted to assess the antileukemic activity of a new tyrosine kinase inhibitor in patients with chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis. All patients enrolled in the study are informed that they would be treated with the tyrosine kinase inhibitor. They are assigned to successive dose cohorts of 300 to 1000 mg/day of the drug. Six to eight patients are assigned to each dose. Treatment efficacy is determined based on the results of complete blood counts and bone marrow assessments conducted regularly throughout the study. This study is best described as which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Prospective observational study\nB. Randomized clinical trial\nC. Quasi-experimental study\nD. Retrospective study\nE. Cohort study\nF. Open-labeled clinical trial\nG. Case-control study\nH. Crossover study\nI. Double-blind clinical trial\nJ. Longitudinal study\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study involves administering a new drug at varying doses to assess efficacy, with all patients aware of the treatment and no mention of blinding or randomization to a control group, making it an open-labeled clinical trial.  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 291, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 351}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5412", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For Binge Eating Disorder it is incorrect that:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. BED patients have higher odds of developing obesity\nB. Binge Eating episodes in BED are usually richer in calories than those of BN, leading patients to obesity\nC. Spontaneous remission is a possible outcome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because binge episodes in bulimia nervosa (BN) are typically similar in caloric content to those in binge eating disorder (BED), and BED does not necessarily involve higher-calorie binges leading more directly to obesity.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 205}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5093", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The best available evidence for an association between amount of sugars and risk of dental caries comes from which type of study design?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Case-control study\nB. Longitudinal study\nC. Non-randomised controlled\nD. Cross sectional observational\nE. Experimental study\nF. Meta-analysis\nG. Qualitative study\nH. Randomised controlled\nI. Cohort\nJ. Ecological study\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The best evidence for a **long-term** association like sugars and dental caries typically comes from prospective cohort studies, which are referred to as \u201clongitudinal studies\u201d in the list.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 187}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5570", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Inviduals suffering from inhalant allergies may also react to cross- reacting food allergens. A person suffering from a natural latex allergy might not react to one of the following allergens\n\n\nOptions: \nA. peanuts\nB. figs\nC. tomato\nD. avocado\nE. peach\nF. kiwi\nG. strawberries\nH. mango\nI. chestnuts\nJ. banana\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A. peanuts** because while latex-fruit syndrome commonly involves cross-reactivity with foods like avocado, banana, kiwi, and chestnut, peanuts are not typically associated with latex cross-reactivity.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 198}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4906", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vitamin D deficiency can often be found as a single nutrient deficiency, that is, in an otherwise well-nourished person. The main reason this can happen is because:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Vitamin D is not essential for the body, therefore, its deficiency doesn't affect the overall nourishment.\nB. Vitamin D is a rare nutrient and can only be found in a few expensive food items.\nC. Vitamin D absorption is not affected by the presence of other nutrients in the body.\nD. The content of vitamin D in foods depends on the soil in which the food was grown so is not related to wealth or age.\nE. Overconsumption of Vitamin D can lead to its deficiency.\nF. Diets containing sufficient other nutrients to promote growth can increase the requirement of vitamin D so that it becomes limiting.\nG. Most vitamin D in the body does not come from food so access to food is not an important determinant of vitamin D status.\nH. Foods containing large amounts of vitamin D are eaten by both poor and wealthy people according to various cultural reasons.\nI. Vitamin D is present in all types of food, therefore, its deficiency is usually accompanied by other nutrient deficiencies.\nJ. Vitamin D is only produced in the body during certain times of the year.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **G**, because the majority of vitamin D is synthesized in the skin from sunlight exposure, not derived from diet, so even well-nourished individuals can become deficient if they have limited sun exposure. This explains why it can occur as an isolated deficiency unrelated to overall nutritional intake. Other options either misstate vitamin D's sources or describe incorrect mechanisms.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 380, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 488}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5312", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new enzyme is found in a transgenic mice that participates in synthesis of an unknown product using two reactants. When using radiolabeled compounds to study the enzyme, it is found that the enzyme catalyzes a process that switches a nitrogen group on one reactant to the other reactant. Which of the following categories would this new enzyme fall under?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ligase\nB. Hydrolase\nC. Transferase\nD. Synthetase\nE. Phosphatase\nF. Lyase\nG. Oxidoreductase\nH. Decarboxylase\nI. Kinase\nJ. Isomerase\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The enzyme transfers a nitrogen group from one reactant to another, which matches the definition of a transferase.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 234}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5180", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 57-year-old man receives radiation therapy for a squamous cell carcinoma of the lung. Despite therapy, the tumor progressively increases in size, and he dies 6 months later. His tumor cells contain a point mutation in the p53 gene (TP53), leading to an inactive gene product. Based on this finding, the progressive tumor growth despite irradiation therapy is most likely to be related to a defect in cell cycle arrest in which of the following phases of the cell cycle?\n\nOptions: \nA. Metaphase\nB. G1\nC. Prophase\nD. G0\nE. Prometaphase\nF. S phase\nG. Anaphase\nH. M\nI. Telophase\nJ. G2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The p53 protein normally induces cell cycle arrest at the G1 phase to allow for DNA repair before replication; a mutation inactivating p53 would impair this checkpoint, allowing damaged cells to progress.  \n\nCorrect choice: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 276}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5143", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sauna use, sometimes referred to as \"sauna bathing,\" is characterized by short-term passive exposure to extreme heat. This exposure elicits mild hyperthermia \u2013 an increase in the body's core temperature \u2013 that induces a thermoregulatory response involving neuroendocrine, cardiovascular, and cytoprotective mechanisms that work together to restore homeostasis and condition the body for future heat stressors\u2026 In recent decades, sauna bathing has emerged as a means to increase lifespan and improve overall health, based on compelling data from observational, interventional, and mechanistic studies. Of particular interest are the findings from studies of participants in the Kuopio Ischemic Heart Disease Risk Factor (KIHD) Study, an ongoing prospective population-based cohort study of health outcomes in more than 2,300 middle-aged men from eastern Finland, which identified strong links between sauna use and reduced death and disease\u2026 The KIHD findings showed that men who used the sauna two to three times per week were 27 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes than men who didn't use the sauna.[2] Furthermore, the benefits they experienced were found to be dose-dependent: Men who used the sauna roughly twice as often, about four to seven times per week, experienced roughly twice the benefits \u2013 and were 50 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes.[2] In addition, frequent sauna users were found to be 40 percent less likely to die from all causes of premature death. These findings held true even when considering age, activity levels, and lifestyle factors that might have influenced the men's health.[2]... The KIHD also revealed that frequent sauna use reduced the risk of developing dementia and Alzheimer's disease in a dose-dependent manner. Men who used the sauna two to three times per week had a 66 percent lower risk of developing dementia and a 65 percent lower risk of developing Alzheimer's disease, compared to men who used the sauna only one time per week\u2026 The health benefits associated with sauna use extended to other aspects of mental health, as well. Men participating in the KIHD study who used the sauna four to seven times per week were 77 percent less likely to develop psychotic disorders, regardless of the men's dietary habits, socioeconomic status, physical activity, and inflammatory status (as measured by C-reactive protein)\u2026Exposure to high temperature stresses the body, eliciting a rapid, robust response. The skin and core body temperatures increase markedly, and sweating ensues. The skin heats first, rising to 40\u00b0C (104\u00b0F), and then changes in core body temperature occur, rising slowly from 37\u00b0C (98.6\u00b0F, or normal) to 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F) and then rapidly increasing to 39\u00b0C (102.2\u00b0F)\u2026  Cardiac output, a measure of the amount of work the heart performs in response to the body's need for oxygen, increases by 60 to 70 percent, while the heart rate (the number of beats per minute) increases and the stroke volume (the amount of blood pumped) remains unchanged.[5] During this time, approximately 50 to 70 percent of the body's blood flow is redistributed from the core to the skin to facilitate sweating. The average person loses approximately 0.5 kg of sweat while sauna bathing.[11] Acute heat exposure also induces a transient increase in overall plasma volume to mitigate the decrease in core blood volume. This increase in plasma volume not only provides a reserve source of fluid for sweating, but it also acts like the water in a car's radiator, cooling the body to prevent rapid increases in core body temperature and promoting heat tolerance\u2026 Repeated sauna use acclimates the body to heat and optimizes the body's response to future exposures, likely due to a biological phenomenon known as hormesis, a compensatory defense response following exposure to a mild stressor that is disproportionate to the magnitude of the stressor. Hormesis triggers a vast array of protective mechanisms that not only repair cell damage but also provide protection from subsequent exposures to more devastating stressors\u2026 The physiological responses to sauna use are remarkably similar to those experienced during moderate- to vigorous-intensity exercise. In fact, sauna use has been proposed as an alternative to exercise for people who are unable to engage in physical activity due to chronic disease or physical limitations.[13]\n\nThe review article sources a lot of data from Finland population studies, where the incidence of sauna use is substantially higher than most countries. Using the data, which of the following is something that is more plausible in Finland than elsewhere?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lower rates of cardiovascular-related deaths among frequent sauna users.\nB. More gold medals in adolescent skiing.\nC. A higher percentage of the population with optimized body's response to heat.\nD. Higher incidence of sauna-related injuries.\nE. Increased prevalence of heat tolerance in the population.\nF. Decreased rates of psychotic disorders among frequent sauna users.\nG. Improved marriage satisfaction rates.\nH. An 86-year old male mayor who is revered in the community.\nI. Decreased risk of dementia and Alzheimer's disease due to frequent sauna use.\nJ. Increased rate of pets in the household.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for something more plausible in Finland than elsewhere based on the data, which highlights Finland's high sauna use leading to heat acclimatization and hormesis. The most direct inference from the text is that frequent sauna use optimizes the body's response to heat, making a higher percentage of the population likely to have this adaptation in Finland. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1126, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 1204}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5483", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sauna use, sometimes referred to as \"sauna bathing,\" is characterized by short-term passive exposure to extreme heat. This exposure elicits mild hyperthermia \u2013 an increase in the body's core temperature \u2013 that induces a thermoregulatory response involving neuroendocrine, cardiovascular, and cytoprotective mechanisms that work together to restore homeostasis and condition the body for future heat stressors\u2026 In recent decades, sauna bathing has emerged as a means to increase lifespan and improve overall health, based on compelling data from observational, interventional, and mechanistic studies. Of particular interest are the findings from studies of participants in the Kuopio Ischemic Heart Disease Risk Factor (KIHD) Study, an ongoing prospective population-based cohort study of health outcomes in more than 2,300 middle-aged men from eastern Finland, which identified strong links between sauna use and reduced death and disease\u2026 The KIHD findings showed that men who used the sauna two to three times per week were 27 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes than men who didn't use the sauna.[2] Furthermore, the benefits they experienced were found to be dose-dependent: Men who used the sauna roughly twice as often, about four to seven times per week, experienced roughly twice the benefits \u2013 and were 50 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes.[2] In addition, frequent sauna users were found to be 40 percent less likely to die from all causes of premature death. These findings held true even when considering age, activity levels, and lifestyle factors that might have influenced the men's health.[2]... The KIHD also revealed that frequent sauna use reduced the risk of developing dementia and Alzheimer's disease in a dose-dependent manner. Men who used the sauna two to three times per week had a 66 percent lower risk of developing dementia and a 65 percent lower risk of developing Alzheimer's disease, compared to men who used the sauna only one time per week\u2026 The health benefits associated with sauna use extended to other aspects of mental health, as well. Men participating in the KIHD study who used the sauna four to seven times per week were 77 percent less likely to develop psychotic disorders, regardless of the men's dietary habits, socioeconomic status, physical activity, and inflammatory status (as measured by C-reactive protein)\u2026Exposure to high temperature stresses the body, eliciting a rapid, robust response. The skin and core body temperatures increase markedly, and sweating ensues. The skin heats first, rising to 40\u00b0C (104\u00b0F), and then changes in core body temperature occur, rising slowly from 37\u00b0C (98.6\u00b0F, or normal) to 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F) and then rapidly increasing to 39\u00b0C (102.2\u00b0F)\u2026  Cardiac output, a measure of the amount of work the heart performs in response to the body's need for oxygen, increases by 60 to 70 percent, while the heart rate (the number of beats per minute) increases and the stroke volume (the amount of blood pumped) remains unchanged.[5] During this time, approximately 50 to 70 percent of the body's blood flow is redistributed from the core to the skin to facilitate sweating. The average person loses approximately 0.5 kg of sweat while sauna bathing.[11] Acute heat exposure also induces a transient increase in overall plasma volume to mitigate the decrease in core blood volume. This increase in plasma volume not only provides a reserve source of fluid for sweating, but it also acts like the water in a car's radiator, cooling the body to prevent rapid increases in core body temperature and promoting heat tolerance\u2026 Repeated sauna use acclimates the body to heat and optimizes the body's response to future exposures, likely due to a biological phenomenon known as hormesis, a compensatory defense response following exposure to a mild stressor that is disproportionate to the magnitude of the stressor. Hormesis triggers a vast array of protective mechanisms that not only repair cell damage but also provide protection from subsequent exposures to more devastating stressors\u2026 The physiological responses to sauna use are remarkably similar to those experienced during moderate- to vigorous-intensity exercise. In fact, sauna use has been proposed as an alternative to exercise for people who are unable to engage in physical activity due to chronic disease or physical limitations.[13]\n\nBased on the article, which of the following statements is the author likely to agree with?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sauna use can prevent the onset of dementia in all cases.\nB. Sauna use is beneficial for mental health regardless of other lifestyle factors.\nC. Patients on a diet would benefit from sauna use.\nD. Patients with skin conditions may be cured with sauna use.\nE. Sauna use may increase the risk of heart disease.\nF. Salt restriction would be equal to sauna use for hypertensive patients.\nG. Heart surgery patients who cannot run on treadmills may benefit from sauna use.\nH. Frequent sauna use causes a significant loss of body weight.\nI. Sauna use can be a potential treatment for Alzheimer's disease.\nJ. Sauna use can completely replace the need for exercise.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the article, the author emphasizes that sauna use can serve as an alternative for those unable to exercise, which aligns with option G.  \nThe article also states that benefits were observed \u201cregardless of the men\u2019s dietary habits\u2026and physical activity,\u201d supporting option B.  \nHowever, since the question asks for the *most likely* correct answer, G is the best match because it is explicitly mentioned in the text.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1114, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 1207}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5507", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Laryngoscopic examination of the vocal folds after suspected recurrent laryngeal nerve damage usually shows that the vocal fold on the injured side is tensed and in an intermediate position between adduction and abduction. This is because\n\nOptions: \nA. Both cricothyroid and interarytenoid muscles are fully active.\nB. Cricothyroid muscle is weak but the interarytenoids are paralyzed.\nC. cricothyroid muscle is paralyzed but the interarytenoids are fully active.\nD. cricothyroid muscle is paralyzed but the interarytenoids are weak.\nE. Cricothyroid muscle is weak but the interarytenoids are fully active.\nF. cricothyroid muscle is still functional but the interarytenoid muscles are fully active.\nG. Interarytenoid muscles are still functional but the cricothyroid is weak.\nH. Both cricothyroid and interarytenoid muscles are paralyzed.\nI. cricothyroid muscle is still functional but the interarytenoids are weak.\nJ. Interarytenoid muscles are still functional but the cricothyroid is fully active.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The recurrent laryngeal nerve supplies all intrinsic laryngeal muscles except the cricothyroid (which is supplied by the external branch of the superior laryngeal nerve). If it is injured, the cricothyroid remains functional, but the interarytenoids (along with other adductors) are paralyzed, leaving the vocal fold in the paramedian (intermediate) position due to unopposed cricothyroid tension.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 297, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 394}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5408", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about intestinal \"brakes\" and \"accelerators\" is FALSE?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Short-chain fatty acids which move from colon to caecum (reflux) promote ileo-caecal motility\nB. The arrival of fiber in the colon causes an increase in motility and a switch from the \"fasting\" to the \"feeding\" pattern.\nC. The arrival of lipid in the duodenum causes an immediate reduction in motility and a switch from the \"fasting\" to the \"feeding\" pattern.\nD. Food in the stomach causes gastrin release, which stimulates acid secretion\nE. Protein ingestion leads to immediate increase in intestinal motility\nF. Gastric acid secretion inhibits small intestinal motility\nG. The presence of bile in the intestine slows down motility\nH. The presence of undigested food in the colon stimulates intestinal motility\nI. Dietary starch is a potent stimulator of small intestinal motility because it causes insulin release from the pancreas\nJ. The presence of glucose in the duodenum accelerates intestinal motility\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The false statement is **C**, because lipid in the duodenum typically triggers the **ileal brake**, which reduces motility and prolongs the fasting pattern rather than switching to the feeding pattern.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 321, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 374}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5179", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study is designed to evaluate the feasibility of acupuncture in children with chronic headaches. Sixty children with chronic headaches are recruited for the study. In addition to their usual therapy, all children are treated with acupuncture three times a week for 2 months. Which of the following best describes this study design?\n\nOptions: \nA. Randomized control trial\nB. Case-control\nC. Case series\nD. Crossover\nE. Longitudinal\nF. Meta-analysis\nG. Cohort\nH. Cross-sectional\nI. Qualitative study\nJ. Systematic review\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study involves a single group receiving an intervention without a control group, which is characteristic of a case series design.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 243}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5422", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A psychologist conducts an experiment in which subjects are asked to learn a series of \u201cfacts\u201d which are actually statements that have been fabricated by the research team. The subjects consist of undergraduate students at the university where the experiment is being conducted. The subjects are randomly assigned to groups that are compensated either $10 or $20 for their participation, are given either 15 minutes or 30 minutes to learn the facts, and are asked to recall the facts either in the same room in which they learned the facts or in a very different, unfamiliar setting. Which of the following are dependent variables in this experiment?\nI. The amount the subjects were compensated.\nII. The room in which the subjects were asked to recall facts.\nIII. The number of facts the subjects can recall.\nIV. The time the subjects were given to learn the facts.\n\nOptions: \nA. I and II only\nB. III only\nC. I, II, and III only\nD. II, III, and IV only\nE. I and IV only\nF. I and III and IV only\nG. I, III, and IV only\nH. II and IV only\nI. II only\nJ. I, II, and IV only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The dependent variable is what is measured as the outcome; here, that is the number of facts recalled (III). Compensation amount (I), recall room (II), and learning time (IV) are all manipulated by the researcher, so they are independent variables.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 339, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 404}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5313", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A teacher sets up a reward system for her elementary school students. At the end of each day, she gives a sticker to each student who showed up on time that morning. At the end of each week, she gives a sticker to any student who got above a 90% on three quizzes in a row. After months of this regimen, she finds that performance on the quizzes has increased significantly but that tardiness has only decreased slightly. Which of the following best explains the teacher\u2019s observation?\n\nOptions: \nA. The students had more intrinsic motivation to do well on quizzes than to show up on time.\nB. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nC. The students were more excited about the quizzes than about the reward system.\nD. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-interval schedule than it was to a fixed-ratio schedule.\nE. Variable ratio schedules create the strongest responses and behavior that is the least susceptible to extinction.\nF. The students\u2019 behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nG. The students' behavior change was weaker in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nH. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-interval schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nI. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a continuous reinforcement schedule than it was to a variable-ratio schedule.\nJ. The students\u2019 behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a variable-interval schedule.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **F** because the quiz reward follows a fixed-ratio schedule (reinforcement after a set number of correct responses \u2014 3 high quiz scores), which tends to produce strong and steady behavior change, while the tardiness reward uses continuous reinforcement (every instance of on-time arrival), which is less resistant to extinction and can lead to weaker long-term change when compared.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 505, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 609}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5316", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A scientist using mouse models to determine the response of blood hormones to large levels of glucose in the body discovers a new hormone not previously described. According to his data, this hormone is found both inside and out of cells when carrying out its function, increase the amount of nucleic acid in the cell while functioning, and are derived from a structure containing four hydroxycarbon rings. This will likely be categorized as which type of hormone?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lipid-based\nB. Eicosanoid\nC. Glycoprotein\nD. Enzymatic\nE. Protein-based\nF. Carbohydrate-based\nG. Nucleic acid-based\nH. Steroid\nI. Amino acid\nJ. Peptide\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The hormone is described as being derived from a structure containing four hydroxycarbon rings, which is characteristic of steroids, and steroids are lipid-based hormones that can enter cells and affect gene expression (increasing nucleic acid).  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 230, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 299}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5107", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All other things being equal, which of the following persons is likely to live the longest?\n\nOptions: \nA. A black woman\nB. A Hispanic man\nC. A white woman\nD. An Asian man\nE. A white man\nF. A Native American man\nG. A Hispanic woman\nH. A Native American woman\nI. A black man\nJ. An Asian woman\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on U.S. life expectancy data, Asian women generally have the longest life expectancy among the listed demographic groups.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 145, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5294", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a cohort study of elderly women, the relative risk ratio for hip fractures among those who exercise regularly is 1.2 (95% confidence interval of 1.1 to 1.8). Which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion about the effect of regular exercise on the risk for hip fracture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Statistically significant overall increase in risk\nB. Statistically insignificant change in risk for those who exercise regularly\nC. Statistically significant overall decrease in risk\nD. Statistically nonsignificant decrease in risk\nE. Statistically significant decrease in risk only for those over 80\nF. Statistically significant overall decrease in risk for those who exercise regularly\nG. Statistically nonsignificant overall decrease in risk\nH. Statistically significant increase in risk only for those under 70\nI. No statistically significant change in risk\nJ. Statistically nonsignificant increase in risk\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The relative risk is 1.2, and the 95% confidence interval (1.1 to 1.8) does not include 1.0, so the increase in risk is statistically significant.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 300, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 342}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5402", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements is incorrect regarding fatty acid \u00df-oxidation?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The rate of \u00df-oxidation is regulated by the availability of carbohydrates and the rate of utilisation of \u00df-oxidation products\nB. Peroxisomes are the site for the degradation of xenobiotics and eicosanoids\nC. Within the liver peroxisomes serve to oxidise very long chain fatty acids to medium chain products\nD. The rate of b-oxidation is regulated by the availability of fatty acids and the rate of utilisation of b-oxidation products\nE. The major site of fatty acid \u00df-oxidation is the peroxisomes, the mitochondria also contain enzymes for this pathway\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The incorrect statement is **E**, because the major site of fatty acid \u03b2-oxidation is actually the mitochondria (not peroxisomes), though peroxisomes do handle very long-chain fatty acids initially.  \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 234, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 286}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4952", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During a study of renal glomeruli, a healthy animal kidney is kept in a vascular bath preparation at a constant afferent arterial pressure of 100 mm Hg. If the efferent arteriole is constricted with a vascular clamp, which of the following Starling forces is most likely to change in the glomeruli?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased filtration coefficient (Kf)\nB. Increased hydrostatic pressure\nC. Increased blood flow\nD. Increased oncotic pressure\nE. Decreased hydrostatic pressure\nF. No change in Starling forces\nG. Decreased oncotic pressure\nH. Decreased filtration coefficient (Kf)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Constricting the efferent arteriole increases resistance downstream from the glomerulus, raising the glomerular capillary hydrostatic pressure. This is a key Starling force for filtration.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 241}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5411", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The function of the gastrointestinal tract can be classified in several ways. Which of the following functions is most important for survival immediately after a meal?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Elimination of toxins\nB. Stimulation of appetite\nC. Maintenance of barrier function\nD. Extraction of maximum value from nutrients\nE. Control of blood sugar levels\nF. Production of hormones for growth and repair\nG. Regulation of body temperature\nH. Processing of food into a liquid form\nI. Absorption and retention of water and electrolytes\nJ. Production of digestive enzymes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most critical immediate function after a meal is to process food into a liquid form (chyme) so that nutrients can later be absorbed; without this mechanical and chemical breakdown, other digestive steps cannot proceed efficiently. While absorption and blood sugar control are important, they follow digestion.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 178, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 243}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5524", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new severe respiratory illness caused by a newly identified virus is discovered. Which of the following properties of a killed vaccine relative to a live vaccine is the most appropriate rationale for developing a killed vaccine for this illness?\n\nOptions: \nA. Is more likely to provide sterilizing immunity\nB. Can be administered in higher doses\nC. Develops more rapid protective immunity\nD. Is less likely to require subsequent boosters for lifelong immunity\nE. Is less likely to cause an allergic reaction\nF. Is more effective for immunocompromised individuals\nG. Is most likely to generate mucosal immunity\nH. Is less likely to cause local adverse reactions at the site of injection\nI. Avoids the concern for reversion to virulence\nJ. Is less likely to be affected by preexisting antibodies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **I** because a killed vaccine uses inactivated virus, which eliminates the risk of the pathogen reverting to virulence\u2014a safety advantage over live vaccines especially for a newly identified severe respiratory virus.  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 271}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5164", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient suffers a broken neck with damage to the spinal cord at the level of the sixth cervical vertebra.\n\nOptions: \nA. It is impossible to predict an effect on breathing.\nB. Their breathing rate will significantly increase.\nC. They will only be able to breathe quietly.\nD. Their breathing will be erratic and unpredictable.\nE. They will be unable to breathe without life support.\nF. Breathing will be unaffected.\nG. They will be able to breathe only with the help of a ventilator.\nH. They will be able to breathe only in short, shallow breaths.\nI. They will have to breathe through a tracheostomy tube.\nJ. They will not be able to breathe out, only in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "C6 is above the C3\u2013C5 region that contains the phrenic nerve motor neurons, so diaphragmatic breathing is likely preserved; however, intercostal and abdominal muscle function would be impaired, leading to reduced breathing capacity.\n\nThis matches best with option **H** (they will be able to breathe only in short, shallow breaths).\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 278}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4996", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assuming that the level of glucose is low, a mutation in the repressor associated with the lac operon of E. coli which prevents binding of the repressor to lactose should result in: \n\nOptions: \nA. expression of the genes only when glucose is present\nB. lack of expression or reduced expression of the lac operon genes under all circumstances\nC. no change in the expression of the lac operon genes\nD. expression of the genes only when lactose is absent\nE. constitutive expression of the lac operon genes\nF. expression of the genes only when lactose is present\nG. increased expression of the lac operon genes under all circumstances\nH. expression of the genes only when glucose is absent\nI. constitutive repression of the lac operon genes\nJ. reduced expression of the lac operon genes only when lactose is present\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The mutation prevents the repressor from binding lactose, so it cannot be inactivated even when lactose is present. This means the repressor would remain bound to the operator and block transcription regardless of lactose levels. Therefore, the lac operon genes would not be expressed under any condition.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 275, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 354}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5397", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study is conducted to assess the effectiveness of a new drug for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus. A total of 1000 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus are enrolled. Patients are randomly assigned to receive the new drug or standard treatment. The alpha and beta values for calculating probability are 0.05 and 0.20, respectively. Results show that the new drug is significantly better than standard treatment. If this study had been performed in a population of only 500 patients, which of the following would have been most likely to increase?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chance of a type II error\nB. Chance of a false positive result\nC. Size of the study population\nD. Power of the study\nE. Sensitivity of the study\nF. Specificity of the study\nG. Chance of a false negative result\nH. Probability of the alpha value\nI. Chance of a type I error\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Reducing the sample size from 1000 to 500 decreases the power of the study (which is 1 \u2212 \u03b2, and \u03b2 was 0.20 originally). With lower power, the probability of failing to detect a true effect (type II error) increases, meaning the chance of a false negative result also increases.  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 283, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 355}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5214", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following factors has NOT received as much support as the others in research investigating why social support is related to better health?\n\nOptions: \nA. Physiological\nB. Behavioral\nC. Biological\nD. Anthropological\nE. Environmental\nF. Psychological\nG. Gerontological\nH. Neurological\nI. Social\nJ. Sociological\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks which factor has **not** received as much support in research on why social support improves health.  \nThe most commonly supported pathways in health psychology are behavioral, psychological, and physiological/biological mechanisms, while **anthropological** explanations are not a standard category in this research literature.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 198}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5269", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If links between various diseases are found, then future older adults will probably\n\nOptions: \nA. Have a shorter life expectancy\nB. Be less likely to seek medical advice\nC. Take fewer medications\nD. Pay far less for pharmaceuticals\nE. Have higher medical insurance premiums\nF. Be able to self-diagnose diseases\nG. Have to undergo more medical tests\nH. Have increased immunity to diseases\nI. Pick and choose the disease(s) they want\nJ. Be able to avoid certain diseases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "If links between diseases are discovered, it could lead to better prevention or early intervention, making it possible for future older adults to avoid certain conditions. Among the options, the one that logically follows from such medical advances is the ability to avoid certain diseases.  \n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 189, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 264}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5064", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 77-year-old female presents to the office for evaluation of a syncopal event that occurred while she was walking. Cardiac examination reveals a grade 3/6\u00a0systolic murmur, heard best at the right upper sternal border. There is radiation of the murmur into the neck. The valvular abnormality that most likely caused this episode is\n\nOptions: \nA. bicuspid aortic valve\nB. aortic insufficiency\nC. mitral valve prolapse\nD. tricuspid stenosis\nE. mitral regurgitation\nF. pulmonary regurgitation\nG. aortic stenosis\nH. pulmonary stenosis\nI. tricuspid regurgitation\nJ. mitral stenosis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The murmur described (systolic, loud, radiating to the neck, right upper sternal border) is classic for aortic stenosis, which is a common cause of syncope, especially with exertion in older adults.  \n**Answer:** \\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 271}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4860", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following releases most energy when completely oxidised in the body?\n\nOptions: \nA. One gram of glycerol\nB. One gram of lactose\nC. One gram of fructose\nD. One gram of palmitic acid\nE. One gram of cellulose\nF. One gram of glucose\nG. One gram of alcohol\nH. One gram of leucine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D. One gram of palmitic acid** because fats (like palmitic acid, a saturated fatty acid) yield about 9 kcal/g upon oxidation, which is more than carbohydrates (~4 kcal/g) or proteins (~4 kcal/g). Glycerol, lactose, fructose, cellulose, glucose, alcohol, and leucine all have lower energy densities per gram.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 144, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 229}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5500", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Loss of muscle fiber may be due to loss of neurons which may be due to\n\nOptions: \nA. Exposure to extreme cold\nB. Clogged blood vessels\nC. Loss of collagen\nD. Loss of skin elasticity\nE. Decreased water intake\nF. Loss of bone density\nG. Increased fat intake\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Loss of neurons that leads to muscle fiber atrophy is most directly linked to **clogged blood vessels** (ischemia), which can reduce oxygen and nutrient supply to nerve cells.  \nThe correct choice is **B**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 178}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5020", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A placebo-controlled clinical trial is conducted to assess whether a new antihypertensive drug is more effective than standard therapy. A total of 5000 patients with essential hypertension are enrolled and randomly assigned to one of two groups: 2500 patients receive the new drug and 2500 patients receive placebo. If the alpha is set at 0.01 instead of 0.05, which of the following is the most likely result?\n\nOptions: \nA. The study will have less power\nB. The study will require fewer participants\nC. There is an increased likelihood of statistically significant findings\nD. The study will be less reliable\nE. Significant findings can be reported with greater confidence\nF. The placebo effect will be more pronounced\nG. The study will have more power\nH. There is a decreased likelihood of statistically significant findings\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Reducing alpha (from 0.05 to 0.01) means the threshold for rejecting the null hypothesis becomes stricter. This lowers the probability of a Type I error but increases the probability of a Type II error, thus reducing the power of the study and making statistically significant findings less likely.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 230, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 298}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5453", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 22-year-old male presents to the office with a\u00a05-day\u00a0history of diarrhea after completing his third course of antibiotics for mastoiditis. Physical examination reveals vague generalized abdominal pain on palpation. Culture on hektoen enteric agar is positive. The most likely etiologic agent causing the diarrhea is\n\nOptions: \nA. Clostridium difficile\nB. Entamoeba histolytica\nC. Vibrio cholerae\nD. Escherichia coli\nE. Staphylococcus aureus\nF. Campylobacter jejuni\nG. Giardia lamblia\nH. Salmonella typhi\nI. Yersinia enterocolitica\nJ. Shigella dysenteriae\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A. *Clostridium difficile*** because the patient has antibiotic-associated diarrhea following multiple courses of antibiotics, and *C. difficile* is the most common cause of this presentation. Hektoen enteric agar is typically used for *Salmonella* and *Shigella*, but *C. difficile* is diagnosed by toxin assay or selective culture, not this agar; however, the clinical history strongly points to *C. difficile* despite the agar detail being a distractor.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 310}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5447", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 30-year-old nulliparous female presents to the office with the complaint of mood changes. She says that for the past several months she has been anxious, hyperactive, and unable to sleep 3 to 4\u00a0days prior to the onset of menses. She further reports that on the day her menses begins she becomes acutely depressed, anorectic, irritable, and lethargic. She has no psychiatric history. Physical examination findings are normal. She and her husband have been trying to conceive for over 2\u00a0years. History reveals a tuboplasty approximately 1\u00a0year ago to correct a closed fallopian tube. The most likely diagnosis is\n\nOptions: \nA. generalized anxiety disorder\nB. bipolar I disorder, mixed\nC. Premenstrual dysphoric disorder\nD. cyclothymic personality\nE. Persistent depressive disorder (dysthymia)\nF. Post-traumatic stress disorder\nG. Seasonal affective disorder\nH. Bipolar II disorder\nI. adjustment disorder with depressed mood\nJ. Major depressive disorder\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The symptoms are temporally linked to the menstrual cycle, with mood changes occurring specifically in the days before and at the onset of menses, which is characteristic of **premenstrual dysphoric disorder**.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 310, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 365}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5123", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 19-year-old male presents to the office for evaluation after he was hit from behind below the right knee while playing football. Gait analysis reveals a lack of fluid motion. Standing flexion test results are negative. Cruciate and collateral knee ligaments appear intact. Foot drop on the right is noted. The most likely diagnosis is\n\nOptions: \nA. meniscus tear\nB. tibial stress fracture\nC. posterior cruciate ligament tear\nD. unilateral sacral shear\nE. patellar dislocation\nF. medial collateral ligament sprain\nG. posteriorly deviated fibular head\nH. anterior cruciate ligament tear\nI. plantar flexed cuboid\nJ. anteriorly deviated distal femur\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The foot drop suggests peroneal nerve injury, which can occur with a fibular head displacement due to trauma near the knee. A posteriorly deviated fibular head could compress the nerve, matching the mechanism and findings.  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 234, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 292}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5295", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 33-year-old man undergoes a radical thyroidectomy for thyroid cancer. During the operation, moderate hemorrhaging requires ligation of several vessels in the left side of the neck. Postoperatively, serum studies show a calcium concentration of 7.5 mg/dL, albumin concentration of 4 g/dL, and parathyroid hormone concentration of 200 pg/mL. Damage to which of the following vessels caused the findings in this patient?\n\nOptions: \nA. Branch of the costocervical trunk\nB. Branch of the external carotid artery\nC. Branch of the thyrocervical trunk\nD. Tributary of the internal jugular vein\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has hypocalcemia with high PTH, indicating secondary hyperparathyroidism due to parathyroid gland damage or compromised blood supply after thyroidectomy. The parathyroid glands are primarily supplied by branches of the inferior thyroid artery, which arises from the thyrocervical trunk.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 299}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5443", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A healthy 22-year-old man participates in a study of glucose metabolism. At the beginning of the study, his serum glucose concentration is within the reference range. He consumes an 800-calorie meal consisting of protein, fat, and carbohydrates. He then sleeps through the night without additional food or drink. Twelve hours later, his serum glucose concentration remains within the reference range. Which of the following mechanisms is most likely involved in maintaining this man's serum glucose concentration?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased glucose uptake by the brain\nB. Continued gut absorption of calories from the ingested meal\nC. Increased glucose uptake by red blood cells\nD. Glucose release from skeletal muscle\nE. Glycogenolysis in the liver\nF. Increased leptin release from adipose tissues\nG. Enhanced gluconeogenesis in the kidney\nH. Elevated insulin secretion from the pancreas\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "After fasting overnight, the liver maintains blood glucose primarily through glycogen breakdown (glycogenolysis). The other options either do not occur during fasting (like elevated insulin) or are not the main source of glucose after a 12-hour fast.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 293, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 361}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4885", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An 18-year-old man is brought to the emergency department 10 minutes after he sustained a stab wound to his chest. On arrival, he is unresponsive to painful stimuli. His pulse is 130/min, respirations are 8/min and shallow, and palpable systolic blood pressure is 60 mm Hg. He is intubated and mechanically ventilated, and infusion of 0.9% saline is begun. After 5 minutes, his pulse is 130/min, and blood pressure is 70/40 mm Hg. Examination shows a 2-cm wound at the left sixth intercostal space at the midclavicular line. There is jugular venous distention. Breath sounds are normal. The trachea is at the midline. Heart sounds are not audible. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pericardiocentesis\nB. Perform a CT scan of the chest\nC. Thoracentesis\nD. Bronchoscopy\nE. Administer morphine for pain management\nF. Echocardiography\nG. Chest x-ray\nH. Surgical exploration of the wound\nI. Administer intravenous antibiotics\nJ. Administer oxygen therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has signs of cardiac tamponade (hypotension, jugular venous distention, muffled heart sounds) following a stab wound to the chest, which requires immediate pericardiocentesis to relieve the tamponade.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 322, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 381}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4907", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Water transport can occur from the lumen of the intestine to the blood stream, or from the blood stream to the intestinal lumen. Which single statement about this phenomenon, below, is actually correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Dietary intake of water is always greater than water movement in the small intestine\nB. Water flows into the gut from the mucosa, during digestion of starch and protein, in order to reduce luminal osmolality\nC. Water flows out of the gut from the mucosa, during digestion of starch and protein, in order to increase luminal osmolality\nD. Water is primarily transported by movement within the cells lining the gut (enterocytes)\nE. Water is mostly absorbed by movement between the cells lining the gut (enterocytes) via tight junctions\nF. Water transport from the blood stream to the intestinal lumen only occurs during digestion\nG. Water transport from the intestine to the blood stream does not occur during digestion\nH. A \"flip-flop\" mechanism efficiently transports water directly across the enterocyte membrane\nI. Water is mostly absorbed by the cells lining the gut (enterocytes) via osmosis\nJ. Water movement in the small intestine is always lesser than dietary intake of water\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Correct answer:**  \n\\boxed{E}\n\nWater absorption in the intestine primarily occurs via paracellular pathways (between enterocytes) driven by osmotic gradients, especially in the small intestine. Tight junctions allow bulk fluid movement, making this the most quantitatively significant route compared to transcellular transport.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 305, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 363}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5013", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 35-year-old woman comes to the office because of a 3-day history of severe right back pain. She has not had any fever, chills, or weight loss. She has no history of major medical illness. Musculoskeletal and neurologic examinations show no abnormalities. When told that her examination is normal, the patient becomes tearful and demands an MRI of her back because her mother just died from breast cancer metastatic to bone and she fears that she may also have cancer. The patient already contacted her insurance company, who told her that if she has neurologic abnormalities an MRI may be covered by her plan. The patient asks the physician to order the MRI indicating that she has neurologic findings. Which of the following is the most appropriate initial action by the physician?\n\nOptions: \nA. Advise the patient to change insurance companies as soon as she is able so that she can receive more comprehensive medical care\nB. Explain that the patient does not need the MRI and that it is not appropriate to misrepresent her examination findings\nC. Immediately inform the patient's insurance company about what the patient has asked the physician to do\nD. Order the MRI as the patient requests\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate initial action is to uphold honesty in medical documentation while addressing the patient\u2019s concerns directly.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 300, "output_tokens": 27, "total_tokens": 327}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5031", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about methods of evaluating protein quality in human nutrition is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The Biological Value (BV) of a protein does not affect its quality in human nutrition.\nB. The Digestible Indispensable Amino Acid Score (DIAAS) is not a reliable method for assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\nC. The growing rat is a good model for assessing protein quality in human nutrition.\nD. The use of rats in protein quality tests overestimates the quality of dietary proteins for human nutrition.\nE. Animal growth assays underestimate the quality of dietary proteins for human nutrition\nF. The Chemical Score (CS) is the most accurate method for assessing protein quality in human nutrition.\nG. The rat net protein-utilisation assay, (NPU), is the best method of assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\nH. The Protein Digestibility Corrected Amino Acid Score (PDCAAS) is the worst method for assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\nI. The Human Amino Acid Requirement Pattern (HAARP) is the most reliable method for assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\nJ. The rat protein efficiency ratio assay, (PER), is a good method of assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because rat growth assays often overestimate protein quality for humans due to differing amino acid requirements between species.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 381, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 423}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5073", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 15-year-old girl is brought to the physician 3 months after she had a blood pressure of 150/95 mm Hg at a routine examination prior to participation in school sports. She is asymptomatic and has no history of serious illness. Twelve months ago, she was diagnosed with a urinary tract infection and treated with oral trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole. She currently takes no medications. Subsequent blood pressure measurements on three separate occasions since the last visit have been: 155/94 mm Hg, 145/90 mm Hg, and 150/92 mm Hg. She is at the 50th percentile for height and 95th percentile for weight. Her blood pressure today is 150/90 mm Hg confirmed by a second measurement, pulse is 80/min, and respirations are 12/min. Examination shows no other abnormalities. Her hematocrit is 40%. Urinalysis is within normal limits. Cardiac and renal ultrasonography shows no abnormalities. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Measurement of serum potassium levels\nB. Measurement of urine corticosteroid concentrations\nC. Exercise and weight reduction program\nD. Captopril therapy\nE. Initiate diuretic therapy\nF. Referral for psychiatric evaluation\nG. Initiate calcium channel blocker therapy\nH. Measurement of urine catecholamine concentrations\nI. Measurement of plasma renin activity\nJ. Initiate beta-blocker therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has persistent hypertension without an identifiable secondary cause on initial workup, and given her obesity (95th percentile for weight), lifestyle modification is the recommended first step.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 364, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 405}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5124", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 16-year-old high school student, whose prenatal course you have managed, delivers a 3256-g (7-lb 3-oz) baby girl during the night with the assistance of your associate. On morning rounds you note that the delivery records report that she had mildly elevated blood pressure during labor and sustained an estimated third-stage blood loss of 500 mL. Today blood pressure is 132/84 mm Hg, she is afebrile, and deep tendon reflexes are normal. The uterine fundus is firm and at the level of the umbilicus, and her perineum is slightly edematous. Hematocrit is 33%. She is cuddling her infant and normal bonding seems to be occurring. Which of the following is the most important next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Order a blood transfusion\nB. Order daily sitz baths\nC. Initiate breastfeeding education\nD. Begin oral methyldopa\nE. Perform a pelvic examination\nF. Institute fundal massage\nG. Prescribe bed rest\nH. Begin intravenous fluids\nI. Administer antihypertensive medication\nJ. Provide education for well-baby care\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has mild postpartum hypertension but no signs of preeclampsia (normal reflexes, no severe symptoms) and stable vital signs with a firm uterus; the most important next step is to ensure uterine tone remains adequate to prevent further bleeding, which is best accomplished with fundal massage.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 327, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 405}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5129", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 76-year-old man comes to the office because of early awakening at night. He has no difficulty falling asleep but routinely wakes up between 2:00 and 3:00 AM. The patient is a retired postal worker, and he has always been physically active. He has diabetes mellitus controlled by diet. The patient drinks one cup of coffee in the morning with breakfast and usually walks for exercise in the morning. Before retiring at night he has one alcoholic beverage. He has no history of depression, nightmares, or snoring and he takes no over-the-counter medications. His wife of 45 years is also in good health. Vital signs are temperature 37.1\u00b0C (98.8\u00b0F), pulse 96/min and regular, respirations 18/min, and blood pressure 135/90 mm Hg. Physical examination shows a well-nourished, well-developed man. He is not obese. Examination of the head and neck is normal; there are no bruits or jugular venous distention. Chest is clear, and heart is normal with S1 and S2. Abdomen is soft and nontender with active bowel sounds and no organomegaly. Rectal examination discloses no abnormalities. Which of the following is the most appropriate management of this patient's insomnia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Recommend the patient to watch television before going to bed.\nB. Prescribe sleeping pills\nC. Advise the patient to read and snack in bed to relax\nD. Recommend a daytime nap to compensate for lost sleep\nE. Prescribe a vigorous pre-bedtime exercise regimen\nF. Prescribe sertraline\nG. Prescribe a low-carb diet\nH. Advise the patient to discontinue his bedtime drink of alcohol\nI. Advise the patient to drink alcohol earlier in the day\nJ. Advise the patient to increase his intake of caffeine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate choice is **H** because alcohol can disrupt sleep architecture and cause early morning awakenings, even if consumed near bedtime.\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 489, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 529}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5135", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the limitations of food balance sheets? (select all that apply)?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Accurate information on food production is always guaranteed\nB. They account for the impact of climate change on food availability\nC. They take into account the consumption of processed and packaged food items\nD. All of the options given are correct\nE. They provide a comprehensive overview of the nutritional status of a population\nF. They provide real-time data on food availability and consumption\nG. They always include data on home-grown and locally sourced food items\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answers are none of the above, as all options describe things food balance sheets do **not** do reliably. Based on the given choices, the limitations are implied by **E** and **F**, but since \"select all that apply\" is stated and the format requests a single boxed letter, the most fitting single choice covering multiple limitations is not present. Given the instruction, the best answer from the options is:  \n\\boxed{E}  \n\n*Food balance sheets are aggregate supply estimates and do not provide a comprehensive overview of individual nutritional status, nor do they provide real-time data.*", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 171, "output_tokens": 122, "total_tokens": 293}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5183", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 38-year-old man with Down syndrome and severe mental retardation is brought to the emergency department by ambulance because of increasing lethargy for the past several hours. The patient is noncommunicative and you are unable to obtain an initial history of his present illness or a past medical history. You do not know if he takes any medications. Vital signs are temperature 38.3\u00b0C (100.9\u00b0F), pulse 90/min, respirations 19/min, and blood pressure 120/60 mm Hg. On physical examination the patient is awake but lethargic. Auscultation of the chest discloses clear lungs; cardiac examination discloses a systolic click. Neurologic examination shows decreased muscle tone. Serum electrolyte concentrations are normal. Complete blood count shows a leukocyte count of 18,000/mm3 with 23% band neutrophils. The patient's caregiver, who is also the patient's guardian, cannot be located and staff at the group home where the patient resides cannot be reached by telephone. The patient refuses lumbar puncture for examination of cerebrospinal fluid. Toxicologic screening of the urine is negative. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step?\n\nOptions: \nA. Obtain echocardiography\nB. Administer oral antibiotics\nC. Provide intravenous fluids and observe\nD. Order a chest X-ray\nE. Initiate seizure precautions\nF. Await contact with the caregiver before proceeding with management\nG. Wait for the patient's consent for a lumbar puncture\nH. Obtain CT scan of the head\nI. Administer intravenous antibiotics\nJ. Perform a psychiatric evaluation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has signs of infection (fever, leukocytosis with left shift) and lethargy, suggesting possible meningitis or sepsis; given the refusal of lumbar puncture and inability to obtain history, starting empiric intravenous antibiotics is urgent while further diagnostics are arranged.\n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 386, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 443}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5235", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 5-year-old boy is brought to the physician by his mother because of a 2-day history of a low-grade fever, cough, and runny nose. His temperature is 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F). Examination findings are consistent with a diagnosis of a common cold. The physician refers to a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical trial that evaluated the effectiveness of a new drug for the treatment of the common cold. The mean time for resolution of symptoms for patients receiving the new drug was 6.4 days, compared with a mean time of 6.7 days for patients receiving the placebo (p=0.04). Which of the following is the most appropriate interpretation of these study results?\n\nOptions: \nA. The findings are statistically significant, but the clinical relevance is undetermined\nB. The findings are statistically significant, but their clinical significance is negative.\nC. The findings are neither clinically nor statistically significant\nD. The findings are clinically and statistically significant\nE. The findings suggest a potential clinical significance, but are statistically insignificant\nF. The findings are statistically insignificant, but the clinical relevance is undetermined\nG. The findings are both clinically and statistically indeterminate\nH. The findings are statistically insignificant, but they suggest a trend towards clinical significance\nI. The findings are clinically significant but statistically insignificant\nJ. The findings are clinically insignificant but statistically significant\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The p-value of 0.04 indicates statistical significance, but a difference of only 0.3 days in symptom resolution is likely too small to be considered clinically meaningful.  \nTherefore, the results are statistically significant but of uncertain clinical relevance.  \nThe best match is **J** (clinically insignificant but statistically significant) though option **A** also acknowledges clinical relevance is undetermined; however, **J** directly addresses the small magnitude difference described.\n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 342, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 439}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5254", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about the nutritional status of older people is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Consuming multivitamins can eliminate all nutritional deficiencies in older people.\nB. High protein diet is harmful for older people.\nC. Older people are more prone to Vitamin A overdose.\nD. All older people require dietary supplementation to maintain nutritional status.\nE. The risk of high iron stores is greater than the risk of iron deficiency in older people.\nF. Older people should consume more sodium to maintain their health.\nG. All older people living in Western countries have low vitamin D status.\nH. Low dietary intake of vitamin B12 is the main cause of vitamin B12 deficiency in older people.\nI. Calcium intake is not important for older people.\nJ. There is strong evidence that vitamin C supplements lower the risk of cancer in older people.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the options given, **E** is the most likely correct answer: the risk of high iron stores can indeed be a concern in older adults, especially men and postmenopausal women, due to reduced iron excretion and potential accumulation from supplements or diet, which increases the risk of chronic diseases.  \nThe other statements are either false or too absolute (e.g., A, D, F, G, I) or misrepresent current evidence (B, C, H, J).  \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 230, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 334}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5296", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 37-year-old man with type 1 diabetes mellitus is admitted to the hospital because of inadequate control of his glucose concentrations for the past 2 months. Despite his poor control, he demands that he be discharged. He reports that he has had a 3-month history of fatigue, irritability, and feelings of hopelessness. He says that he has been noncompliant with his diabetic regimen, adding, \"Sometimes I forget.\" He has been avoiding his family and friends because he is not in the mood to see them but admits that he is lonely. He did not get out of bed for 2 days, which prompted his wife to call an ambulance and have him admitted to the hospital. Prior to admission to the hospital, his only medication was insulin, although he often missed doses. He does not drink alcohol. He is 168 cm (5 ft 6 in) tall and weighs 100 kg (220 lb); BMI is 36 kg/m2 . His temperature is 37\u00b0C (98.6\u00b0F), pulse is 68/min, respirations are 18/min, and blood pressure is 150/85 mm Hg. Physical examination shows no abnormalities. On mental status examination, he is tired and has a restricted affect. There is no evidence of suicidal ideation. Cognition is intact. His fasting serum glucose concentration is 120 mg/dL. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Start a diet and exercise regimen\nB. Prescribe medication for depression\nC. Begin a psychotherapy session\nD. Insist on hospitalization against the patient's wishes\nE. Adhere to the patient's wishes and discuss home-care options\nF. Schedule neuropsychological testing\nG. Seek a court order to appoint a legal guardian\nH. Adhere to the patient's wishes on the condition that he agree to home nursing care\nI. Conduct a full body physical examination\nJ. Initiate insulin therapy immediately\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has depressive symptoms affecting his diabetes management but lacks acute medical instability or suicidality, so involuntary hospitalization is not justified. The most appropriate step is to address his depression to improve adherence and outcomes.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 460, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 510}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5300", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 35-year-old male presents to the office for the result of an HIV test, and he is informed that the result is positive. The patient resists disclosure to his wife because he has not told her about his extramarital sexual partners. The physician informs the patient that his wife's right to know is paramount because she could also be HIV positive. Which of the following relationships best describes the rationale for the physician's recommendation that the patient inform his wife of his condition rather than withhold this information?\n\nOptions: \nA. justice overrides autonomy\nB. nonmaleficence overrides beneficence\nC. beneficence overrides justice\nD. autonomy overrides beneficence\nE. autonomy is equal to nonmaleficence\nF. autonomy overrides justice\nG. nonmaleficence overrides autonomy\nH. justice overrides beneficence\nI. beneficence is equal to justice\nJ. beneficence overrides autonomy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The physician prioritizes preventing harm to the wife (nonmaleficence) over the patient\u2019s right to confidentiality (autonomy), which matches the principle that **nonmaleficence overrides autonomy** in this case.  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 263, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 315}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5338", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 49-year-old man, who is recovering in the hospital 2 days after uncomplicated left femoral-popliteal bypass grafting for claudication, has now developed increasing pain in his left foot. Until now, the patient's postoperative course had been unremarkable and he has been treated with low-dose morphine for pain control. Medical history is remarkable for type 2 diabetes mellitus controlled with metformin and diet. Vital signs now are temperature 36.8\u00b0C (98.2\u00b0F), pulse 80/min and regular, respirations 20/min, and blood pressure 150/92 mm Hg. The surgical incision appears clean and well approximated without abnormal erythema or swelling. The left lower extremity and foot appear pale. Palpation of the left lower extremity discloses a strong femoral pulse, a weak popliteal pulse, and a cool, pulseless foot. Which of the following is the most appropriate management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Intraoperative angiography\nB. Intravenous heparin therapy\nC. Immediate surgical exploration\nD. Initiate antibiotic therapy\nE. Computed Tomography (CT) of the lower extremity\nF. Intra-arterial tissue plasminogen activator (tPA) therapy\nG. Doppler ultrasonography of the left lower extremity\nH. Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) of the left lower extremity\nI. Bedside compartment pressure measurements\nJ. Pain management and observation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient has signs of acute limb ischemia (pale, cool, pulseless foot) after vascular bypass surgery, which suggests graft thrombosis or occlusion. This is a surgical emergency requiring immediate evaluation and likely revascularization. The most appropriate next step is immediate surgical exploration to assess and salvage the graft.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 402, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 489}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5346", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After being severely beaten and sustaining a gunshot wound to the abdomen, a 42-year-old woman undergoes resection of a perforated small bowel. During the operation, plastic reconstruction of facial fractures, and open reduction and internal fixation of the left femur are also done. Thirty-six hours postoperatively, she is awake but not completely alert. She is receiving intravenous morphine via a patient-controlled pump. She says that she needs the morphine to treat her pain, but she is worried that she is becoming addicted. She has no history of substance use disorder. She drinks one to two glasses of wine weekly. Which of the following initial actions by the physician is most appropriate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Advise her to drink more wine to help with the pain\nB. Maintain the morphine, but periodically administer intravenous naloxone\nC. Switch the patient to oral acetaminophen as soon as she can take medication orally\nD. Recommend a consultation with a psychiatrist to address her fears of addiction\nE. Suggest biofeedback therapy to control pain\nF. Switch the patient to intramuscular lorazepam\nG. Reassure the patient that her chance of becoming addicted to narcotics is minuscule\nH. Administer methadone as an alternative to morphine\nI. Increase the dose of morphine to relieve her anxiety\nJ. Encourage the patient to endure the pain without medication to prevent addiction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate initial action is to address her fear directly with education and reassurance, as her concern is a common barrier to adequate pain management in hospitalized patients.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 419, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 468}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5356", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about protein digestion and absorption is most correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The products of protein digestion may be absorbed as free amino acids or as di- or tripeptides\nB. Gastric digestion of all proteins is equally efficient because of the grinding action of the antrum\nC. Gastric zymogenic (chief) cells produce and secrete chymotrypsin, elastase and carboxypeptidase A and this initiates the process of protein digestion\nD. The products of digestion of dietary protein by luminal and brush-border enzymes are only absorbed by one of the 14 different amino acid transporters\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Answer:** A is correct because protein digestion yields free amino acids, dipeptides, and tripeptides, which are all absorbed via specific intestinal transporters.  \n\n**Explanation:**  \n- B is incorrect because gastric protein digestion efficiency varies with food type and grinding is mechanical, not enzymatic.  \n- C is incorrect because chymotrypsin, elastase, and carboxypeptidase are pancreatic enzymes, not secreted by gastric chief cells.  \n- D is incorrect because products of protein digestion are absorbed by multiple transporters, not just one.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 142, "total_tokens": 362}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5390", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 46-year-old woman, gravida 1, para 1, comes to the office because of a 2-week history of black discharge from her right nipple. The patient had mammography and ultrasonography of the breasts 2 months ago for evaluation of increased glandularity, palpated in the upper outer quadrant of the right breast, noted at her most recent annual examination. The studies showed likely benign findings with recommended follow-up in 6 months. Medical history is otherwise unremarkable and she takes no medications. BMI is 30 kg/m2 . Vital signs are normal. Palpation of the right breast discloses glandularity in the upper outer quadrant but no other masses. There is scant, black discharge from the right nipple. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in diagnosis?\n\nOptions: \nA. Core needle biopsy of the right breast\nB. Ductography\nC. Start on antifungal treatment\nD. Excisional biopsy of glandular tissue\nE. MRI of the right breast\nF. Fine needle aspiration of the right nipple discharge\nG. Mammography of the left breast\nH. Repeat ultrasonography of the right breast\nI. Histopathological study of the discharge\nJ. Repeat mammography\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate next step is **ductography** to evaluate the specific duct producing the discharge, especially since recent imaging showed likely benign findings.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 358, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 403}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5392", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 29-year-old Hispanic woman, gravida 3, para 3, comes to the office because of recurrent low back pain during the past year. Rest and analgesics usually eradicate the pain within 2 weeks. However, the pain seems to recur every 2 to 3 months. Medical history is remarkable for gestational diabetes mellitus during her pregnancies. She takes no medications except for an oral contraceptive. She walks 3 miles daily for exercise and works as a sales representative for a computer software company. She is 165 cm (5 ft 5 in) tall and weighs 100 kg (220 lb); BMI is 37 kg/m2 . Vital signs are normal, and physical examination discloses no abnormalities. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step?\n\nOptions: \nA. Refer for chiropractic treatment\nB. Order a CT scan of the lumbosacral spine\nC. Prescribe stronger painkillers\nD. Suggest a change in occupation\nE. Order x-rays of the lumbosacral spine\nF. Recommend beginning a weight loss program\nG. Order MRI of the lumbosacral spine\nH. Administer an epidural injection of methylprednisolone\nI. Recommend physical therapy\nJ. Recommend surgery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient\u2019s recurrent low back pain is most likely mechanical and related to obesity (BMI 37 kg/m\u00b2), with no red flags on exam. The most appropriate initial conservative management is addressing modifiable risk factors.  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 347, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 405}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5396", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 37-year-old Anglo-American man is admitted to the hospital for treatment for cocaine dependency. He says he has tried repeatedly to abstain from cocaine use but lives in a part of town where there are heavy drug sales. He did not like his hospital outpatient group but liked his single session at Cocaine Anonymous. Vital signs are temperature 37.0\u00b0C (98.6\u00b0F), pulse 70/min, respirations 16/min, and blood pressure 125/85 mm Hg. Physical examination shows a thin man with good muscle strength and no focal neurologic deficits. The patient is using insurance coverage through his wife but does not wish for his diagnosis to be disclosed to anyone. He is on probation after a conviction for aggravated robbery 3 years ago. There is also a warrant for his arrest for assault and battery. After listening to his requests and weighing your obligations, you should disclose this patient's diagnosis only to which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. His Cocaine Anonymous sponsor\nB. His wife\nC. The police, due to his outstanding warrant\nD. The hospital's patient advocacy group\nE. Insurance company\nF. His family doctor\nG. His probation officer\nH. No one, to respect his request for privacy\nI. His previous outpatient group counselor\nJ. His employer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **E. Insurance company**, because the patient\u2019s insurance is covering treatment, and necessary billing and treatment details can be disclosed to the insurer despite the patient\u2019s general request for privacy.  \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 328, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 377}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5525", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Select the single most accurate statement about the absorptive area of the human intestine?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The absorptive area is equivalent to that of a tennis court\nB. All of the options given are correct\nC. Changes in motility increase the contact time between nutrients and absorptive surface\nD. The presence of folds, villi and microvilli on the surface of enterocytes magnifies the absorptive area\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement about folds, villi, and microvilli magnifying the absorptive area is the most directly accurate and specific description among the options.  \nWhile the tennis court analogy is sometimes used, it is an approximation and not a precise anatomical fact.  \nTherefore, D is the best choice.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 173, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 250}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5544", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With respect to theories of senescence, it's probably safe to say that\n\nOptions: \nA. Programmed theories are the best we have at present\nB. Only one theory can accurately explain senescence\nC. All of these theories are merely speculation at this point\nD. All of these theories have been widely accepted by the scientific community\nE. Theories of senescence are being disproven at a rapid rate\nF. The evidence for these theories is insufficient and not compelling\nG. Many theories will have to be combined to explain senescence\nH. Senescence is not yet fully understood and cannot be explained by any theory\nI. Programmed theories are completely incorrect\nJ. The evidence for these theories is direct and quickly accumulating\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the current scientific understanding of aging, senescence is a complex process likely involving multiple mechanisms, so the most accurate statement is that **many theories will have to be combined to explain it**.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 253, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 311}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5565", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about absorption from the gastro-intestinal (GI) tract is most correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The absorption of glucose is associated with sodium uptake.\nB. Fructose is absorbed more rapidly than glucose.\nC. Galactose and fructose are absorbed by the same transporter at the brush border membrane.\nD. Most water absorption along the GI tract occurs in the colon.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most correct statement is **A**, because glucose absorption via SGLT1 at the brush border is coupled with sodium transport.  \n\nFructose is absorbed more slowly than glucose (B is false), galactose and fructose use different transporters (C is false), and most water absorption occurs in the small intestine, not the colon (D is false).  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 253}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_88", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which 18th century writer produced a famous book called 'The Wealth of Nations'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frederick Taylor\nB. Henry Mintzberg\nC. Adam Smith\nD. Dr Samuel Johnson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Adam Smith, an 18th-century Scottish economist and philosopher, authored *The Wealth of Nations* in 1776. The other options are not associated with that work.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_11", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Hawthorn Studies are most associated with which writer?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mary Parker Follett\nB. Elton Mayo\nC. Lillian Gilbreth\nD. Frederick Taylor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hawthorn Studies are most famously linked to **Elton Mayo**, who played a leading role in the experiments and their interpretation.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 135}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_6", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is a feature of McGregor's Theory X?\n\nOptions: \nA. Workers enjoy responsibility.\nB. Workers view physical and mental effort as a natural part of work.\nC. Workers like to show initiative.\nD. Workers like to be directed.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "McGregor's Theory X assumes that workers are inherently lazy, avoid responsibility, and prefer to be directed. Among the options, the statement that aligns with this view is that workers like to be directed.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 188}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_68", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is Frank Gilbreth`s work most noted for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Working conditions\nB. Time and motion studies\nC. Work psychology\nD. Work as a social setting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Frank Gilbreth is best known for pioneering time and motion studies to improve work efficiency. Among the options, this directly corresponds to \"Time and motion studies.\"  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_56", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does PEST stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Political, environmental, strategic, testing\nB. Political, environmental, strategic, technological\nC. Political, economic, strategic, technological\nD. Political, economic, social, technological\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "PEST is a common business analysis framework that stands for Political, Economic, Social, and Technological factors.  \nThis matches option D exactly.  \nThe other options incorrectly replace one of these core elements.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 130, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 187}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_36", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the purpose of a 'quality circle'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bring together managers and workers to find improvements.\nB. Bring together managers and workers to discuss output.\nC. Bring together managers and workers to review quality of work.\nD. Bring together managers and workers to review targets.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A quality circle is a group of employees who meet regularly to identify, analyze, and solve work-related problems, primarily focusing on **improvements** in quality, processes, and productivity. While reviewing quality (C) is part of it, the core purpose is proactive problem-solving for improvements, not just discussion or review.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 237}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_74", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: From what does a chain of command extend?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bottom to top\nB. Top to bottom\nC. Diagonally\nD. Laterally\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The chain of command refers to the formal line of authority within an organization, which typically flows from the highest level of management down to the lowest. This means it extends from top to bottom.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_92", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of what is advertising a form?\n\nOptions: \nA. Focusing strategy\nB. Differentiation\nC. Cost leadership\nD. Growth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Advertising is a form of **differentiation** because it is used to distinguish a product or brand from competitors in the market.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 129}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_98", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a whistleblower?\n\nOptions: \nA. Someone who reports illegal or unethical acts\nB. Someone who commits illegal or unethical acts\nC. Someone who benefits from illegal or unethical acts\nD. Someone who devises illegal or unethical acts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A whistleblower is typically defined as a person who exposes wrongdoing, such as illegal or unethical activities, within an organization.  \nAmong the options, this matches most closely with reporting such acts rather than committing, benefiting from, or devising them.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_5", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a Gantt chart a type of?\n\nOptions: \nA. Work flow design\nB. Work schedule design\nC. Work rate design\nD. Work output design\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A Gantt chart is a visual tool that displays tasks or activities against time, making it primarily a scheduling instrument. Among the options, it most directly represents a **work schedule design**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_95", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vertical integration forwards is when a firm mergers or acquires another\n\nOptions: \nA. Towards the source of supply\nB. Towards the consumer\nC. At the same stage of the supply chain\nD. In another industry\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Vertical integration forwards means moving closer to the end user, so the firm would be moving **towards the consumer**.\n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_99", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is T-group training?\n\nOptions: \nA. A group whose aim is transformational change\nB. A group brought together to deliver training programmes\nC. Team training for the purposes of advancing technology\nD. Team building activities involving learning\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "T-group training, also known as sensitivity training, focuses on interpersonal dynamics and personal growth through group interaction, which aligns with transformational change in individuals. Among the options, this best matches a group aimed at transformational change.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_32", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When does an acquisition take place?\n\nOptions: \nA. Two equal partners decide to work together.\nB. Two equal partners share resources.\nC. Two unequal partners join together.\nD. Two unequal partners become one after a buyout.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An acquisition typically involves one company purchasing another, resulting in two unequal partners becoming one after a buyout. This distinguishes it from mergers or partnerships where entities may combine as equals. Therefore, the best match among the options is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 197}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_18", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Belbin (1981) an extroverted and enthusiastic person fits with what role?\n\nOptions: \nA. Co-ordinator\nB. Shaper\nC. Resource investigator\nD. Implementer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on Belbin's team roles, an extroverted and enthusiastic person is best described as a **Resource Investigator**, as this role involves exploring opportunities and networking with others externally.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 166}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_57", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the acronym SMART stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Suitable, measurable, actionable, rewarded and timely\nB. Specific, measurable, actionable, resourced and timely\nC. Standardised, measurable, achievable, rewarded, and timely\nD. Specific, measurable, achievable, rewarded and timely\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most widely accepted definition of SMART in goal-setting is **Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, and Time-bound**, but since that exact phrase isn't an option, the closest match is \"Specific, measurable, achievable, rewarded and timely,\" which aligns with common variations despite \"rewarded\" being non-standard.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 196}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_63", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term used in Ansoff's matrix for increasing market share with existing products in existing markets?\n\nOptions: \nA. Product development\nB. Market penetration\nC. Diversification\nD. Market development\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on Ansoff's Matrix, the strategy for increasing market share with existing products in existing markets is **market penetration**.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 166}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_101", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not part of Schein's model of the formation of culture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Shared values\nB. Pre-conceptions\nC. Shared beliefs\nD. Norms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Schein's model of organizational culture consists of three levels: artifacts, espoused values, and basic underlying assumptions. \"Pre-conceptions\" is not one of the levels or core components in his widely recognized model. The other options (shared values, shared beliefs, and norms) align with elements of cultural models, but \"pre-conceptions\" is the term that does not fit.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 207}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_22", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To what does emotional intelligence refer?\n\nOptions: \nA. How people view and understand the world.\nB. How people view and understand themselves.\nC. How people view and understand others.\nD. How people view and understand themselves and others.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Emotional intelligence refers to the ability to perceive, understand, and manage one's own emotions as well as the emotions of others, which aligns with viewing and understanding both oneself and others.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 192}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_65", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the Five Factor model, 'extraversion' as a personality type is characterised by what type of people?\n\nOptions: \nA. Good natured\nB. Calm and self-confident\nC. Sensitive and curious\nD. Assertive and sociable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to the Five Factor model, extraversion is primarily characterized by traits such as being outgoing, energetic, and sociable. The option that best matches this description is \"assertive and sociable.\"  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_41", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the definition of a scenario in scenario planning?\n\nOptions: \nA. An imagined sequence of future events\nB. An unpredictable event\nC. A planned for event\nD. An unplanned for event\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An **imagined sequence of future events** is the standard definition of a scenario in scenario planning, as it involves constructing plausible stories about how the future might unfold to aid strategic thinking.  \n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_87", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Enhancement of job satisfaction and productivity are key characteristics of which theoretical perspective of work design?\n\nOptions: \nA. Process improvement\nB. Techno-structural change model\nC. Job characteristics model\nD. Socio-technical systems\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is the **job characteristics model**, which specifically focuses on how core job dimensions (like skill variety and autonomy) lead to psychological states that enhance job satisfaction and productivity.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_9", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who of the following is the industrial philanthropist?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frederick Taylor\nB. Seebohm Rowntree\nC. Henry Ford\nD. Max Weber\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Seebohm Rowntree was a British sociological researcher and chocolate manufacturer known for his studies on poverty and welfare, fitting the description of an industrial philanthropist.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_10", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Individualism as a guiding moral philosophy was advocated by which economist?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Kenneth Galbraith\nB. John Maynard Keynes\nC. Milton Friedman\nD. Alfred Marshall\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Milton Friedman was a strong advocate for individualism and free-market principles in economics. The other economists listed are not primarily known for championing individualism as a guiding moral philosophy.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_51", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are group norms?\n\nOptions: \nA. Modes of behaviour that are acceptable to and shared by group members\nB. Modes of behaviour that are shared by some members of the group\nC. Modes of behaviour that challenge group values and beliefs\nD. Modes of behaviour that are different of those of the other group members\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Group norms are the shared expectations and standards for behavior within a group, making option A the most accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 150, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_35", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the richest form of information?\n\nOptions: \nA. Telephone\nB. Face-to-face\nC. E-mail\nD. Video conference\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on communication theories like media richness theory, face-to-face interaction is considered the richest because it allows for immediate feedback, multiple cues (verbal and nonverbal), and personal focus.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_33", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who of these is the entrepreneur?\n\nOptions: \nA. Barack Obama\nB. James Dyson\nC. Damien Hirst\nD. Mo Farah\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "James Dyson is best known as the inventor and founder of Dyson Ltd., a company built on his innovations in vacuum cleaners and other technology, which fits the definition of an entrepreneur. The others are primarily known as a politician, an artist, and an athlete, respectively.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_42", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What assumption is the garbage can model of decision making based on?\n\nOptions: \nA. Limited knowledge and great insight\nB. Limited knowledge but high level of experience\nC. Limited knowledge and uncertainty\nD. Limited knowledge and high risk\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The garbage can model of decision making emphasizes that decisions often occur in environments of ambiguity and unclear processes, which aligns with conditions of **limited knowledge and uncertainty**.  \n\nAmong the options, this is directly stated in choice **C**.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 132, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_26", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was a major protagonist of utilitarianism?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Stuart Mill\nB. Thomas Hobbes\nC. Karl Marx\nD. Adam Smith\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Stuart Mill is the philosopher most directly associated with developing and advocating utilitarianism. While other thinkers contributed to moral and political philosophy, Mill is the classic proponent of this ethical theory.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_53", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term for the extent to which competition in one country is influenced by competition in other countries?\n\nOptions: \nA. International trade\nB. Global economics\nC. Global competition\nD. Globalisation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term refers to competition across borders affecting domestic markets, which is most directly captured by **global competition**.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_0", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term for a sub-optimal but acceptable outcome of negotiations between parties?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bargaining\nB. Satisficing\nC. Accepting\nD. Compromising\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term \"satisficing\" refers to choosing an option that meets a minimum threshold of acceptability rather than aiming for the optimal outcome, which fits the description in the question.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_60", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What one of these is not a recognised type of authority?\n\nOptions: \nA. Executive\nB. Functional\nC. Line management\nD. Supplier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for a type of authority that is **not** recognised.  \nIn organizational management, recognised authority types typically include line, staff, functional, and sometimes project authority.  \n\"Supplier\" is not a standard category of authority within an organization's internal structure.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_86", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is intuitive decision making based on?\n\nOptions: \nA. Guesswork\nB. Gambling\nC. Instinct\nD. Rationality\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Intuitive decision making relies on subconscious processes and gut feelings rather than deliberate analysis, which aligns most closely with instinct. While it is not purely guesswork or gambling, it also does not involve systematic rationality.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 144}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_58", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which writer was concerned with the reaction of workers to key characteristics of bureaucracies?\n\nOptions: \nA. Merton\nB. Weber\nC. Gouldner\nD. Mayo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A. Merton**, as he examined how bureaucratic structures can lead to unintended consequences like rigidity and ritualism among workers. Weber focused on defining bureaucracy itself, while Gouldner and Mayo studied different aspects of workplace dynamics. Merton\u2019s work specifically addressed worker adaptation to bureaucratic characteristics.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 216}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_72", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Workers' acceptance of change is characteristic of what type of culture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Team culture\nB. Collaborative culture\nC. Group culture\nD. Collective culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Workers' acceptance of change is most closely associated with a **collaborative culture**, which emphasizes adaptability, open communication, and shared problem-solving in response to change. While other options involve group dynamics, \"collaborative culture\" specifically highlights flexibility and receptiveness to change.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_27", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As what is ensuring that one individual does not carry the burden of a whole work task referred to?\n\nOptions: \nA. Work specialisation\nB. Work design\nC. Work schedule\nD. Work shift\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on common management and organizational behavior terminology, ensuring that work tasks are distributed rather than placed on one person relates to dividing labor into specific, specialized roles. This is a core concept known as **work specialization**.  \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **A**.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_40", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a succession plan?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dismissing an employee for a more favourable employee\nB. A formal process of planning to fill a role that will become vacant\nC. A vote of no confidence in a board member\nD. The formal process of acquiring a new staff member\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A succession plan is a proactive strategy to ensure continuity by preparing for future vacancies, which aligns with option B.  \nThe other options describe different HR or governance actions unrelated to succession planning.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_43", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By which principle is utilitarianism defined?\n\nOptions: \nA. Equality for everyone\nB. Maximisation of outcomes for individuals\nC. The best outcome for the majority of people\nD. The least worst outcome for everybody\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Utilitarianism is classically defined as aiming for the greatest good for the greatest number, which aligns with seeking the best outcome for the majority.  \n\nTherefore, the correct choice is:  \n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_2", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a normative perspective?\n\nOptions: \nA. The way things are.\nB. The way things are going to be.\nC. The way things should be.\nD. The way things were.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A normative perspective deals with values, ideals, or judgments about how things ought to be, rather than describing how things actually are. This matches the option stating \"The way things should be.\"  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_64", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is characteristic for the location of a virtual team?\n\nOptions: \nA. In the same building\nB. In the same industry\nC. In the same country\nD. remotely\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A virtual team is defined by members working together from different locations, typically not sharing the same physical workspace.  \nAmong the options, only \"remotely\" captures this essential characteristic of being geographically dispersed.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_38", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Profitability stemming from how well a firm positions itself in the market is a key feature of which writer's view on strategy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peter Drucker\nB. Jay Barney\nC. Michael Porter\nD. Henry Mintzberg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to profitability linked to market positioning, which is central to Michael Porter\u2019s competitive strategy framework. Porter emphasizes that strategy involves choosing a unique and valuable position derived from a set of activities.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 194}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_82", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To what time-frame do strategic plans relate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Long-term\nB. Medium-term\nC. Short-term\nD. Unspecified time it takes to achieve an aim\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Strategic plans typically involve setting long-term goals and directions for an organization, often looking several years into the future. This aligns with long-term planning rather than medium-term, short-term, or unspecified durations.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_77", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term Tuckman uses for reaching consensus as a group?\n\nOptions: \nA. Storming\nB. Performing\nC. Forming\nD. Norming\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct stage in Tuckman\u2019s model for when a group reaches consensus and establishes cohesion is **Norming**.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_16", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a paradigm?\n\nOptions: \nA. A theoretical assumption\nB. An illustration\nC. A theoretical model\nD. An example serving as a model\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A paradigm is best understood as a broad theoretical framework or model that guides thinking in a field. While it can include examples or illustrations, its core meaning aligns with a foundational model.  \n\nCorrect choice: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 163}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_90", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what order do managers typically perform the managerial functions?\n\nOptions: \nA. organising, planning, controlling, leading\nB. organising, leading, planning, controlling\nC. planning, organising, leading, controlling\nD. planning, organising, controlling, leading\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct order is planning first, then organizing, then leading, and finally controlling, which matches the classic management sequence.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 179}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_30", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one is not an element in the primary activities of a value chain?\n\nOptions: \nA. Procurement\nB. Inbound logistics\nC. Outbound logistics\nD. Service\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**A. Procurement** is not part of the primary activities in Porter\u2019s value chain model; it is a support activity.  \nThe primary activities are inbound logistics, operations, outbound logistics, marketing & sales, and service.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_102", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not one of the layers of cultural influence?\n\nOptions: \nA. Social\nB. Business\nC. Organisational\nD. Company\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Business** is not typically considered a distinct layer in models of cultural influence, which more commonly address national, organizational, and subcultural (including social/group) levels.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_31", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term for the act of getting individuals to behave in ways that are acceptable to a group?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indoctrination\nB. Brainwashing\nC. Propaganda\nD. Socialisation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term that describes the process of learning acceptable group behaviors is **socialisation**, as it involves acquiring the norms and values of a society.  \nIndoctrination, brainwashing, and propaganda are more associated with imposing specific beliefs rather than general behavioral adaptation.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_80", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a definition of an objective?\n\nOptions: \nA. A defined specified outcome to be achieved in the long-term\nB. A clear set of goals to be attained given a set number of resources\nC. A clearly defined and measurable outcome to be achieved over a specified timeframe\nD. A set standard of performance agreed by workers and managers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most precise definition among the options is **C**, as it emphasizes that an objective should be both clearly defined and measurable within a specific timeframe.  \nWhile the other choices touch on related concepts like long-term outcomes or agreed standards, they lack the explicit emphasis on measurability and timeframe that characterizes a well-formed objective.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 207}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_50", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a strategic alliance?\n\nOptions: \nA. Any form of partnership between one firm and another\nB. Formal agreement committing two or more firms to exchange resources to produce products or services\nC. Formal agreement to share profits from a shared investment\nD. Formal agreement to share knowledge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A strategic alliance is best described as a formal agreement between firms to exchange resources for joint production or service provision, which aligns most closely with option B.  \n\nThe other options are either too broad (A) or too narrow (C and D) to capture the core idea of a strategic alliance.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 147, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 228}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_73", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a virtual organisation?\n\nOptions: \nA. An organisation that uses information and communications technologies (ICT's) to coordinate activities without physical boundaries between different functions\nB. An organisation that uses internet technologies to sell products to customers\nC. An organisation that manages the supply chain using digital technologies\nD. An organisation that coordinates the workforce via video conferencing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A virtual organization primarily relies on ICTs to coordinate activities across functions without being constrained by physical boundaries, which aligns most closely with option A.  \nWhile the other options describe specific uses of technology, they are narrower aspects rather than the core definition.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 191, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 273}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_8", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which writer is most associated with bureaucratic structures?\n\nOptions: \nA. Henry Fayol\nB. Max Weber\nC. Adam Smith\nD. Mary Parker Follett\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Max Weber is widely known for his theory of bureaucracy, which describes the ideal characteristics of rational-legal authority and hierarchical structures in organizations. While other thinkers contributed to management theory, Weber\u2019s work is most directly linked to bureaucratic systems.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 154}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_47", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who of the following is a leading writer on contingency theory of leadership?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rosabeth Kanter\nB. Joan Woodward\nC. Rensis Likert\nD. Fred Fiedler\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Fred Fiedler is the scholar most associated with the contingency theory of leadership, which matches option D.  \nThe other theorists are known for different contributions: Kanter for organizational change, Woodward for technology and structure, and Likert for management systems.  \nTherefore, the correct answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_12", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How can you describe the thinking and outlook of transformational leaders?\n\nOptions: \nA. Strategic\nB. Operational\nC. Functional\nD. Developmental\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Transformational leaders focus on inspiring change, long-term vision, and growth, which aligns most closely with a **strategic** and **developmental** outlook. However, among the given options, \"Strategic\" best captures their forward-thinking and big-picture orientation.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_23", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of what is individual freedom to schedule work an example?\n\nOptions: \nA. Job design\nB. Job enrichment\nC. Job rate\nD. Job planning\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Individual freedom to schedule work is typically a part of **job design**, as it involves structuring work to increase autonomy and flexibility for the employee.  \nWhile it can be an element of job enrichment, job enrichment is a specific method under the broader category of job design.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_28", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How do you describe a work group that comprises workers with demarcated tasks and distant line managers?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dependent\nB. Independent\nC. Interdependent\nD. Collaborative\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description of workers with demarcated tasks and distant managers suggests they operate largely on their own without close coordination, which aligns with an **independent** work group.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_39", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Functional structures help to create\u0085...\n\nOptions: \nA. teamwork\nB. specialisation\nC. project work groups\nD. multi-skilled employees\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Functional structures organize a company by departments based on specialized roles, which promotes expertise in specific areas.  \nAmong the options, this aligns most directly with creating **specialisation**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_81", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not a purpose of an organisational structure?\n\nOptions: \nA. To coordinate people and resources\nB. To organise lines of communication\nC. To formalise authority\nD. To limit workers' rights\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The purpose of an organizational structure is to define roles, coordination, and authority, not to restrict workers' rights, which is more a legal or policy matter. Options A, B, and C are typical functions of organizational structure, while D is not a standard or intended purpose.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 172}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_85", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does situational theory of leadership emphasise?\n\nOptions: \nA. Personality traits\nB. Events\nC. Environment\nD. Political situation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Situational theory of leadership emphasizes that effective leadership depends on the specific environment or context in which it is exercised. Among the options, \"Environment\" best captures this focus on adapting to varying circumstances.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_89", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of these characteristics is most commonly associated with the 'rational goal' model of management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Worker welfare\nB. Health and safety\nC. Interpersonal relationships\nD. Productivity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The rational goal model of management emphasizes clear objectives, efficiency, and output, making productivity its central focus. Worker welfare, health and safety, and interpersonal relationships are more closely associated with other management models (such as human relations or internal process models).  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 203}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_91", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does lateral communication in an organisation occur?\n\nOptions: \nA. Information passes upwards.\nB. Information passes downwards.\nC. Information is a two-way process.\nD. Information passes between different departments and functions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lateral communication refers to the exchange of information between peers or units at the same hierarchical level, such as across different departments.  \nAmong the options, this is best described as information passing between different departments and functions.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_94", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of what is worker autonomy in decision making an example?\n\nOptions: \nA. Worker freedom\nB. Greater worker negotiation\nC. Worker empowerment\nD. Increased worker power\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Worker autonomy in decision making is a key aspect of **worker empowerment**, as it involves granting employees the authority and responsibility to make choices about their work. While the other options are related, empowerment directly encompasses the concept of autonomy.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_14", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an assumption underpinning the rational decision making model?\n\nOptions: \nA. Incomplete information\nB. An agreed goal\nC. A structured problem\nD. High level of certainty regarding the environment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The rational decision-making model assumes full information, clear goals, a structured problem, and certainty about outcomes.  \nTherefore, **incomplete information** is not an assumption of the model.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_17", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What one of the following is not a key management skill in planning?\n\nOptions: \nA. Conceptual skills\nB. Analytical skills\nC. IT and computing skills\nD. Communication skills\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "IT and computing skills are not inherently essential for the planning function in management, whereas conceptual, analytical, and communication skills are directly involved in setting goals and developing plans.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_25", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is not a characteristic of corporate social responsibility?\n\nOptions: \nA. Product safety\nB. Consumer rights\nC. Environmental policies\nD. Price-fixing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**D. Price-fixing** is not a characteristic of corporate social responsibility, as it is an illegal anticompetitive practice rather than an ethical responsibility. CSR focuses on ethical obligations such as product safety, consumer rights, and environmental stewardship.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_34", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not an advantage of a virtual team?\n\nOptions: \nA. Team members can be recruited for their specific skills or experience.\nB. No overhead costs associated with physical buildings.\nC. Conflict can be resolved easily using face-to-face meetings.\nD. Low transport or commuting costs.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The option that is **not** an advantage of a virtual team is C, because virtual teams typically do not meet in person regularly, making face-to-face conflict resolution difficult and contrary to the nature of such teams.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 204}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_46", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What type of organisational culture is most likely to deliver stability and efficiency?\n\nOptions: \nA. Task culture\nB. Role culture\nC. Power culture\nD. People culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A role culture emphasizes clear structures, defined responsibilities, and standardized procedures, which are key for achieving stability and efficiency in an organization.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_49", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an advantage of a hierarchical structure?\n\nOptions: \nA. Clear chain of command\nB. Quick response to change\nC. Discipline and stability\nD. Small span of control\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The hierarchical structure is known for its clear reporting lines and stability, but it tends to be rigid and slow to adapt. Quick response to change is typically a disadvantage, not an advantage, of this structure.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_61", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is not a characteristic of a team?\n\nOptions: \nA. Minimal and formal knowledge sharing\nB. Collective output\nC. Individual and collective responsibility\nD. Fluid dimension to roles and tasks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The characteristic that is **not** typical of a team is **minimal and formal knowledge sharing**, because effective teams usually rely on open communication and collaboration.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_93", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not a component of an agile organisation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Market focus and position\nB. Human resources: multi-skilling\nC. Organisational structure\nD. Project-based culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The component that is **not** typically considered a core part of an agile organization is **A. Market focus and position**, because while important, it is more of a strategic outcome rather than a structural or cultural component of agility itself. Agile organizations are characterized by flexible structures, cross-functional teams, and adaptive cultures.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 176}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_97", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not a characteristic of a corporate social responsibility framework?\n\nOptions: \nA. Retaining the status quo\nB. Understanding society\nC. Harnessing diversity\nD. Building capacity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The characteristic that does not fit a corporate social responsibility (CSR) framework is **retaining the status quo**, as CSR typically involves proactive efforts to improve social and environmental outcomes rather than maintaining existing conditions.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_4", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following political leaders could not be termed a 'transformational' leader?\n\nOptions: \nA. Margaret Thatcher\nB. Mikhail Gorbachov\nC. Nelson Mandela\nD. Bill Clinton\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "While all were significant leaders, Bill Clinton is generally not classified as a \"transformational\" leader in the same sense as the others, who fundamentally reshaped their nations' political systems or ideologies. Thatcher, Gorbachev, and Mandela each led profound systemic transformations, whereas Clinton's presidency is more often seen as pragmatic and incremental.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 212}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_21", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not part of the recognised challenges for modern managers?\n\nOptions: \nA. Micro-managing the workforce\nB. Managing communications\nC. Managing change\nD. Managing the learning organisation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**A. Micro-managing the workforce** is not a recognised challenge for modern managers; it is generally considered a poor management practice rather a key challenge like the others listed.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_management_59", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the optimal span of control?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. 5\nC. 7\nD. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The optimal span of control is not a fixed number, as it depends on factors like task complexity, employee experience, and organizational structure.  \nTherefore, no single number universally applies in all management situations.  \nThe best answer is that it varies, which aligns with \u201cNone of the above.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1494", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Object permanence seen in which stage of Jean Piaget\u2019s theory\n\nOptions: \nA. Sensorimotor\nB. Pre-operational stage\nC. Concrete operations stage\nD. Formal operations stage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Object permanence is the understanding that objects continue to exist even when they cannot be seen, heard, or touched. According to Piaget\u2019s theory, this cognitive milestone develops during the **sensorimotor stage** (birth to about 2 years).\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2273", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increased calories required during pregnancy:September 2012\n\nOptions: \nA. 300\nB. 400\nC. 550\nD. 800\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The recommended increase in daily caloric intake during pregnancy is typically around 300 extra calories, especially in the second and third trimesters.  \nThis is a standard guideline in maternal nutrition.  \nThus, the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_195", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Fourth generation apex locater based on\n\nOptions: \nA. Resistance\nB. lmpedence\nC. Frequency\nD. Multiple frequency ratio\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Fourth-generation apex locators use multiple frequencies to determine the position of the apical foramen, making the **multiple frequency ratio** method the correct basis.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_695", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Kroll designed\n\nOptions: \nA. RPI clasp\nB. Bar clasp\nC. Circumferential clasp\nD. Altered clasp\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Kroll designed the **RPI clasp** (rest, proximal plate, and I-bar), which is a specific type of clasp assembly used in removable partial dentures.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 139}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_182", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Freedom of centric relation correlates with\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.15 - 1.5 mm\nB. 0.20 - 0.40 mm\nC. 0.5 to 1.5 mm\nD. 1 to 2 mmm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The typical range for freedom in centric relation is about 0.5 to 1.5 mm, which matches option C.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2643", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Creep rate decreases with:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase force of condensation\nB. Decrease force of condensation\nC. Under or overtrituration\nD. Dealy in time between trituration and condensation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because delaying the time between trituration and condensation allows the material to set partially, reducing its flow (creep) under load.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_335", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Production and citation impact of published work of a scientist or scholar\n\nOptions: \nA. Impact factor\nB. Citation\nC. H index\nD. Z index\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The **h-index** is a metric that combines both the productivity (number of publications) and citation impact of a researcher's work.  \nThe other options measure different aspects: impact factor is for journals, citation is a single count, and the z-index is less common.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 180}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_693", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Natural disaster causing maximum deaths\n\nOptions: \nA. Hydrological\nB. Meterological\nC. Geological\nD. Fires\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on global historical data, hydrological disasters (such as floods and tsunamis) have generally caused the greatest number of deaths over time, particularly due to major flood events in densely populated regions. While meteorological disasters (like storms) are frequent, and geological disasters (like earthquakes) can be highly deadly in single events, the cumulative death toll from floods is typically highest.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2755", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Guiding planes help in:\n\nOptions: \nA. For better clasp prediction\nB. Vertical to occlusal plane\nC. Balanced occlusion\nD. Avoid precision attachment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Guiding planes help in aligning the path of insertion and removal for a dental prosthesis, which aids in proper clasp positioning and retention. Among the options, this function is most directly related to improving clasp prediction and stability.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2180", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Amount of heat that is required to change boiling water into vapor is referred to as\n\nOptions: \nA. Latent Heat of vaporization\nB. Latent Heat of sublimation\nC. Latent Heat of condensation\nD. Latent heat of fusion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The heat required to change boiling water into vapor is specifically the **latent heat of vaporization**, which is the energy needed for a phase change from liquid to gas at the boiling point.  \nThe other options refer to different phase changes: sublimation (solid to gas), condensation (gas to liquid), and fusion (solid to liquid).  \nTherefore, the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 202}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1201", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: causes of thyroid storm\n\nOptions: \nA. ineffective pre-operative hormonal control\nB. manhandling of the thyroid gland during surgery\nC. parathyroid tail left after surgery\nD. Poor Preoperative preparation of the patient\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "All options can contribute to thyroid storm, but the most direct and classic cause among these is **poor preoperative preparation of the patient**, which includes inadequate control of thyroid hormone levels before surgery.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2135", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rotation speed of profile instruments\n\nOptions: \nA. 50-100 RPM\nB. 100-3000 RPM\nC. 300-500 RPM\nD. 150-300 RPM\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The typical rotation speed for profile instruments (like those used in soil or rock profiling) is in the low to moderate range, often between 150 and 300 RPM for consistent measurement without excessive disturbance.  \nComparing the options, 150\u2013300 RPM is a common specification for such equipment.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 176}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1870", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a non-diabetic high risk pregnancy the ideal time for non stress test monitoring is:\n\nOptions: \nA. 48 hrs\nB. 72 hrs\nC. 96 hrs\nD. 24 hrs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In high-risk pregnancies, nonstress tests (NSTs) are commonly performed at least twice weekly, typically with intervals of 2\u20133 days. A 48-hour interval aligns with standard obstetric practice for high-risk antenatal surveillance in a non-diabetic patient.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1027", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Light transmitting wedges transmit:\n\nOptions: \nA. 70-80% of incident light\nB. 80-85% of incident light\nC. 85-90% of incident light\nD. 90-95% of incident light\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Light transmitting wedges are typically designed for high optical efficiency in applications like photometry or colorimetry, where minimal light loss is important.  \nThe most common transmission range cited for such precision optical components is 90\u201395% of incident light.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2607", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Millennium development goal was adopted in which year?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1977\nB. 2000\nC. 1984\nD. 2004\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Millennium Development Goals were adopted by the United Nations in 2000.  \nThis matches option B.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 28, "total_tokens": 124}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1866", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \u03b2-oxidation of odd-chain fatty acids produce:\n\nOptions: \nA. Succinyl CoA\nB. Propionyl CoA\nC. Acetyl CoA\nD. Malonyl CoA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\u03b2-oxidation of odd-chain fatty acids yields acetyl-CoA in each cycle until the final three-carbon unit remains, which is **propionyl-CoA**.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 145}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1631", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Improved marginal adaptation in a composite restoration can be achieved by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Moisture free environment\nB. Application of pressure\nC. Acid etching\nD. Continued packing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **C. Acid etching**, as it creates micromechanical retention and improves the seal at the composite-tooth interface. Moisture control and pressure application are important but do not directly enhance marginal adaptation in the same fundamental way. Continued packing helps with contour but not primarily with marginal adaptation.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 172}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_570", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to 2011 census, life expectancy at birth for male and female is\n\nOptions: \nA. 67 and 70\nB. 70 and 67\nC. 61 and 69\nD. 69 and 61\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the 2011 Census of India, the life expectancy at birth for males was about 67 years and for females about 70 years. This matches the figures given in option A.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 163}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_760", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Key indicator for AFP surveillance ?.\n\nOptions: \nA. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 1000 population of under 5 years\nB. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 100000 population of under 5 year\nC. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 1000 population of under 15 years\nD. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 100000 population of under 15 years\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct indicator for AFP (acute flaccid paralysis) surveillance is based on detecting at least one case per year per 100,000 population in children under 15 years old, as this is the standard benchmark used by the World Health Organization for polio surveillance.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 169, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 241}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_861", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bakers anchorage is a type of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Intramaxillary anchorage\nB. Intermaxillary anchorage\nC. Extraoral anchorage\nD. Muscular anchorage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Baker's anchorage is a type of extraoral anchorage used in orthodontics, involving forces applied from outside the mouth, such as headgear.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2580", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Least complication in outlet forceps is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Complete perinea! tear\nB. Vulval hematoma\nC. Extension of episiotomy\nD. Cervical tear\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on typical obstetric data, the least common complication among these options following outlet forceps delivery is **cervical tear**, as outlet forceps are applied when the head is on the perineum, minimizing cervical trauma.  \nIn contrast, perineal tears, vulval hematoma, and episiotomy extensions are more directly associated with the perineal and vulval area where the forceps are applied.  \nTherefore, cervical tear is the least likely complication in this specific setting.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 126, "total_tokens": 233}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2491", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Exact number of weeks between last menstrual period and expected date of delivery :March 2005\n\nOptions: \nA. 38 weeks\nB. 39 weeks\nC. 40 weeks\nD. 41 weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The typical duration of pregnancy from the last menstrual period to the expected date of delivery is 40 weeks. This is the standard used in obstetrics for calculating due dates. Therefore, the most likely correct answer is 40 weeks.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_104", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Guiding planes are:\n\nOptions: \nA. Located adjacent to the edentulous area\nB. Located far anterior to the edentulous area\nC. Helps in the stability of the denture\nD. Provides a different path of insertion and removal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Guiding planes are vertical surfaces on abutment teeth that are prepared to be parallel to each other, helping to control the path of insertion and removal of a removable partial denture. Among the options, the one that directly describes this function is that they **provide a different path of insertion and removal**, though more precisely they provide a *consistent* path.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 199}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1481", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Maximum thermic effect of food is seen with\n\nOptions: \nA. Carbohydrates\nB. Protein\nC. Fat\nD. Not dependent on macronutrients\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The thermic effect of food is highest for protein because it requires more energy for digestion, absorption, and metabolism compared to carbohydrates or fats.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_340", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pickling is done:\n\nOptions: \nA. To remove oxide film from casting\nB. Polish the casting\nC. Improve the strength of casting\nD. Avoid casting defects\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Pickling is a chemical cleaning process used to remove oxides, scale, and contaminants from metal surfaces, including castings. Among the options, the most direct purpose is to remove oxide films formed during heating or processing.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 175}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_279", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For how long should NiTi files be submerged in NaOCl at 122-degree F to prevent damage to file corrosion\n\nOptions: \nA. 20 mins\nB. 45 mins\nC. 60 mins\nD. 2 hours\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The recommended time to prevent corrosion of NiTi files in heated NaOCl is generally limited to 20 minutes. Longer exposure increases the risk of corrosion and weakening.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2170", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: COPRA came into action on:\n\nOptions: \nA. 15th April 1987\nB. 15th April 1989\nC. 25th April 1988\nD. 15th April 1986\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Consumer Protection Act (COPRA) was enacted in 1986 and came into force on **15 April 1987**.  \nThat matches option A.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2718", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lithium should be stopped how many days before anaesthesia\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 day\nB. 2 days\nC. 3 days\nD. 4 days\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lithium is typically discontinued 24\u201348 hours before anesthesia to reduce the risk of perioperative complications such as toxicity or interactions. Among the given options, 2 days (48 hours) is the most commonly recommended timeframe.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1643", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: IPC section dealing with illegal aboion with woman consent?\n\nOptions: \nA. 310\nB. 312\nC. 313\nD. 314\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct IPC section for causing miscarriage with the woman's consent is **Section 312**, which deals with \"causing miscarriage\" voluntarily.  \nSection 313 covers miscarriage without consent, and Section 314 deals with death caused by an act done with intent to cause miscarriage.  \nThus, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2001", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Weber-Fechner law related to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Number of nerve Fibers\nB. Number of muscle Fibers\nC. Number of stimulus\nD. Intensity of stimulus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Weber\u2013Fechner law describes the relationship between the physical intensity of a stimulus and its perceived intensity, specifically stating that perception increases logarithmically with stimulus intensity.  \nTherefore, it is directly related to the **intensity of stimulus**.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 180}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2581", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: IQ range 90-109 is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Superior.\nB. Average.\nC. Low average.\nD. Borderline.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The IQ range 90\u2013109 is classified as average intelligence in most standard IQ classifications, such as the Wechsler scales.  \nThis range represents the middle of the distribution where the majority of the population falls.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2160", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sodium nitroprusside is metabolized to form an active metabolite. This active metabolized to form an active metabolite. This active metabolite of sodium nitroprusside act activation of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Phospholipase A\nB. Phospholipase C\nC. Guanylate cyclase\nD. Protein Kinase C\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The active metabolite of sodium nitroprusside is nitric oxide (NO), which activates guanylate cyclase, leading to increased cGMP and vasodilation.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 180}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_373", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sonic frequency range is:\n\nOptions: \nA. 1000-2000 Hz\nB. 1500-6000 Hz\nC. 20,000-30,000 Hz\nD. 10,000 Hz\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sonic frequency range refers to the range of human hearing, which is typically 20 Hz to 20,000 Hz. Among the given options, none exactly match the full range, but the closest to covering part of the upper end of human hearing is **10,000 Hz**, which falls within it. The other options are either too narrow or correspond to ultrasonic ranges (above 20,000 Hz).\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2303", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Split impedence based apex locator is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Generation 1\nB. Generation 2\nC. Generation 3\nD. Generation 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Split impedance-based apex locators are considered the first type of electronic apex locators developed, which places them in Generation 1.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_504", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treatment of choice in childhood thyrotoxicosis :\n\nOptions: \nA. Radio Iodine\nB. Lugols Iodine\nC. Carbimazole\nD. Surgery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The treatment of choice for childhood thyrotoxicosis is typically antithyroid drugs like carbimazole, as radioactive iodine and surgery are usually avoided in children due to safety concerns and Lugol's iodine is only for short-term preoperative use.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2040", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Epidemiological surveillance is defined as\n\nOptions: \nA. Active surveillance\nB. passive surveillance\nC. Sentinel surveillance\nD. Epidemiological surveillance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for the definition of \u201cepidemiological surveillance,\u201d and among the options, \u201cepidemiological surveillance\u201d is the broad, encompassing term for the ongoing systematic collection and analysis of health data. The other choices (A, B, C) are specific types or methods of surveillance.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 192}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1231", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Marker appearing last in MI\n\nOptions: \nA. LDH\nB. CPK-MB\nC. Troponin T\nD. Troponin I\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The marker that appears last in myocardial infarction (MI) is Troponin I, as it remains elevated the longest after an MI compared to the other options.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 139}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_211", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Long term assessment of glucose control can be made by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Estimation of post prandial blood sugar\nB. Estimation of fasting blood sugar\nC. Estimation of urine sugar level\nD. Estimation of blood level of glycosylated hemoglobin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because glycosylated hemoglobin (HbA1c) reflects average blood glucose levels over the previous 2\u20133 months, making it the standard for long-term glucose control assessment.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1375", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Green Vermillion index measures\n\nOptions: \nA. Periodontal disease\nB. Oral hygiene\nC. Bone level\nD. Gingival health\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Green Vermillion index measures oral hygiene, specifically assessing the presence of debris and calculus. It is not primarily focused on periodontal disease, bone level, or gingival health alone.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_567", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Average daily dose of vitamin-C is:\n\nOptions: \nA. 30 - 40 mg\nB. 50 - 60 mg\nC. 60 - 100 mg\nD. 100 - 150 mg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The recommended daily allowance for vitamin C is generally 75\u201390 mg for adults, making 60\u2013100 mg the most accurate range among the options.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 146}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2346", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Olympian brown and rhagdes are seen in-\n\nOptions: \nA. CMV inclusion disease\nB. Ectodermal dysplasia\nC. Congenital syphilis\nD. Hyper IgE syndrome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The terms \"Olympian brown\" and \"rhagades\" are classic signs of congenital syphilis, with rhagades referring to fissures around the mouth and Olympian brown describing a characteristic skin discoloration.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1582", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When a person lies down :\n\nOptions: \nA. There is immediate increase in venous return\nB. Heart rate becomes stable at slightly more than normal\nC. Cerebral blood flow increases & becomes stable at more than normal\nD. Blood flow to the Apex of lung decreases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When a person lies down, gravity no longer pulls blood downward, so venous return initially increases. This leads to a transient rise in cardiac output, but heart rate typically decreases slightly due to baroreceptor reflexes, not increase.  \n\nThe most likely correct answer is **A**, as the immediate effect is an increase in venous return.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 224}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_853", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Physical sign of severe aortic stenosis is:\n\nOptions: \nA. A late peaking holosystolic murmur\nB. A delayed carotid upstroke\nC. A diastolic rumble\nD. An opening snap\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Answer:** B  \n\n**Explanation:** Severe aortic stenosis classically presents with a **delayed carotid upstroke** (pulsus parvus et tardus). A late-peaking systolic murmur is typical, but it is not \"holosystolic\" (that describes mitral regurgitation), and an opening snap or diastolic rumble are features of mitral valve disease, not aortic stenosis.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 188}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2004", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Schielder principle is\n\nOptions: \nA. Minimal enlarged apical foramen\nB. Shape of the canal can be changed\nC. Use of 3-5 times larger than first binding file\nD. Original canal curvature should be altered to make it compatible with obturating material\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Answer:** The correct choice is **A**, as the Schilder principle refers to preparing the apical foramen to its minimal enlarged size while maintaining the natural shape of the canal.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_353", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pickling:\n\nOptions: \nA. Is accomplished by soaking the casting in baking soda\nB. Causes porosity in gold\nC. Removes surface oxides from gold castings\nD. Remove investment from gold casting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Pickling is a process used in jewelry making to clean metal surfaces, especially after casting. It typically involves using a warm acid solution to remove oxides and flux residue from the surface of the metal, such as gold castings.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2546", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Force generated by 90\u00b0 rotation of finger spring in pendulum appliance with distalisation:\n\nOptions: \nA. 75 gms\nB. 125 gms\nC. 150 gms\nD. 200 gms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The pendulum appliance typically generates about 150\u202fg of force when the finger spring is rotated 90\u00b0 for distalization.  \nThis is a standard value in orthodontic mechanics for molar distalization with this appliance.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_225", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Renal feed for CKD patients-\n\nOptions: \nA. Low calorie low volume\nB. Low calorie high volume\nC. High calorie low volume\nD. High calorie high volume\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For patients with chronic kidney disease (CKD), nutritional management often focuses on providing adequate energy (calories) while restricting fluid and certain electrolytes, which typically means a **high-calorie, low-volume** diet to prevent malnutrition and fluid overload.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2366", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is under-5 moality' rate in world by 2010?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6 million\nB. 8 million\nC. 10 million\nD. 12 million\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question appears to refer to the **number of under\u20115 deaths per year worldwide around 2010**, not a rate expressed as a percentage.  \nAccording to UNICEF and WHO estimates, the annual number of under\u20115 deaths in 2010 was roughly **8 million**.  \nThus, the best match among the options is **8 million**.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 179}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1815", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Drugs causing hyperglycemia:\n\nOptions: \nA. \u03b2-blocker\nB. Glucocorticoids\nC. Acetylcholine\nD. \u03b1-blockers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B. Glucocorticoids**, as they increase blood glucose by promoting gluconeogenesis and reducing insulin sensitivity.  \nWhile some \u03b2-blockers can also impair glucose metabolism, glucocorticoids are a more classic and potent cause of drug-induced hyperglycemia.  \nAcetylcholine and \u03b1-blockers are not typically associated with hyperglycemia.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2193", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Largest Faciolingual dimension is seen in\n\nOptions: \nA. Lower 1st molar\nB. Upper 1st molar\nC. Lower 2nd molar\nD. Upper 2nd molar\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The largest faciolingual dimension is typically found in the **upper first molar** due to its prominent mesiobuccal and distobuccal cusps. Among the options, this corresponds to choice B. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_625", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In CPITN index zero score means:\n\nOptions: \nA. Gingival bleeding\nB. Grade 1 mobility of teeth\nC. Healthy tooth\nD. Spontaneous bleeding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The CPITN index score of zero indicates no signs of periodontal disease, which corresponds to a healthy tooth.  \nAmong the options, this matches \"Healthy tooth.\"  \nTherefore, the correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_547", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Function of WHO collaborating centers:\n\nOptions: \nA. Collection, collation and dissemination of information\nB. Functioning and forming new guidelines/definitions for diseases\nC. Contact with grass root workers\nD. Collaborate information mainly\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because WHO collaborating centers primarily serve as reference hubs for data and information exchange.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 136}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2417", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Frankfort - horizontal is a reference plane constructed by joining which of the following landmarks?\n\nOptions: \nA. Nasion and Sella\nB. Porion and Sella\nC. Porion and Nasion\nD. Porion and Orbitale\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Frankfort horizontal plane is defined by connecting the porion (upper margin of the external auditory meatus) and the orbitale (lowest point of the orbital margin).  \nAmong the options, this corresponds to **Porion and Orbitale**.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1059", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The strength of a gypsum investment is dependent\non:\n\nOptions: \nA. Carbon content\nB. Silica content\nC. Gypsum\nD. Copper\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The strength of gypsum investment materials used in dentistry primarily comes from the gypsum binder, which hardens through a hydration reaction. The other components like silica modify properties but do not provide the fundamental strength.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1031", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Anchorage not being applied here:\n\nOptions: \nA. Reciprocal\nB. Stationary\nC. Intramaxillary\nD. Intraoral\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Answer:**  \nThe likely correct choice is **B. Stationary** because \"stationary anchorage\" is not a recognized anchorage classification in orthodontics; the other terms are standard types of dental anchorage.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1847", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Father of statistics\n\nOptions: \nA. John Snow\nB. John Graunt\nC. MacMahon\nD. John M. Last\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The title \"Father of Statistics\" is most commonly attributed to **John Graunt** for his early work in demography and statistical analysis in the 17th century. While others contributed significantly, Graunt is widely recognized as a foundational figure.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_189", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ashley-Howe model analysis is used to predict:\n\nOptions: \nA. Tooth material excess\nB. Maxillo-mandibular relationships\nC. Basal bone-transverse relationship\nD. Growth prediction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Ashley-Howe model analysis is used to predict tooth material excess relative to supporting bone structure. This aligns with option A.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_295", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Shelf life of colourless, aqueous solution of suxamethonium is\n\nOptions: \nA. 6 months\nB. 1 year\nC. 2 yr\nD. 3 yr\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The shelf life of a colorless, aqueous solution of suxamethonium is relatively short due to its instability in water, typically ranging from a few months to about a year under refrigeration. Among the given options, **1 year** is the most commonly cited shelf life when stored properly.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1253", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nutra sweet is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Saccharin.\nB. Aspartame.\nC. Xylitol.\nD. Sorbitol.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "NutraSweet is a brand name for the artificial sweetener aspartame.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 116}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1498", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Enzyme regulating the conversion of ethanol to acetaldehyde:\n\nOptions: \nA. Alcohol dehydrogenase\nB. Acetaldehyde dehydrogenase\nC. Catalase\nD. Enolase\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The enzyme that converts ethanol to acetaldehyde is alcohol dehydrogenase.  \nThe other enzymes listed either act on different substrates or catalyze later steps.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1321", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 4th generation apex locators are based on?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frequency based\nB. Impedence based\nC. Multiple frequency ratio based\nD. Resistance based\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "4th generation apex locators use multiple frequencies to determine the position of the apical foramen, making them more accurate than earlier single-frequency or impedance-based models.  \n\nThe correct answer is **C. Multiple frequency ratio based**.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1967", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Impedence based apex locator is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Generation 1\nB. Generation 2\nC. Generation 3\nD. Generation 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Impedance-based apex locators are considered the earliest type, developed first among electronic apex locator technologies.  \nThey operate by measuring electrical impedance in the root canal without using multiple frequencies.  \nThis corresponds to the first generation of apex locators.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1005", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Grape bunch\" shaped colonies are seen in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Streptococcus\nB. Staphylococcus\nC. E.coli\nD. Gonococci\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\"Grape bunch\" shaped colonies are characteristic of **Staphylococcus**, which grows in clusters resembling grapes.  \nStreptococcus typically forms chains, while E. coli and Gonococci do not exhibit this specific clustering pattern.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_450", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Most common phobia in chilhood:\n\nOptions: \nA. Zoophobia\nB. Nyclophobia\nC. Xenophobia.\nD. Claustrophobia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most common childhood phobia is fear of animals (zoophobia), whereas the others are less frequent in that age group.\n\n**Correct choice:**  \n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 129}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1569", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Potential generated due to movement of freely diffusible ions across a semi-permeable membrane is calculated using:\n\nOptions: \nA. Nemst equation\nB. Gibbs equation\nC. Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz equation\nD. Fick principle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz equation is used to calculate the membrane potential when multiple ions with different permeabilities are moving across a semi-permeable membrane, which matches the description. The Nernst equation applies to a single ion at equilibrium, not multiple freely diffusible ions. The other options are unrelated to this specific calculation.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 189}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_796", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What should be the ideal temperature in delivery room for the neonates to be kept in warmer?\n\nOptions: \nA. 22-26degC\nB. 28-30degC\nC. 30-35degC\nD. 37degC\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ideal delivery room temperature for neonates under a warmer is typically around 30\u201335\u00b0C to prevent hypothermia and maintain thermal stability immediately after birth.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 161}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2790", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Frankel's behavior rating scale, a positive child:\n\nOptions: \nA. May become uncooperative during treatment.\nB. Reluctant to accept treatment.\nC. Good rapport with the dentist.\nD. Show slight negativism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on Frankel's behavior rating scale, a positive child is characterized by good rapport with the dentist, which corresponds to a rating of \"positive\" or \"definitely positive.\" The other options describe negative or less cooperative behaviors.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 190}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1362", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Correlation between the height and weight of children is best represented by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Histogram\nB. Line diagram\nC. Scatter diagram\nD. Bar diagram\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A scatter diagram is used to show the relationship between two continuous variables, such as height and weight, by plotting points for each pair of values.  \n\nThe correct choice is: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_803", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The effectiveness of condensing porcelain powder to\nreduce shrinkage is determined by\n\nOptions: \nA. Shape and size of the particle\nB. Thickness of the platinum matrix\nC. Speed of increase of furnace heat\nD. Using powder of same particle size\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**, because the particle shape and size affect how densely the powder can be packed, which directly influences the amount of shrinkage during firing.  \nOther options like matrix thickness, heating rate, or uniform particle size are not the primary determinants of condensation effectiveness.  \nThus, the most likely correct choice is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 132, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 224}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2588", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Biomarker of alcoholic hepatitis:\n\nOptions: \nA. ALP\nB. AST\nC. LDH\nD. GGT\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "GGT (gamma-glutamyl transferase) is a sensitive marker for chronic alcohol consumption and is often elevated in alcoholic liver disease, including alcoholic hepatitis.  \nWhile AST is also commonly elevated in alcoholic hepatitis, GGT is considered a more specific biomarker for alcohol-induced liver injury.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 175}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2414", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 'Store in a cool place' is written on a drug label. It means drug should be stored at a temperature of:\n\nOptions: \nA. -2 degree Celsius\nB. 0 degree Celsius\nC. 2-8 degree Celsius\nD. 8-15 degree Celsius\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrase \"store in a cool place\" on a drug label typically corresponds to a temperature range of **8\u201315\u00b0C**. Among the options, choice **D** matches this range.\n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2769", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"First hand knowledge\" refers to\n\nOptions: \nA. Opinion of a doctor in cou\nB. Handwriting expe\nC. Common witness\nD. Fingerprint expe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\"First hand knowledge\" typically means direct personal observation or experience, which aligns most closely with a common witness who testifies about what they personally saw or heard.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1080", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Chances of recurrence of multicystic ameloblastoma after surgical enucleation is:\n\nOptions: \nA. <50%\nB. <10%\nC. 50-100%\nD. 18-25%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on clinical data, multicystic ameloblastoma has a high recurrence rate after simple enucleation due to its infiltrative growth. The reported recurrence rate typically falls within the range of **50\u2013100%**.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2444", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person of eonism derives pleasure from.\n\nOptions: \nA. Wearing clothes of opposite sex\nB. Fondling female body pas\nC. Rubbing genitalia against body of other person\nD. Seeing the opposite paner nude\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Eonism refers to the practice of wearing clothes typically associated with the opposite sex, which aligns with option A. The other options describe different paraphilias not associated with eonism. Therefore, the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1278", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Recommnended daily intake of iodine in pregnancy-\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 microgram\nB. 120 microgram\nC. 150 microgram\nD. 250 microgram\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The recommended daily iodine intake during pregnancy is higher than for non-pregnant adults to support fetal neurodevelopment. According to WHO and other major health organizations, it is 250 \u00b5g/day.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 161}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_288", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Estrogen and progesterone in the first 2 months pregnancy are produced by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Fetal ovaries\nB. Fetal adrenal\nC. Placenta\nD. Corpus luteum\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the first two months of pregnancy, the corpus luteum is responsible for producing estrogen and progesterone until the placenta takes over later. The placenta becomes the primary source after about 8\u201310 weeks, but early on it is the corpus luteum.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2169", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Surveyor is used on master cast to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Locate guiding planes\nB. Determine aesthetics\nC. Delineate areas of maximum convexity\nD. Locate undercuts to be used for retention or to be blocked out\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A surveyor is primarily used on a master cast to identify undercuts for retention or to be blocked out during the fabrication of a dental prosthesis.  \n\nThe correct choice is **D**.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1651", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: C wave in JVP due to\n\nOptions: \nA. Atrial contraction\nB. Atrial filling\nC. Tricuspid bulging\nD. Rapid ventricular filling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The C wave in the jugular venous pressure (JVP) is caused by the bulging of the tricuspid valve into the right atrium during early ventricular systole.  \nAmong the options, this corresponds to tricuspid bulging.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2128", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to WHO, anemia in pregnancy is diagnosed, when hemoglobin is less than:\n\nOptions: \nA. 10.0 gm%\nB. 11.0 gm%\nC. 12.0 gm%\nD. 9.0 gm%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to WHO guidelines, anemia in pregnancy is diagnosed when hemoglobin is less than **11.0 g/dL** (or gm%).  \n\nThe correct answer is **B**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 146}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_33", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In plasmodium vivax malaria, relapse is caused by:September 2012\n\nOptions: \nA. Sporozoite\nB. Schizont\nC. Hypnozoite\nD. Gamteocyte\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C. Hypnozoite** because in *Plasmodium vivax*, dormant liver-stage forms called hypnozoites can reactivate weeks or months later, causing relapse. Sporozoites initiate infection, schizonts are responsible for asexual reproduction, and gametocytes are involved in transmission to mosquitoes.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1154", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Algophobia is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Phobia of closed space.\nB. Phobia of large space.\nC. Phobia of pain.\nD. Phobia of animals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Algophobia is the fear of pain. The other options describe different phobias: claustrophobia (closed spaces), agoraphobia (large/open spaces), and zoophobia (animals).  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1379", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Optimal anti-rotational design in a blade is incorporated by offset not greater than?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 mm\nB. 5 mm\nC. 3 mm\nD. 6 mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on common dental implant guidelines, the anti-rotational feature (such as a flat or offset) in a blade implant design is typically limited to 3 mm to minimize excessive stress concentration and ensure stability.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1389", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Shy Drager syndrome is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Intestinal polyp\nB. Acute adernergic shock\nC. Vasovagal hypotension\nD. Orthostatic hypotension\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shy Drager syndrome, now known as multiple system atrophy (MSA), is primarily characterized by autonomic dysfunction, including severe **orthostatic hypotension**. Among the options, this matches most closely with orthostatic hypotension.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 172}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_832", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Perception of taste even in absence of stimuli is known as\n\nOptions: \nA. Ageusia\nB. Dysguesia\nC. Cocoguesia\nD. Phantoguesia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D. Phantoguesia**, which refers to a taste sensation perceived without an external stimulus, similar to a taste \"phantom.\" Ageusia is the loss of taste, dysgeusia is distorted taste, and cogaguesia is not a standard term. Phantoguesia specifically matches the description in the question.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_563", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Molecule with permanent dipole\n\nOptions: \nA. Oxygen\nB. Helium\nC. Liquid nitrogen\nD. Water\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Water is a polar molecule with an uneven distribution of charge, giving it a permanent dipole moment. The other options (oxygen, helium, and liquid nitrogen) consist of nonpolar molecules or atoms with no permanent dipole.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_484", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Resistance to corrosion in a cobalt-chrome casting is due to presence of:\n\nOptions: \nA. High quality iron\nB. Chrome\nC. Cobalt\nD. Nickel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The corrosion resistance in cobalt-chrome alloys is primarily due to the formation of a passive oxide layer on the surface, which is provided by the chromium content.  \nAmong the options, chrome is the key element responsible for this protective effect.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 172}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1852", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dry heat destroys microorganisms by\n\nOptions: \nA. Lysis\nB. Oxidation\nC. Hydrolysis of DNA\nD. Coagulation of proteins\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Dry heat primarily destroys microorganisms through the process of oxidation, which damages cellular components by removing electrons and breaking down molecules. The other options are more characteristic of other sterilization methods, such as moist heat causing protein coagulation.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_292", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compared with autoclave, use of a dry heat oven for sterilization has the following disadvantage:\n\nOptions: \nA. Time-consuming\nB. Less effective\nC. Causes instruments to rust\nD. Causes sharp instruments to dull\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The main disadvantage of a dry heat oven compared to an autoclave is that it requires a longer exposure time at higher temperatures to achieve sterilization, making it more time-consuming. While it is effective for heat-stable, moisture-sensitive items, it is not less effective when used correctly for appropriate materials. Rusting and dulling are not primary disadvantages of dry heat; autoclaving (moist heat) poses more risk for corrosion and dulling of sharp edges.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 120, "total_tokens": 245}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2340", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Anti-hypeensive drug contraindicated in pregnancy is:September 2005, 2010 March 2007, March 2013\n\nOptions: \nA. Hydralazine\nB. Methyldopa\nC. Enalapril\nD. Amlodopine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C. Enalapril**, because ACE inhibitors like enalapril are contraindicated in pregnancy due to risks of fetal injury, especially in the second and third trimesters. The other options are either considered safer or used with caution in pregnancy.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 186}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2411", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Habits are classified as Intentional and Unintentional by:\n\nOptions: \nA. William James\nB. Kingsley\nC. Earnest Klein\nD. Finn and Sim\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The classification of habits as intentional and unintentional is attributed to **William James** in his work *The Principles of Psychology*.  \nThis distinguishes habits formed by conscious will from those acquired automatically.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 165}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_419", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Square root of pq/n indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Standard error of mean\nB. Standard error of difference of means\nC. Standard error of proportions\nD. Standard error of difference in proportions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The expression \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{pq}{n}}\\) is the formula for the standard error of a proportion, where \\(p\\) is the proportion of success, \\(q = 1-p\\), and \\(n\\) is the sample size.  \n\n**Correct choice:** C  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2021", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Km value indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Purity of Enzyme\nB. Physiological role\nC. The substrate concentration at half maximal velocity\nD. A\ufb03nity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Km value is defined as the substrate concentration at which the reaction velocity is half of Vmax.  \nThis matches option C directly.  \nWhile Km can relate to affinity in some cases, its primary definition is as stated in C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 166}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2713", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Following renal disorder is associated with worst pregnancy outcome:\n\nOptions: \nA. Systemic lupus erythromatosus\nB. IgA nephropathy\nC. Autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease\nD. Scleroderma\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Among the listed conditions, scleroderma (systemic sclerosis) carries the highest risk of severe complications in pregnancy, including renal crisis and maternal mortality.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1028", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is responsible for rhythm generation of inspiration?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dorsal nucleus of vagus\nB. Pre botzinger complex\nC. ventral respiratory neurons\nD. Pneumotaxic center\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The pre-B\u00f6tzinger complex in the medulla is recognized as the primary site for generating the rhythm of inspiration in mammals.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2138", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Iodine is primarily important in the biochemical synthesis of:\n\nOptions: \nA. ACTH\nB. Thyroxine\nC. Adrenaline\nD. Calcitonin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Iodine is a key component of thyroid hormones, and thyroxine (T4) is the major hormone produced by the thyroid gland that contains iodine. While calcitonin is also produced by the thyroid, it is not an iodine-dependent hormone like thyroxine.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2143", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The maximum shrinkage during firing process in ceramic occurs in:\n\nOptions: \nA. High Bisque stage\nB. Low Bisque stage\nC. Medium Bisque stage\nD. Fusion stage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most shrinkage in ceramics occurs when clay loses water and particles draw together during the early stages of firing, which is the **Low Bisque stage** before major sintering. The other stages involve less overall dimensional change.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1824", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TNM Staging is what type of scale\n\nOptions: \nA. Ordinal\nB. Ratio\nC. Nominal\nD. Interval\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "TNM staging classifies cancer progression into ordered categories (e.g., Stage I, II, III, IV) without equal intervals or a true zero, which fits the definition of an ordinal scale. The other scale types do not match: nominal lacks order, interval has equal intervals, and ratio has a true zero. Therefore, the correct choice is ordinal.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 181}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_260", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Landmark for pup chamber opening is :\n\nOptions: \nA. CEJ\nB. Cervical third of crown\nC. Level of alveolar bone\nD. Enamel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely answer is **A. CEJ** (cementoenamel junction) because the pulp chamber opening (pulp horn) is typically located near the cementoenamel junction in molars, especially in younger teeth.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_65", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The resolution of IOPA is about:\n\nOptions: \nA. 10 Lp/mm\nB. 16 Lp/mm\nC. 28 Lp/mm\nD. 30 Lp/mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The resolution of intraoral periapical (IOPA) radiography is typically around 20 line pairs per millimeter (lp/mm), but among the given options, 16 lp/mm is the closest and most commonly cited value in dental radiology references.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1340", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Initial clicking of TMJ while opening is due to\n\nOptions: \nA. Protruded condyle in respect to articular disc\nB. Retruded condyle in respect to articular disc\nC. Perforated disc\nD. Lateral displacement of the condyle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The initial clicking during TMJ opening is typically caused by a momentary disc-condyle misalignment that resolves as movement continues, often described as the condyle moving from a slightly retruded position relative to the disc.  \n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is **B**.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 176}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1145", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Highly vascular tumor of brain and spinal cord in adults:\n\nOptions: \nA. Metastasis\nB. Pilocytic astrocytoma\nC. Hemangioblastoma\nD. Cavernous malformation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **C. Hemangioblastoma**, as it is a highly vascular tumor that typically occurs in the cerebellum or spinal cord in adults.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_461", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The advantage of glass ionomer cement reinforced with metal particles is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreased strength but biocompatibility\nB. Increased resistance to abrasion\nC. Better colour\nD. Ease of manipulation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B. Increased resistance to abrasion** because metal-reinforced glass ionomer cements (such as cermets) are specifically designed to improve wear resistance and durability compared to conventional glass ionomers.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1200", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Multifactorial Causation\" theory was given by\n\nOptions: \nA. McMohan Pugh\nB. Pettenkofer of Munich\nC. Winslow\nD. Robert Koch\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Multifactorial Causation\" theory is associated with **Pettenkofer of Munich**, who emphasized that disease is caused by multiple interacting factors, not a single agent.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_145", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The transport of CO is diffusion limited because\n\nOptions: \nA. Binds avidly with Hb\nB. Partial pressure of CO is less\nC. CO is less absorbed in water\nD. Alveolar membrane is less permeable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because carbon monoxide binds to hemoglobin with very high affinity (about 240 times greater than oxygen), which keeps the partial pressure of CO in the blood extremely low, making diffusion into the blood the limiting step in its transport.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 189}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_157", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Measuring variation between two different units is done through\n\nOptions: \nA. Variance\nB. Standard deviation\nC. Coefficient of variation\nD. Range\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The coefficient of variation is specifically used to compare variation between different units because it is a dimensionless ratio (standard deviation divided by mean). Variance, standard deviation, and range are not suitable for direct comparison across different units.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 179}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_192", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In processing methyl methacrylate, the resin may show porosity if the flask is placed too soon. Porosity most likely occur\n\nOptions: \nA. Throughout the denture\nB. Near the borders\nC. In the thickest part\nD. On the denture surface\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Porosity from packing the flask too soon occurs because the resin is still expanding when polymerization begins, causing voids in the thickest sections where heat buildup and expansion are greatest.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 186}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_254", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Child Pugh score put patients into three categories of Score A (<7), Score B (7-9) and Score C (10-15). The following is a type of which scale?\n\nOptions: \nA. Nominal\nB. Ordinal\nC. Quantitative\nD. Continuous\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Child\u2013Pugh score groups patients into ordered categories (A, B, C) based on severity, which indicates an ordinal scale.  \nIt is not merely naming categories (nominal), nor is it a numeric measurement without categories (quantitative/continuous).  \nThus, the correct classification is ordinal.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 200}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_290", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tracheostomy will:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase dead air space\nB. Increase respiratory resistance\nC. Decrease respiratory work\nD. Cause obstruction in respiration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tracheostomy bypasses the upper airway, reducing anatomical dead space and airway resistance, which in turn decreases the work of breathing.  \nAmong the options, this corresponds to a decrease in respiratory work.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_313", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 22 years old male presented with history of fever, sore throat and enlarged neck lymph nodes. He was ordered a Paul-Bunnell test with a suspicion of Infectious mononucleosis. What is the immunological basis behind the use of this test?\n\nOptions: \nA. Heterophile antibody test\nB. Complement mediated agglutination reaction\nC. Homophile antibody test\nD. Latex agglutination test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Paul-Bunnell test detects heterophile antibodies produced in infectious mononucleosis, which agglutinate sheep or horse red blood cells.  \nThis makes it a heterophile antibody test, not based on complement, homophile antibodies, or latex particles.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 167, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 237}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_315", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The microwave method of processing resin is better than the conventional in that it provides:\n\nOptions: \nA. Better shine\nB. Less porosity\nC. Less shrinkage\nD. Color stability\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The microwave method of processing resin typically reduces internal defects and improves curing uniformity, which leads to fewer voids compared to conventional heating. Among the options, this directly corresponds to less porosity.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_337", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Induction of inhalational agent is faster.\n\nOptions: \nA. Agent with high blood gas solubility\nB. Combined with nitrous oxide\nC. Person with increased residual volume\nD. Right to left shunt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because nitrous oxide reduces the concentration of other agents needed and speeds induction by the second gas effect.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_341", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: HCO3/H2CO3 is the best buffer because it is:\n\nOptions: \nA. pKa near physiological pH\nB. Its components can be increased or decreased in the body as needed\nC. Good acceptor and donor of H+ ions\nD. Combination of a weak acid and weak base\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because the pKa of the HCO\u2083\u207b/H\u2082CO\u2083 system is about 6.1, which is close enough to physiological pH (7.4) to be effective in buffering.  \nWhile other options describe true characteristics of buffers, the key reason this specific pair is the *best* physiological buffer is its near-physiological pKa combined with the body\u2019s ability to regulate its components (lungs and kidneys).  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 227}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_380", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A voluntary donor underwent apheresis for platelet donation for the first time after which he developed perioral tingling and numbness. This is seen because\n\nOptions: \nA. His platelet count was low for donation\nB. He underwent apheresis for the first time\nC. Due to fluid depletion\nD. Due to citrate based anticoagulant\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The symptoms described are a known side effect of citrate-based anticoagulants used in apheresis, which can cause hypocalcemia leading to perioral tingling and numbness.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 152, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 197}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_433", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Malaria control means\n\nOptions: \nA. To reduce Malaria moality to Zero\nB. To prevent local transmission for 3 years\nC. To reduce Malaria disease so that its no longer a Public Health Problem\nD. To reduce Incidence to Zero\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most accurate definition of malaria control is to reduce the disease burden so it ceases to be a major public health issue, rather than aiming for complete elimination.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 178}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_478", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes the resistance form in endodontic root canal preparation?\n\nOptions: \nA. The establishment of apical tug back resistance to prevent the apical root fracture during obturation\nB. The cavity form which is obtained for application of condenser in vertical compaction\nC. The cavity form which is designed for application of condenser in lateral compaction\nD. Cavity form which is designed to obtain for entry of condenser during obturation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because resistance form in endodontic preparation specifically refers to creating a shape that provides apical resistance to prevent overextension of filling material and reduce the risk of apical fracture during obturation.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 153, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_481", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Internal occlusal rest provided in partial denture does not provide:\n\nOptions: \nA. Horizontal stabilization\nB. Retention\nC. Vertical stop\nD. Occlusal support\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The internal occlusal rest in a partial denture primarily provides vertical support and stabilization against occlusal forces, but it is not designed to provide direct retention\u2014that function is typically handled by clasps or other retentive elements.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_487", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For statistical test output of p value is interpreted as\n\nOptions: \nA. Rejective Ho, p <0.05\nB. Rejective Ho, p>0.05\nC. Rejective H1, p<0.05\nD. Accepting Ho, p<0.05\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct interpretation is that we reject the null hypothesis (H\u2080) when the p-value is less than the significance level, typically 0.05.  \nTherefore, the option matching this is \u201cReject H\u2080, p < 0.05.\u201d  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The principal reason for placing an aluminium filter in\nthe primary beam of radiation is to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Reduce exposure time\nB. Decrease development time of the films\nC. Reduce radiation to the skin of the patient\nD. Obtain greater definition of the images of teeth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The primary purpose of an aluminum filter in the primary beam is to absorb low-energy, less penetrating radiation that would otherwise increase patient skin dose without improving image quality. Therefore, it is mainly used to reduce radiation exposure to the patient\u2019s skin.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 139, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 211}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_575", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient presented with acute exacerbation of bronchial asthma. Salbutamol inhalation didn't improve the condition of the patient. So, intravenous coicosteroids and aminophylline were added and the condition improved. What is the mechanism of action of coicosteroids in this condition?\n\nOptions: \nA. They cause bronchodilatation when given with xanthines\nB. They increase bronchial responsiveness to salbutamol\nC. They increase the action of aminophylline on adenosine receptors\nD. They increase the mucociliary clearance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because corticosteroids reduce airway inflammation and hyperresponsiveness, which helps restore the effectiveness of beta-agonists like salbutamol.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 249}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_734", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Central value of a set of 180 values can be obtained by\n\nOptions: \nA. 2nd tertile\nB. 90th percentile\nC. 2nd quartile\nD. 9th decile\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The central value of a set of 180 values is the median.  \nThe median corresponds to the 2nd quartile (Q2), which divides the data into two equal halves.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_747", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compared to unfractionated heparin, Low molecular weight heparin (LMWH) has reliable anticoagulant action because:\n\nOptions: \nA. It interferes with thrombin and antithrombin III simultaneously\nB. It is less protein bound\nC. It is given subcutaneously\nD. It is cleared by macrophages\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "LMWH has a more predictable anticoagulant effect than unfractionated heparin primarily because it has less binding to plasma proteins, leading to more reliable bioavailability.  \n\nCorrect choice: **B**  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_793", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mandibular fracture managed by adapting mini plates is a type of\n\nOptions: \nA. Load bearing osteosynthesis\nB. Load sharing\nC. Non rigid osteosynthesis\nD. Rigid osteosynthesis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Miniplate fixation for mandibular fractures is considered **load-sharing** because the bone bears some of the functional load alongside the plate. It provides semi-rigid stability rather than absolute rigidity.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_800", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following cause an increase in ACh release from the presynaptic neuron?\n\nOptions: \nA. Blocking calcium channels on presynaptic\nB. Blocking chloride channel on presynaptic\nC. Blocking Na channel\nD. Blocking K channels\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Blocking potassium channels on the presynaptic neuron would prolong depolarization, allowing more calcium influx and thus increasing acetylcholine release.  \n\nThe correct choice is:  \n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_864", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is used for selecting patients with respect to potential factors that will affect the results?\n\nOptions: \nA. Systematic random sampling\nB. Simple random sampling\nC. Stratified random sampling\nD. Cluster sampling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Stratified random sampling** ensures subgroups (strata) of patients are represented in the sample, which helps control for potential factors that could affect the results.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 146}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_947", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bacteria associated with caries are able to cause the same due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Production of extxacellular polysaccharides like dextrans and levans\nB. Production of acid to hydrolyse diet carbohydrates\nC. Production of enzymes which inhibit normal flora\nD. Inhibition of secretory IgA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Answer:**  \nBacteria involved in caries primarily produce acid from dietary carbohydrates, which demineralizes tooth enamel.\n\nThe most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1054", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Disadvantages of using a GRID during radiography is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased patient exposure due to more exposure time\nB. Decreased exposure time\nC. Increased secondary radiation fog to film\nD. Reduces secondary radiation to film\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**, because using a grid requires an increase in exposure factors (such as mAs) to compensate for the absorption of scattered radiation, which results in higher patient dose.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1134", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Beveling of the pulpoaxial line angle of a class II cavity\nis done to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase the strength of the restoration\nB. Improved marginal adaptation\nC. To prevent the fracture of enamel\nD. To prevent the fracture of amalgam\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Beveling the pulpoaxial line angle in a class II cavity is primarily done to remove unsupported enamel rods and create a stronger enamel margin, which helps prevent enamel fracture under occlusal load.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 130, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 188}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1167", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The purpose of pulpotomy in young permanent tooth\n\nOptions: \nA. Prevent tooth fracture\nB. To induce root formation\nC. Formation of hard base to support restoration\nD. To minimize infection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **B. To induce root formation**, as pulpotomy in a young permanent tooth aims to preserve pulp vitality and allow continued root development (apexogenesis).  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 169}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1169", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The penetration of the fissure sealant into the fissure:\n\nOptions: \nA. Is not influenced by the wettability of the enamel\nB. Is independent of the chemical composition of the enamel\nC. Is the result of a chemical bond between the sealant and enamel\nD. Must occur before the polymerization of the material\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because sealant must flow into the fissure before it hardens; penetration is a physical process that occurs prior to polymerization.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1203", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is main cause of pain during pulpal injury progression?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased vascular permeability\nB. Decreased threshold of nerve fibres to pain\nC. Arteriolar dilatation\nD. Decrease pressure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The main cause of pain during pulpal injury progression is increased pressure within the rigid pulp chamber due to inflammation and edema, which corresponds to a **decrease** in the ability to relieve that pressure. Among the options, \"Decrease pressure\" is likely a typographical error and is meant to indicate a decrease in the ability to relieve pressure or an increase in pressure, but it is the option that points toward pressure change. Therefore, the intended correct choice is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 124, "total_tokens": 250}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1204", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Decay of enamel following radiotherapy is initiated due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decrease in salivary flow\nB. Direct radiations contacting the enamel\nC. Dessication of tooth structure\nD. Hypocalcification and pitting of enamel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A. Decrease in salivary flow** because radiotherapy to the head and neck often damages salivary glands, leading to xerostomia, which reduces the protective and remineralizing effects of saliva, thereby increasing the risk of enamel decay.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 195}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1227", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The decreased phosphate levels seen in hyper parathyroidism is due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreased intestinal phosphate absorption\nB. Increased calcium excretion\nC. Decreased renal phosphate absorption\nD. Increased loss of phosphate in urine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because in hyperparathyroidism, excess parathyroid hormone (PTH) reduces renal phosphate reabsorption, leading to increased urinary phosphate excretion and thus decreased serum phosphate levels.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 189}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1250", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: HIV sentinel surveillance provides data:\n\nOptions: \nA. To monitor disease trends\nB. To identify high risk population\nC. To estimate disease incidence\nD. To assess the quality of related services\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "HIV sentinel surveillance is primarily used to monitor trends in HIV prevalence over time within specific populations, such as pregnant women attending antenatal clinics. While it can indirectly inform about high-risk groups and service quality, its main purpose is tracking epidemiological trends. Therefore, the most directly aligned option is monitoring disease trends.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 216}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1298", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increased depth in posterior palatal seal area of denture \ncauses:\n\nOptions: \nA. Tingling sensation\nB. Gagging\nC. Increased retention\nD. Unseating of denture base\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Increased depth in the posterior palatal seal area can overextend the denture, leading to irritation and triggering the gag reflex. The correct answer is **B. Gagging**.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1309", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which factor of the following contributes to short duration of anesthetic action of single dose thiopental\n\nOptions: \nA. Rapid biotransformation\nB. Rapid accumulation in body fat\nC. High lipid solubility\nD. Ability to enter and leave brain tissue every rapidly\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The primary reason thiopental\u2019s anesthetic action is brief after a single dose is its rapid redistribution from the brain to other tissues\u2014especially muscle and fat\u2014rather than rapid metabolism. Among the options, **D** directly addresses this redistribution by noting its ability to leave brain tissue rapidly.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 179}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1319", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Test to exclude a disease\n\nOptions: \nA. Positive predictivity\nB. Negative predictivity\nC. Specificity\nD. Sensitivity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The test that best helps exclude a disease is the one that correctly identifies those without the disease, which is measured by **negative predictivity** \u2014 the probability that a negative test result truly means absence of the disease.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1344", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The usefulness of a screening test depends upon it\n\nOptions: \nA. Sensitivity\nB. Specificity\nC. Reliability\nD. Predictive value\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate answer is **D. Predictive value** because it directly indicates the probability that a positive or negative test result correctly identifies whether the disease is present or absent, which is most relevant for clinical usefulness. Sensitivity and specificity are important test characteristics, but predictive values incorporate disease prevalence to assess real-world performance. Reliability (consistency) is necessary but not sufficient for a test to be useful.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 124, "total_tokens": 228}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1360", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Isosorbide 5 \u2014 mononitrate is preferred because\n\nOptions: \nA. Less tolerance develops\nB. Sublingual absorption is better\nC. Longer duration of action\nD. Direct coronary vasodilatory action is more\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because isosorbide 5\u2011mononitrate has a lower tendency to induce tolerance compared to other nitrates, making it a preferred long\u2011term option.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 166}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1394", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrous oxide alone is not used as a G.A agent because of\n\nOptions: \nA. Difficulty in maintaining an adequate oxygen concentration\nB. Expense of the agent and its exposure hazards\nC. Adverse effect on liver\nD. Poor analgesic property\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nitrous oxide alone cannot provide sufficient oxygen concentration if used at high concentrations for general anesthesia, making it unsafe as a sole agent. The primary issue is the risk of hypoxia, which aligns with option A.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 130, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 192}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1402", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Angles between Adhesive and Adherent is Zero degree, it indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Complete wetting of surfaces\nB. Rough surfaces between Adhesive & Adherent\nC. Adherent and adhesive molecules are tangent to each other\nD. Irregularities present between Adherent surfaces\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A contact angle of zero degrees means the liquid adhesive spreads completely over the adherent surface, indicating ideal **complete wetting**.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1413", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Schizonts and late trophozoite stages of plasmodium falciparum not seen in peripheral blood smear because:\n\nOptions: \nA. They are sequestered in the spleen\nB. Due to adherence to the capillary endothelium, they are not seen in peripheral blood\nC. Due to antigen-antibody reaction and removal\nD. They are seen in mosquito blood\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because *Plasmodium falciparum* schizonts and late trophozoites adhere to capillary endothelium in internal organs (a process called cytoadherence), which prevents them from circulating in peripheral blood.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 154, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 215}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1436", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During relining procedures fear lies in the alteration of\n\nOptions: \nA. Balanced occlusion\nB. Centric occlusion\nC. Vertical dimension\nD. Condylar guidance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "During relining procedures, the primary concern is the potential change to the **vertical dimension** because adding material to the denture base can alter the fit and increase the occlusal height. Balanced occlusion, centric occlusion, and condylar guidance are affected secondarily if the vertical dimension is altered.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 199}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1451", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these findings is not specific of blast injury?\n\nOptions: \nA. Abrasion\nB. Bruise\nC. Puncture laceration\nD. Fracture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An abrasion is a non-specific superficial injury that can occur from any blunt trauma, whereas a bruise, puncture laceration, and fracture are more characteristic patterns in blast injuries due to blast waves, penetrating debris, or fractures from being thrown.  \nTherefore, **A. Abrasion** is not a specific finding of blast injury.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1488", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Phosphate bonded investment should be completely carbon free, otherwise:\n\nOptions: \nA. Investment chips off when molten metal enters the mold space\nB. Black castings\nC. Carbon makes the casting brittle\nD. Smooth casting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Phosphate-bonded investments are used for high-temperature casting, and any residual carbon can cause a reducing atmosphere that leads to oxidation and darkening of the casting. Therefore, if not carbon-free, it results in **black castings**.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1523", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: NK cells are effective against viral infected cells only if the cell with infection:\n\nOptions: \nA. Express MHC class I proteins\nB. Unable to express MHC class I proteins\nC. Express MHC class II proteins\nD. Unable to express MHC class II proteins\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "NK cells target cells that lack MHC class I molecules, which is a common evasion strategy by viruses. Therefore, the correct condition is that the infected cell is **unable to express MHC class I proteins**.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1570", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mean and standard deviation can be worked out only if data is on\n\nOptions: \nA. Nominal scale\nB. Dichotomous scale\nC. Interval/Ratio scale\nD. Ordinal scale\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mean and standard deviation require data that have meaningful intervals and a true zero point, which are characteristics of interval or ratio scales. Nominal, dichotomous, and ordinal scales do not meet these requirements.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 169}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1572", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mean and standard deviation can be worked out only if data is on -\n\nOptions: \nA. Interval/Ratio scale\nB. Dichotomous scale\nC. Nominal scale\nD. Ordinal scale\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mean and standard deviation require data that have meaningful intervals and a true zero point, which are characteristics of interval or ratio scales.  \nNominal, ordinal, and dichotomous scales do not generally support these calculations.  \nThus, the correct choice is the one that specifies interval or ratio scale.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1576", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increased size of filler particle in composite:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increases strength\nB. Decreases surface roughness\nC. Increases exposure time\nD. decreases viscosity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Increased filler particle size generally decreases viscosity because larger particles have less total surface area for a given volume, reducing particle-matrix interactions. This makes **D** the correct choice.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1595", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Feed forward mechanism..\n\nOptions: \nA. Feeling thirsty while walking in hot temperature\nB. Shivering on exposure to cold temperature\nC. Salivation on smelling food\nD. Increase blood pressure during supine posture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The feed forward mechanism involves a physiological response in anticipation of a change, often triggered by a sensory cue before the main stimulus occurs. Salivation on smelling food is a classic example because the smell signals the imminent arrival of food, preparing the digestive system ahead of time.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1623", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In reversible hydrocolloid the property by which the transformation from sol to gel and gel to sol occurs, is a function of the:\n\nOptions: \nA. Concentration of fillers and plasticizer\nB. Percentage composition by weight of water\nC. Concentration of potassium sulphate\nD. Temperature\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The transformation between sol and gel in reversible hydrocolloid is controlled by temperature changes, not by chemical composition adjustments.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 186}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1641", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following hormones is controlled by feedforward control?\n\nOptions: \nA. ADH\nB. Insulin\nC. Coicosteroids\nD. Prolactin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The hormone most clearly associated with feedforward control is **insulin**, which can be released in anticipation of a rise in blood glucose (e.g., before or during a meal) rather than solely in response to an increase.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1696", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Radio density can be increased by\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreasing MA\nB. Decreasing kVp\nC. Decreasing target film distance\nD. Increasing target film distance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Radio density refers to the overall blackening of an image, and increasing it requires more exposure reaching the film. Decreasing the target-film distance (TFD) increases exposure by reducing the divergence of the x-ray beam, thereby increasing density. Therefore, the correct choice is decreasing TFD.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 187}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1721", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does low volume of distribution of a drug mean?\n\nOptions: \nA. Low bioavailability\nB. Does not accumulates in tissues\nC. Low absorption\nD. Not metabolized in the body\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Low volume of distribution generally means the drug is largely confined to the plasma and does not extensively distribute into tissues.  \n\nAmong the options, this corresponds most closely to **B. Does not accumulates in tissues**.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 178}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1731", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pulpectomy and pulp capping are more successful in\nprimary teeth because of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased odontoblastic activity in the young\nB. Increased blood supply through the wide apex\nC. Increased volume of pulp in primary teeth\nD. Lesser amount of collagen fibres in young\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **B** because primary teeth have wider apical openings, allowing better blood supply and healing potential for pulp therapies like pulpectomy and pulp capping.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 192}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1779", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Low apparent volume of distribution of a drug indicates That\n\nOptions: \nA. Drug has low half life\nB. Drug has low bioavailability\nC. Drug has low efficacy\nD. Drug is not extensively distribution to tissue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The apparent volume of distribution is a measure of how extensively a drug distributes into tissues versus remaining in the plasma. A low value means the drug is largely confined to the plasma and is not widely distributed into tissues.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 190}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1789", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the advantage of chromic gut over plain\ngut suture in deep wounds?\n\nOptions: \nA. Greater strength\nB. Greater ease of use\nC. Delayed resorption\nD. Less tissue irritation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Chromic gut is treated to resist breakdown, which slows its absorption compared to plain gut, making it more suitable for deep wounds where longer wound support is needed.  \nTherefore, the key advantage is **delayed resorption**.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 176}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1822", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Streptococci have the ability to adhere to the tooth surfaces and contribute to caries development as they?\n\nOptions: \nA. Are penicillinase resistant\nB. Produce acid during metabolism\nC. Produce extracellular polysachharides\nD. Ferment carbohydrates\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Streptococci like *Streptococcus mutans* are key in caries because they adhere via extracellular polysaccharides, forming plaque and trapping acid against the enamel. While they also produce acid (B) and ferment carbohydrates (D), the specific ability that enables persistent adherence to the tooth surface is the production of extracellular polysaccharides.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 181}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1885", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If rate of loading is decreased, the mechanical properties of material:\n\nOptions: \nA. Remains unchanged\nB. Increases\nC. Decreases\nD. Becomes unpredictable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When the rate of loading is decreased, materials typically become less brittle and can exhibit slightly lower yield strength but often show increased ductility, so overall mechanical properties like strength often **decrease** slightly compared to high strain-rate loading.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1896", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Condylar fracture which leads to disruption of TMJ anteriorly is an example of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Simple fracture\nB. Compound fracture\nC. Complex fracture\nD. Comminuted fracture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This refers to a fracture where the condylar head is displaced anteriorly out of the glenoid fossa, creating an open communication with the external environment via the external auditory meatus, making it a compound fracture.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1904", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During exercise in physiological limits what is the effect on end systolic volume?\n\nOptions: \nA. ESV decreases\nB. ESV increase\nC. ESV remain unchanged\nD. ESV first decrease and then increases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "During moderate exercise within physiological limits, sympathetic stimulation increases contractility and heart rate, which leads to more complete ejection of blood from the ventricles, thereby decreasing end-systolic volume (ESV).\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 180}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1920", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tachycardia in a patient in shock is response to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hypotension\nB. Vasoconstriction\nC. CNS anoxia\nD. Anxiety\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tachycardia in shock is primarily a compensatory response to low blood pressure, which reduces perfusion and triggers increased heart rate to maintain cardiac output. Among the options, hypotension is the direct physiological trigger for this compensatory tachycardia.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1926", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Inferior thyroid artery ligation during thyroidectomy is done\n\nOptions: \nA. For recurrent Laryngeal nerve\nB. Superior laryngeal nerve\nC. Vagus nerve\nD. Glossopharyngeal nerve\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The inferior thyroid artery is closely related to the recurrent laryngeal nerve, and careful ligation during thyroidectomy is performed to avoid injuring this nerve.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 165}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1943", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a coho study, to study association between factor and disease, the risk ratio was calculated to be equal to 1. What does this signifies?\n\nOptions: \nA. There is no association present between the factor and the disease\nB. There is positive association between the factor and the disease\nC. There is negative association between the factor and the disease\nD. Data insufficient to comment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A risk ratio of 1 means the risk of disease is the same in both exposed and unexposed groups, indicating no association.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 169, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 207}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1971", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following leads to an increase in enzyme activity -\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase in temperature\nB. Decrease in activation energy\nC. Extremes of pH value\nD. Low substrate concentration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An increase in temperature generally raises enzyme activity up to an optimal point, while a decrease in activation energy (often via enzymes) increases reaction rate. Extremes of pH or low substrate concentration typically reduce enzyme activity.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 188}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2032", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The speed with which the electrons travel from the\nfilament of cathode to the anode depends upon\n\nOptions: \nA. Potential difference between the two electrodes\nB. Number of milliamperes in the tube circuit\nC. Angle between the filament and target\nD. Voltage of the filament\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The speed of electrons in a cathode ray tube is determined by the electric field accelerating them, which is set by the potential difference between the cathode and anode.  \nThe filament voltage affects electron emission but not their final speed, while milliamperes relate to current (number of electrons) and the angle is irrelevant to speed.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 229}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2046", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Good contacts in primary teeth with lack of spacing predicts?\n\nOptions: \nA. Normal occlusion in permanent teeth\nB. Crowding in permanent teeth\nC. Anterior cross bite\nD. Spaced permanent dentition\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Good contacts in primary teeth with no spacing often indicate that there will be insufficient space for the larger permanent teeth, leading to crowding.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 165}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2063", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a patient with acute pulpitis, it is difficult for the patient to locate the pain. This is because?\n\nOptions: \nA. No nociceptors are present in the pulp\nB. Less proprioceptors are present in the pulp\nC. Patient cannot speak\nD. Patient is not cooperative\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because the pulp lacks proprioceptors, which are needed for precise localization of pain.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2098", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following hormones increases the sensitivity of heart to epinephrine:\n\nOptions: \nA. Parathyroid\nB. Insulin\nC. Thyroid\nD. Glucagon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C. Thyroid** because thyroid hormones (specifically T3) upregulate beta-adrenergic receptors in the heart, enhancing its sensitivity to catecholamines like epinephrine.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2113", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Interdental papilla protruding from the rubber dam, most common cause is\n\nOptions: \nA. Inflammation of interdental papillae\nB. Use of light weight rubber dam\nC. Punch are placed too far\nD. Punch are placed too close\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause is that the punch holes were placed too close together, which does not allow enough dam material between the teeth and forces the papilla to protrude.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2183", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study was done where the sale of anti-asthma drug was recorded and the number of deaths because of asthma was measured over a period of 15 years (1975-1990). This is which type of study.\n\nOptions: \nA. Ecological\nB. Case reference\nC. Experimental\nD. Psephology\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This is an **ecological study** because it examines aggregate data (sales and deaths) over time without linking individual exposures to outcomes.  \n\nThe correct answer is:  \n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 137, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2243", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Phenylbutyrate is used in management of urea cycle disorders. What is its role?\n\nOptions: \nA. Activates enzymes of urea cycle\nB. Excretion of products of urea cycle\nC. Maintains energy production\nD. Scavenges nitrogen\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Phenylbutyrate is converted to phenylacetate, which conjugates with glutamine to form phenylacetylglutamine, a compound excreted in urine, thereby helping to remove excess nitrogen. This makes it a **nitrogen-scavenging** agent.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2276", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Standard deviation of means measures -\n\nOptions: \nA. Non-sampling errors\nB. Sampling error\nC. Random errors\nD. Conceptual errors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The standard deviation of means, often called the standard error of the mean, quantifies the variability of sample means around the population mean due to random sampling variation. This is directly a measure of **sampling error**.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2282", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following gives the rate of drug absorption in plasma concentration graph?\n\nOptions: \nA. Tmax and Cmax\nB. Area under the curve\nC. Tmax alone\nD. Cmax alone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Cmax alone** is the best answer because it represents the peak plasma concentration, which directly reflects the rate of absorption\u2014faster absorption leads to a higher and earlier Cmax.  \nTmax indicates the time to reach peak concentration but not the rate itself, while AUC reflects total exposure, not the absorption rate.  \nThus, among the options, Cmax alone is most directly tied to the rate of drug absorption.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 221}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2290", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is an example of placebo?\n\nOptions: \nA. Herbal medication with no known effect\nB. Physiotherapy\nC. Sham surgery\nD. Cognitive behavioral therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C. Sham surgery** because it is a procedure designed to mimic real surgery without any therapeutic effect, which fits the definition of a placebo. Herbal medication may have unknown effects but is not necessarily inert, while physiotherapy and cognitive behavioral therapy are active treatments. A placebo is an inert intervention given as if it were real, and sham surgery is a classic example of this.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 223}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2313", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The setting time of zinc phosphate may be retarded by?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase in the ratio of powder to liquid\nB. Diluting the liquid with water\nC. Increase the addition of powder to liquid\nD. Decrease the addition of powder to liquid\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**B. Diluting the liquid with water**  \nDiluting the liquid with water reduces the concentration of phosphoric acid, slowing the reaction and thus retarding the setting time.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2342", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes paradoxical suicide?\n\nOptions: \nA. Suicide after taking low dose of drug\nB. Suicide occurring at the time when the pt. stas to recover\nC. Suicidal tendency increase as the patient improves\nD. Accidental completion of suicide\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**, as paradoxical suicide refers to suicide occurring when a patient starts to recover from depression, often because they regain just enough energy to act on suicidal thoughts while still having a negative outlook.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 165}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2369", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The number of patients required in a clinical trial to treat a specify disease increases as\n\nOptions: \nA. The drop-out rate increases\nB. The significance level increases\nC. The size of the expected treatment effect increased\nD. The incidence of the disease decreases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because a higher drop-out rate means more participants are needed at the start to ensure enough complete the study for statistical power.  \n\n**B** is incorrect because increasing the significance level (e.g., from 0.01 to 0.05) reduces the required sample size.  \n**C** is incorrect because a larger treatment effect means fewer patients are needed to detect it.  \n**D** is unrelated; incidence affects feasibility but not the calculation of required patients for a given effect size.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 139, "output_tokens": 131, "total_tokens": 270}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2463", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Saliva which is formed in salivary glands, when passes from salivary gland to duct orifices, it undergoes numerous ion exchanges and as a result\nsaliva become ____________ as compared to plasma:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hypertonic sometimes\nB. Hypotonic\nC. Isotonic\nD. Hypertonic always\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Saliva becomes hypotonic compared to plasma because the ducts reabsorb more sodium and chloride than they secrete potassium and bicarbonate.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2477", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following rightly describes the mechanism of \"Pressor Escape\" in SIADH?\n\nOptions: \nA. Characterized by sudden increase in urine volume with decrease in urine osmolality independent of circulating vasopressin levels.\nB. Characterized by sudden increase in urine volume with decrease in urine osmolality dependent of circulating vasopressin levels.\nC. Characterized by sudden decrease in urine volume with increase in urine osmolality independent of circulating vasopressin levels.\nD. Characterized by sudden decrease in urine volume with increase in urine osmolality dependent of circulating vasopressin levels.=\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Pressor escape in SIADH involves a spontaneous increase in urine volume and decrease in urine osmolality despite continued high vasopressin levels, which is a self-correction mechanism independent of changes in circulating vasopressin. This matches option A.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 228, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 300}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2513", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When broad-spectrum antibiotics are administered with coumarin anticoagulants, the anticoagulant action may be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Reduced because of enhanced hepatic drug metabolism\nB. Reduced because of increased protein-binding\nC. Increased because of reduction of vitamin 'K' sources\nD. Increased because of decreased renal excretion of the anticoagulant\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C** because broad-spectrum antibiotics can reduce intestinal vitamin K\u2013producing bacteria, lowering vitamin K levels and thereby enhancing the effect of coumarin anticoagulants.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 134, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 179}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2671", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One day after complete mouth extraction, blue black spots are seen on the neck of the patients. These spots indicate:\n\nOptions: \nA. Thrombocytopenic purpura\nB. Postoperative ecchymosis\nC. Impaired blood circulation\nD. Cellulitis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely answer is **B. Postoperative ecchymosis**, because blue-black spots appearing shortly after an invasive procedure like multiple tooth extractions are typically due to bruising from bleeding into the subcutaneous tissues, which is common postoperatively.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 199}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2692", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Excess of plasma level of lignocaine can cause cardiovascular collapse due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Myocardial depression\nB. Vagal stimulation\nC. Syncope\nD. CN5 excitability\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Excess lignocaine (lidocaine) plasma levels primarily cause cardiovascular collapse through direct myocardial depression, leading to decreased cardiac output and hypotension. Vagal stimulation, syncope, and trigeminal (CN5) excitability are not the primary mechanisms for cardiovascular collapse in lignocaine toxicity.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 200}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2699", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Deepening the pulpal floor during cavity preparation\nprovides for\n\nOptions: \nA. Outline form\nB. Retention form\nC. convenience form\nD. Resistance form\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Deepening the pulpal floor during cavity preparation primarily enhances the cavity's ability to withstand occlusal forces, which is a key aspect of resistance form. While it may contribute to other forms, the main purpose is to ensure the restoration does not fracture under pressure. Therefore, the best match among the options is resistance form.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 198}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2717", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The instrument shown in fig is used for\n\nOptions: \nA. Rapid separation\nB. Slow separation\nC. Not used for separation\nD. Depends on force for separation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The figure likely shows a centrifuge or similar device used for separation based on force. Since centrifuges achieve **rapid separation** using centrifugal force, the best match is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 139}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2726", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Low apparent volume of distribution of drug indicates that:\n\nOptions: \nA. Drug has low half life\nB. Drug has low bioavailability\nC. Drug has low efficacy\nD. Drug is not extensively distributed to tissue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because a low apparent volume of distribution means the drug remains largely within the plasma and is not widely distributed into tissues.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2760", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Thiamine deficiency decreases cellular metabolism because:\n\nOptions: \nA. Thiamine is a coenzyme for pyruvate dehydrogenase and alfa-ketoglutarate dehydrogenases\nB. Activity of transketolase is inhibited\nC. It is required for the process of transamination\nD. It is a cofactor in oxidative reduction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Thiamine deficiency impairs cellular metabolism primarily because thiamine pyrophosphate (TPP) is a coenzyme for key enzymes in energy production, including pyruvate dehydrogenase and alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase in the Krebs cycle. While transketolase activity is also reduced in deficiency, the most direct and broad impact on cellular metabolism comes from disrupted carbohydrate metabolism and ATP generation via these dehydrogenase complexes.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 267}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_276", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A temporary bridge constructed from a synthetic resin\n\nOptions: \nA. Is not required when the missing tooth is provided on a partial denture\nB. Should be cemented with a polycarboxylate cement to ensure retention between the preparation and fitting stages\nC. Should have the same buccal and lingual contours as the permanent bridge\nD. Should restore the occlusion to the same extent as the permanent bridge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because a temporary bridge must maintain proper occlusal function and prevent tooth movement just as the permanent restoration will.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 173, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 219}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1644", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When length of a spring is doubled, the effect is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Doubled\nB. Four times\nC. Six times\nD. Eight times\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The force constant \\( k \\) of a spring is inversely proportional to its length when the material and cross-section are unchanged. If the length is doubled, the spring constant becomes half, but the question asks for the effect when length is doubled \u2014 likely referring to the effect on the spring constant or stored energy for a given displacement. For a given force, the extension would double (so effect is doubled), but if considering energy stored for a given force, it would be four times.  \nGiven typical physics problems, the most common answer is that the effect (on extension for a given force) is doubled.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 223}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1513", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of following will happen with a flexible major connector:\n\nOptions: \nA. It will make other components more effective\nB. Will cause PDL destruction of abutment teeth\nC. Cause ill-fitting of RPD\nD. Will cause difficulty in occlusion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A flexible major connector in a removable partial denture (RPD) lacks rigidity, which can lead to movement and trauma to the abutment teeth, resulting in periodontal ligament (PDL) destruction.  \n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is:  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 142, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2252", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If we know the value of one variable in an individual and wish to know the value of another variable, we calculate -\n\nOptions: \nA. Coefficient of correlation\nB. Coefficient of regression\nC. SE of mean\nD. Geometric mean\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When predicting the value of one variable from another, the appropriate measure is the **coefficient of regression**, as it provides the equation for such predictions.  \n\nThe correlation coefficient measures association strength but does not predict specific values, while the SE of the mean and geometric mean are not used for prediction between variables.  \n\n**Correct choice:**  \n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 225}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1632", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an animal model, the phenomenon of vasomotor reversal of dale can be demonstrated by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Stimulation of alpha-1 followed by stimulation of beta-2\nB. Block of alpha-1 followed by stimulation of beta-2\nC. Stimulation of alpha-1 followed by block of beta-2\nD. Stimulation of beta-1 receptor followed by block of beta-2 receptor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because vasomotor reversal of Dale involves initial \u03b1\u2081-adrenergic stimulation causing vasoconstriction, followed by \u03b2\u2082-adrenergic stimulation leading to vasodilation once \u03b1-receptors are saturated or less responsive.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 157, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 221}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2019", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In case of addition silicones what should be done for better cast\n\nOptions: \nA. Apply ketone over tray\nB. Apply chloroform over tray\nC. Add flavouring agent to prevent bad odour\nD. Delay pouring of cast\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For addition silicones (polyvinyl siloxanes), delaying pouring of the cast allows for complete polymerization and reduces distortion from trapped volatile byproducts.  \nTherefore, the best practice is to wait before pouring.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2515", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a reaction substrate is available in a concentration that is l000times the Km value of the enzyme. After 9 minutes of reaction, l7o substrate is conveed to product (12 microgram/ml). If the concentration of the enzyme is changed to 1/3 and concentration of substrate is doubled. What is the time taken to conve the substrate into the same amount of product, i.e. I 2microgram/ml?\n\nOptions: \nA. 9 minutes\nB. 4.5 minutes\nC. 27 minutes\nD. 13.5 minutes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Since the substrate concentration is initially much larger than \\(K_m\\), the reaction follows zero-order kinetics with rate proportional to enzyme concentration.  \nHalving the enzyme concentration (to 1/3 of original) would make the rate 1/3 as fast, so to produce the same amount of product, the time needed would be 3 times longer.  \nHowever, doubling the substrate does not change the zero-order rate under these conditions, so the new time is \\(3 \\times 9 = 27\\) minutes.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 185, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 306}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2757", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: X,Y,Z are the ee ions pet meaule..\\\\ and V=-30. If at resting membrane potential (RMP), when there is no net electro genic transfer, what is the value of Z?\n\nOptions: \nA. 20\nB. -20\nC. 80\nD. -80\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We know \\(V = -30\\) at RMP with no net electrogenic transfer, meaning the charge distribution inside vs. outside is balanced.  \nIf \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\) are positive ions and \\(Z\\) negative, the net charge likely requires \\(Z\\) to be negative and sufficient to offset positives.  \nGiven \\(V = -30\\) and common values for RMP in such problems, \\(Z = -80\\) fits to give total neutrality with \\(V\\) fixed.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 230}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1333", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The systolic blood pressure in normal healthy males of age group of 40 \u2014 60 has a normal distribution with a mean of 130 in a sample of 100. People with systolic blood pressure more than 130 will be:\n\nOptions: \nA. 100\nB. 75\nC. 50\nD. 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Since the systolic blood pressure follows a normal distribution with a mean of 130, exactly half of the sample is expected to have a value above the mean.  \nIn a sample of 100, that corresponds to 50 people.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 195}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2003", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate net filtration pressure with the following data: PGC = 42 mm Hg pGC = 12 mm Hg PBC= 16 mm Hg Assume that no proteins were filtered.\n\nOptions: \nA. 34 mm Hg\nB. Data not sufficient\nC. 14 mm Hg\nD. 28 mm Hg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Net filtration pressure (NFP) is calculated as (PGC \u2013 PBC) \u2013 (pGC \u2013 pBC). Since no proteins were filtered, pBC is 0. Using the given values: (42 \u2013 16) \u2013 (12 \u2013 0) = 26 \u2013 12 = 14 mm Hg.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1404", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treatment of choice for erythrodermic psoriasis:\n\nOptions: \nA. Methotrexate\nB. Coicosteroids\nC. Coal tar topical\nD. Topical steroids\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The treatment of choice for erythrodermic psoriasis is typically a systemic agent like methotrexate to control the widespread inflammation, as topical therapies are insufficient for this severe form.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1791", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increase in the residual mercury in silver amalgam filling can:\n\nOptions: \nA. Cause fracture of the filling\nB. Tarnish and corrosion\nC. Increase the strength\nD. Decrease condensation pressure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Increased residual mercury in silver amalgam weakens the amalgam structure, making it more prone to tarnish and corrosion. It does not increase strength and is unrelated to condensation pressure.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 175}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2072", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treatment of simple endometrial hyperplasia with atypia in 45 yr female:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hysterectomy\nB. Progestin\nC. Mirena\nD. Postmenopausal women\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **A. Hysterectomy** because endometrial hyperplasia with atypia is a premalignant condition with a high risk of progression to endometrial cancer, and definitive surgical management is typically recommended, especially in a 45-year-old who has completed childbearing.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_94", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The number of dental caries cases reported during last 10 years are given below 250, 320, 190, 300, 5000, 100, 260, 350, 320 and 160. The epidemiologist wants to find out average number of caries cases reported in that town for last 10 yrs. The most appropriate average per this data will be\n\nOptions: \nA. Arithmetic mean\nB. Mode\nC. Median\nD. Geometric mean\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data includes an extreme outlier (5000), which would heavily distort the arithmetic mean. The median is less affected by outliers and gives a better central tendency for skewed data.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 161, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 213}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_849", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Insufficient closure of the flasks during packing of denture base resin can result in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Poor colour stability\nB. Less polymerization shrinkage\nC. Increase in vertical dimension\nD. Decrease in vertical dimension\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Insufficient closure of the flasks during packing of denture base resin can allow excess material to escape, leading to a thinner final denture and a **decrease in vertical dimension**.\n\nThe correct answer is: \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1701", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For testing the statistical significance of the difference in heights of school children among three socio economic groups the most appropriate statistical test is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Student's 't' test\nB. Chi-squared test\nC. Paired 't' test\nD. One way analysis of variance (one way ANOVA)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question involves comparing means across **three independent groups**, which requires a test for more than two groups.  \nStudent\u2019s t\u2011test and paired t\u2011test are for one or two groups, and the chi\u2011squared test is for categorical data.  \nOne\u2011way ANOVA is designed specifically for comparing means across three or more independent groups.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 230}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1848", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For testing the statistical significance of the difference in heights of school children -\n\nOptions: \nA. Student's t test\nB. chi-square test\nC. Paired 't' test\nD. ANOVA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate test for comparing mean heights between groups is **ANOVA** if there are more than two groups, or **Student\u2019s t-test** if comparing exactly two groups.  \nSince the question does not specify the number of groups, but \u201cdifference in heights\u201d often implies comparing means across groups, **ANOVA** is the broader choice for multiple groups, while **Student\u2019s t-test** is for two groups.  \nGiven the options, **Student\u2019s t test** (A) is the standard choice for comparing means of two independent groups, which is a common interpretation of this question.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 237}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2441", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The most appropriate method of testing the statistical significance of the differences between means of two groups is\n\nOptions: \nA. Chi square test\nB. Multiple regression analysis\nC. Correlation coefficient analysis\nD. Student test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most appropriate method for comparing the means of two groups is the Student\u2019s t-test, which is specifically designed for that purpose.  \nChi-square tests are for categorical data, multiple regression examines relationships with multiple predictors, and correlation measures association between two continuous variables.  \nThus, the correct choice is the Student test.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 130, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 225}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_585", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Birth weight of a baby can be increased by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Cessation of smoking\nB. Aspirin\nC. Ca++  and vitamin D supplement\nD. Bed rest\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**A. Cessation of smoking** is the most likely correct answer because smoking during pregnancy is a known risk factor for low birth weight, and stopping smoking can help improve fetal growth.  \n\n**B, C, and D** are not well-supported for directly increasing birth weight in a healthy pregnancy: aspirin is used cautiously for specific conditions (like preeclampsia) but not to increase weight; calcium and vitamin D support maternal bone health but don\u2019t directly increase fetal weight; and bed rest is not recommended routinely and may even pose risks.  \n\nThus, the best choice is:  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 148, "total_tokens": 254}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2323", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 10-year boy with dog bite unprovoked comes to you. Appropriate action is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Give cell culture derived vaccine\nB. Withhold vaccine and observe dog for 10 days\nC. Kill dog and send brain for biopsy\nD. No fuher action is necessary\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct action for an unprovoked dog bite in a child is to begin post-exposure prophylaxis with rabies vaccine and also consider rabies immunoglobulin, while observing the dog if possible. However, among the given options, the most appropriate initial step when the dog is available for observation is to start vaccination and observe the dog for 10 days, which matches option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 200}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_472", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Acetyl choline release can be increased from presynaptic membrane by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Blocking voltage gated Na+ channels on presynaptic membrane\nB. Blocking voltage gated Ca+ channels on presynaptic membrane\nC. Blocking voltage gated K+ channels on presynaptic membrane\nD. Blocking voltage gated CI- channels on presynaptic membrane\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Blocking voltage-gated K\u207a channels on the presynaptic membrane would prolong depolarization, allowing more Ca\u00b2\u207a influx and thereby increasing acetylcholine release.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 155, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 204}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1452", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investigator want to know the similarity of the mean peak flow of expiratory rates and non-smokers, light smokers, moderate smokers, & heavy smokers. Which is statistical test of significance:\n\nOptions: \nA. One way ANOVA\nB. Two way ANOVA\nC. Student-t test\nD. Chi square test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The investigator is comparing means across **more than two independent groups** (four smoking categories), so a one-way ANOVA is the appropriate test.  \nA t-test would only compare two groups, and chi-square is for categorical data, not means.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 210}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2595", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a group of 100 people, the average GFR is 85 ml/ min with a standard detion of 25. What is the range for 90% confidence interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 81-89\nB. 80-90\nC. 75-95\nD. 70-100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 90% confidence interval for the mean with \\(n = 100\\) uses \\(Z \\approx 1.645\\).  \nThe standard error is \\(25 / \\sqrt{100} = 2.5\\), so the margin of error is about \\(1.645 \\times 2.5 \\approx 4.11\\).  \nThus the interval is roughly \\(85 \\pm 4.1\\) \u2192 about 80.9 to 89.1, matching option **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 235}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_441", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If 2 Implants of size 4 mm are to be placed in a ridge, what should be the minimum width required in the ridge\n\nOptions: \nA. 14 mm\nB. 15 mm\nC. 17 mm\nD. 18 mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on common implantology guidelines, placing two 4 mm implants requires a minimum ridge width of about **6\u20137 mm per implant**, plus at least 1\u20132 mm of bone on each side of each implant for safety and vascular health.  \nFor two implants with adequate spacing between them and buccal/lingual bone, the total required width is typically **at least 14\u201315 mm**.  \nAmong the options, **15 mm** is the most widely accepted minimum.\n\n**\\boxed{B}**", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 221}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2384", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A pregnant lady develops chickenpox. During which part of her pregnancy will it lead to highest chance of neonatal infection:\n\nOptions: \nA. Last 5 days\nB. 12-16 week\nC. 8-12 week\nD. 16-20 week\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The highest risk of neonatal chickenpox infection occurs when maternal chickenpox develops in the period just before delivery, because the newborn is exposed to the virus without having received sufficient protective maternal antibodies. This is most likely in the last 5 days before delivery through the first 2 days after delivery.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2048", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The occlusal clearance of an onlay is best detected by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Depth cuts\nB. Visual inspection\nC. Wax chew-in\nD. Articulating paper\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The occlusal clearance of an onlay\u2014which refers to verifying there is enough space between the restoration and the opposing teeth\u2014is best detected while the patient is actively simulating biting, so a wax chew-in allows direct assessment of this clearance during function.  \n\nArticulating paper mainly marks contact points after the restoration is nearly seated, not clearance before finalizing the preparation.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2646", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ECG with \"mean\" axis of 90deg. In which lead there would be the maximum voltage of R wave?\n\nOptions: \nA. III\nB. I\nC. aVF\nD. aVL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "With a mean QRS axis of 90\u00b0, the electrical forces are directed most strongly toward the inferior leads. Among the given options, aVF is the inferior lead that would align best with this axis and show the tallest R wave.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1317", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ECG shows a mean axis of 90 degrees. In which of the following would be present the maximum voltage of R wave?\n\nOptions: \nA. III\nB. I\nC. aVF\nD. aVL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The mean axis of 90\u00b0 points directly toward the positive pole of lead aVF, so the R wave will be tallest in that lead.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 144}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1705", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Among a 100 women with average Hb of 10 gm%, the standard deviation was 1, what is the standard error?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.01\nB. 0.1\nC. 1\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The standard error is calculated as the standard deviation divided by the square root of the sample size:  \n\\[\n\\text{SE} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100}} = \\frac{1}{10} = 0.1\n\\]  \nThus, the correct choice is **B**.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1553", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investigator wants to study the association between maternal intake of iron supplements (Yes or No) and birth weights (in gm) of new born babies. He collects relevant data from 100 pregnant women and their newborns. What statistical test of hypothesis would you advise for the investigator in this situation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chi-square test\nB. Unpaired or independent t - test\nC. Analysis of variance\nD. Student t \u2014 test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The outcome (birth weight) is continuous and the exposure (iron supplement intake) is binary, so comparing the means of two independent groups is appropriate.  \nAn unpaired or independent t-test is designed for exactly this situation.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 177, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 238}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1587", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the angle subtended by the largest letter in the Snellen cha on a person's eye who is reading it from a distance of 6 meters?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 minute\nB. 10 minutes\nC. 50 minutes\nD. 60 minutes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The largest letter on a Snellen chart subtends 5 minutes of arc at the standard testing distance (6 meters), and each part of that letter subtends 1 minute. The question asks for the angle subtended by the *largest letter*, which is 5 minutes, so the closest option is 50 minutes (likely a misprint or intended to be 5 minutes).  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 207}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2338", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Height of group of 20 boys aged 10 years was 140 \u00b1 13 cm and 20 girls of same age was 135 cm \u00b1 7 cm. To test the statistical significance of difference in height, test applicable is -\n\nOptions: \nA. X2\nB. Z\nC. t\nD. F\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Since we are comparing the means of two independent groups (boys and girls) with given standard deviations but unknown population variances, and the sample sizes are small (n=20 each), the appropriate test is the **t-test for independent samples**.  \n\nThus, the correct choice is **C**.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 200}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_531", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Craters in interseptal bone are best eliminated by\n\nOptions: \nA. Gingivectomy\nB. Supragingival curettage\nC. Interseptal massage with stimulators\nD. Osseous recontouring\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Craters in interseptal bone are bony defects that cannot be corrected by soft tissue procedures alone; they require reshaping of the bone itself.  \nOsseous recontouring (osteoplasty/ostectomy) is the definitive surgical method to eliminate these defects and restore normal bone architecture.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2029", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The concentration of a negative ion is 100 mMoUL extracellular and 10 mMo1/1 intracellular. What will be the Nernst potential for this ion?\n\nOptions: \nA. --10 mV\nB. +10 mV\nC. --61 mV\nD. +61 mV\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Nernst potential for a negative ion is calculated using the formula \\( E = \\frac{RT}{zF} \\ln \\frac{[C]_{out}}{[C]_{in}} \\).  \nGiven \\( [C]_{out} = 100 \\) mM and \\( [C]_{in} = 10 \\) mM, the ratio is 10.  \nFor a negative ion (z = -1), the sign flips, so \\( E \\approx -61 \\times \\log_{10}(10) = -61 \\) mV.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 199}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_589", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rearrange the sequence of hand washing: a. b. c. d.\n\nOptions: \nA. a,c,d,b\nB. b,c,a,d\nC. d,a,c,b\nD. c,a,b,d\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question cannot be answered because the steps (a, b, c, d) and the sequence to be rearranged are missing from the prompt.  \nWith only the answer choices provided and no context, the correct selection is indeterminable.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1941", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 28 year old eclamptic woman develop convulsions.The first measure to be done is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Give MgSO4\nB. Sedation of patient\nC. Immediate delivery\nD. Care of airway\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In an eclamptic seizure, the immediate priority is to protect the patient from harm, and securing the airway to prevent aspiration is the critical first step. While MgSO4 is the definitive treatment to prevent further seizures, it is administered after stabilizing the airway.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 190}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1663", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After a building collapse, among remnants, a person's length of humerus is 24.5 cm. What is the predicted height of this person?\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 cm\nB. 110 cm\nC. 130 cm\nD. 146 cm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The humerus length can be used to estimate height in forensic anthropology, with formulas differing by sex and population.  \nFor an average adult, a humerus length of 24.5 cm roughly corresponds to a height around 145\u2013150 cm.  \nAmong the options, 146 cm is the closest match.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 192}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_787", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Digoxin is obtained from a plant product and has a half-life of 36 hours. How does this information help us in formulating treatment?\n\nOptions: \nA. To adjust maintenance dose of digoxin required to keep the blood levels within therapeutic range\nB. Intravenous administration in emergency and urgent dosing\nC. Long half-life permits altemate day dosing\nD. It requires a high loading dose to be administered\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**A. To adjust maintenance dose of digoxin required to keep the blood levels within therapeutic range**  \nThe half-life directly determines how often and at what dose a drug must be administered to maintain steady-state therapeutic levels, which is essential for drugs with a narrow therapeutic index like digoxin.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 144, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 208}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1834", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Arch length analysis of a dentition shows a discrepancy of more than 10 mm. This indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. No extraction required if treated at an early age\nB. No extraction required\nC. Extraction of posterior teeth\nD. Proximal stripping\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A discrepancy of more than 10 mm is severe and cannot be resolved by proximal stripping or growth alone; extraction of teeth (typically premolars) is usually required to gain space. Among the options, extraction of posterior teeth is the most appropriate choice.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 199}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_148", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient is administered 200 mg of a drug. 75 mg of the drug is eliminated from the body in 90 minutes. If the drug follows first order kinetics, how much drug will remain after 6 hours?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12.5 mg\nB. 25 mg\nC. 30 mg\nD. 50 mg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**Step 1: Understand half-life from given data.**  \nIf 75 mg of the original 200 mg is eliminated in 90 minutes, then \\(200 - 75 = 125\\) mg remains after 90 minutes.  \nElimination fraction = \\(75/200 = 0.375\\) removed, so fraction remaining = \\(125/200 = 0.625\\).  \n\nFor first-order kinetics,  \n\\( \\text{fraction remaining} = e^{-kt} \\) with \\( t = 1.5 \\) hours.  \n\\( 0.625 = e^{-k \\cdot 1.5} \\) \u2192 solve for \\(k\\).\n\n**Step 2: Find \\( k \\), then calculate amount after 6 hours.**  \nFrom \\(0.625 = e^{-1.5k}\\),  \n\\( -1.5k = \\ln(0.625) \\approx -0.4700\\) \u2192 \\(k \\approx 0.3133 \\, \\text{hours}^{-1}\\).  \n\nAmount after 6 hours:  \n\\( A = 200 \\cdot e^{-0.3133 \\cdot 6} \\approx 200 \\cdot e^{-1.8798} \\approx 200 \\cdot 0.1529 \\approx 30.58 \\, \\text{mg}. \\)  \n\n**Step 3: Match to options.**  \nClosest is \\( \\mathbf{30 \\, \\text{mg}} \\), which is option C.  \n\n**Step 4: Quick check with half-life method.**  \nFrom 200 \u2192 125 in 1.5 hours: half-life?  \nFraction remaining 0.625 \u2192 half-life \\( t_{1/2} \\) found from \\(0.5 = e^{-k t_{1/2}}\\) but let's use \\(125/200 = 0.625\\) after 1.5 hours.  \nCheck time to halve:  \nLet half-life = \\(T\\): after \\(n\\) half-lives \\( (0.5)^n = 0.625 \\) for \\(t=1.5\\) h \u2192 \\(n = \\log_{0.5}(0.625) = \\frac{\\ln 0.625}{\\ln 0.5} \\approx 0.678 \\) half-lives in 1.5 hours, so \\(T \\approx 1.5 / 0.678 \\approx 2.21\\) hours.  \nIn 6 hours, number of half-lives \u2248 \\(6 / 2.21 \\approx 2.714\\).  \nRemaining = \\(200 \\times (0.5)^{2.714} \\approx 200 \\times 0.151 \\approx 30.2\\) mg \u2192 again about 30 mg.\n\nThus correct answer:  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{C}\n\\]", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 585, "total_tokens": 718}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2812", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study is to be conducted with regards to the fat content in the expressed breast milk of pre-term infants as compared to term infants. Which study design is best suited?\n\nOptions: \nA. Case control\nB. Prospective coho\nC. Longitudinal study\nD. Ambispective\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A **prospective cohort** design is best because it allows for measuring fat content over time starting from birth, comparing pre-term and term infants from exposure forward.  \nA longitudinal study is similar but cohort designs are more specific for comparing two groups from a defined start point.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 216}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_643", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Failure of partial dentures due to poor clasp design can best be avoided by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Using stress breakers\nB. Using bar type clasps\nC. Altering tooth contours\nD. Clasping only those teeth with fairly long crowns and normal bone support\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most effective way to avoid failure from poor clasp design is to ensure teeth selected for clasping have adequate crown length and bone support, which provides stability and reduces stress.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2000", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the most preferred route for drug administration in the management of chronic pain\n\nOptions: \nA. Intrathecal\nB. Oral\nC. Subdermal\nD. Intravenous\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The oral route is generally preferred for chronic pain management due to its convenience, safety, and non-invasiveness, which promote patient adherence for long-term therapy.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 142}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_985", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Most accurate and safe method to diagnose ble pregnancy at 6weeks-\n\nOptions: \nA. Doppler assessment of fetal cardiac activity\nB. USG for fetal cardiac activity\nC. Urinary Beta-hCG determination\nD. Per vaginal examination of uterine size corresponding to 6 weeks gestation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**B. USG for fetal cardiac activity**\n\nUltrasound (USG) is the most accurate and safe first-line method to confirm a viable pregnancy at 6 weeks, as it directly visualizes the gestational sac and fetal cardiac activity without invasive risk. Doppler assessment is generally avoided early in pregnancy due to potential bioeffects, and urinary hCG or per vaginal examination alone cannot confirm viability.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 198}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_473", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a JubLeitter arca pith crude bih rate of 211, what would be the expected number of ANC registrations?\n\nOptions: \nA. 60\nB. 80\nC. 100\nD. 120\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Without additional context or a clear relationship between the crude birth rate and ANC registrations, the most reasonable assumption is that a higher birth rate would correspond to higher antenatal care registrations.  \nAmong the options, 100 is a plausible midpoint estimate given a birth rate of 211 per 1000 (if that is the implied rate).  \nThus, the best choice is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 198}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_751", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A child has received full Rabies vaccination in December 2018 and now presented with oozing wound on Great toe and the pet had vaccination also. Next line of management is\n\nOptions: \nA. No vaccine required\nB. RIG + 5 doses of vaccine\nC. 5 doses of vaccines only\nD. 2 doses of Rabies vaccine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on standard post-exposure prophylaxis guidelines, a patient who has completed a full rabies vaccination series previously typically requires only two booster doses (on days 0 and 3) after a new exposure, provided the pet is also vaccinated. Therefore, the correct answer is **D**.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 145, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 219}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2178", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What should be the time of termination of pregnancy of a female with insulin dependent diabetes?\n\nOptions: \nA. 40 weeks\nB. 38 weeks\nC. 37 weeks\nD. 34 weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Pregnancies in women with insulin-dependent diabetes are often terminated earlier to reduce risks of fetal macrosomia, stillbirth, and maternal complications.  \nStandard obstetric guidelines typically recommend delivery at around **37\u201338 weeks** for such patients.  \nThe most specific option among those provided aligns with **38 weeks**.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 169}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2727", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hormone Replacement therapy is not indicated in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hot flashes\nB. Prevention of CAD\nC. Osteoporosis\nD. Vaginal atrophy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hormone replacement therapy is **not** indicated for the prevention of coronary artery disease (CAD). While HRT is used for vasomotor symptoms (hot flashes), osteoporosis prevention, and vaginal atrophy, studies have not shown cardiovascular benefit and it may increase risk in some women.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1829", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sorting a patient of trauma of head injury on basis of need of care and availability of resources\n\nOptions: \nA. Triage\nB. Emergency care\nC. Definitive care\nD. Hospital care\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A. Triage** because triage involves sorting patients based on the severity of their condition and the resources available to prioritize care.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2308", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 27 year primigravida presents with pregnancy induced hypertension with blood pressure of 150/100 mm of Hg at 32 weeks of gestation with no other complications. Subsequently, her blood pressure is controlled on treatment. If there are no complications, the pregnancy should be terminated at:\n\nOptions: \nA. 40 completed weeks\nB. 37 completed weeks\nC. 35 completed weeks\nD. 34 completed weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on typical guidelines for pregnancy-induced hypertension without complications, delivery is often recommended at 37 completed weeks to balance maternal safety and fetal maturity.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 170, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 224}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_554", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A drug X was given continuous intravenous infusion at 1.6 mg/min. The clearance of the drug is 640 mL/min. With a half-life of 1.8 hours, what would be the steady state plasma concentration of drug?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.002 mg/mL\nB. 0.004 trig/mL\nC. 2.88 mg/mL\nD. 3.55 mg/mL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The steady-state concentration \\( C_{ss} \\) for a continuous IV infusion is given by \\( C_{ss} = \\frac{R_0}{Cl} \\), where \\( R_0 \\) is the infusion rate and \\( Cl \\) is clearance.  \nHere, \\( R_0 = 1.6 \\text{ mg/min} \\) and \\( Cl = 640 \\text{ mL/min} \\), so \\( C_{ss} = \\frac{1.6}{640} = 0.0025 \\text{ mg/mL} \\), which matches **0.002 mg/mL** when rounded.  \nThe half-life is not needed for this calculation since clearance is given directly.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 139, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 252}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1612", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the distribution of intraocular pressure (IOP) seen in 100 glaucoma patients has an average 30 mm with an SD of 1, what is the lower limit of the average that can be expected 95% of times -\n\nOptions: \nA. 28\nB. 26\nC. 32\nD. 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for the lower limit of the average IOP expected 95% of the time, which refers to the lower bound of a 95% confidence interval for the mean.  \nGiven mean = 30, SD = 1, sample size \\( n = 100 \\), the standard error is \\( 1 / \\sqrt{100} = 0.1 \\).  \nFor a 95% CI, the lower limit is \\( 30 - 1.96 \\times 0.1 \\approx 29.8 \\), which rounds to about 30, but the closest option below 30 is 28 (allowing for possible interpretation as a one-sided lower bound using a z-value of about 2 for 95% one-sided, but 28 would require a much larger margin).  \n\nGiven the options, 28 is the only plausible lower bound if using a simplified rule (mean \u2212 2\u00d7SE \u2248 30 \u2212 0.2 = 29.8, not matching any option exactly, but 28 is the only one less than 30).  \n\nHowever, if the question meant the lower limit of the **population mean** 95% of the time (one-sided 95% lower confidence bound), \\( 30 - 1.645 \\times 0.1 \\approx 29.84 \\), still not matching options. Possibly they used mean \u2212 2\u00d7SD (not SE) by mistake: \\( 30 - 2\\times1 = 28 \\), which matches option A.  \n\nThus, the intended answer is likely **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 277, "total_tokens": 406}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1539", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: CLED media better than Macconkey media\n\nOptions: \nA. It stimulates growth of Staph and Candida as it is non selective\nB. Inhibits swarming of proteus\nC. Differentiates between Lactose fermenter and non-lactose fermenters\nD. Sodium taurocholate is used as selective agent.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "CLED media is preferred over MacConkey for urine cultures primarily because it inhibits swarming of *Proteus* and supports the growth of a wider range of organisms while maintaining electrolyte balance.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 176}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_605", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sending the parents outside the operatory and threatening the child that they won't be back until he stops crying-is an example of which of the following behavior management techniques:\n\nOptions: \nA. Omission\nB. Negative reinforcement\nC. Positive reinforcement\nD. Modelling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This is an example of **negative reinforcement** because the removal of the parents (an aversive stimulus for the child) is contingent on the child stopping crying, which increases the likelihood of that behavior.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 163}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1016", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is not an obvious advantage of high pressure oxygen through cannula:\n\nOptions: \nA. Bypassing nasopharyngeal dead space\nB. Decreases need for intubation\nC. PEEP\nD. Hot and Humidification of air\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The option that is **not** an obvious advantage of high-pressure oxygen through a cannula is **D. Hot and Humidification of air**, because high-flow nasal cannula systems typically **add** humidification to prevent mucosal drying, but this is a comfort/therapeutic feature rather than an \"obvious advantage\" in the same physiological sense as the others.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 190}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2209", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The logical explanation for the unique anticariogenic property of most silicate cements is:\n\nOptions: \nA. The reduction in enamel solubility due to fluoride uptake by enamel\nB. That beryllium flux is used in silicates\nC. That silicates show very little leakage at the margins of the restoration\nD. Due to the high silica content\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because silicate cements release fluoride, which is taken up by enamel and reduces its solubility, helping to prevent decay.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 154, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 194}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1198", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not a function of guiding plane?\n\nOptions: \nA. Provide one path of insertion and removal of the restoration\nB. Provide stabilizing characteristics against horizontal rotation of denture\nC. Eliminate detrimental strain to abutment teeth during placing or removing restoration\nD. Engage the abutment tooth in such a manner as to resist displacement of restoration away from basal seat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because it describes a function of a retentive clasp arm, not a guiding plane.\n\nGuiding planes are vertical surfaces on abutment teeth that guide the prosthesis during insertion/removal (A), provide stabilization against rotation (B), and reduce detrimental lateral forces (C). However, they do not actively engage the tooth to resist displacement away from the tissues\u2014that is the role of retentive undercuts and clasps.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 137, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 236}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1809", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Stress breakers are not used in partial denture construction because:\n\nOptions: \nA. They are expensive\nB. Increase the vertical dimension\nC. They are difficult to design and fabricate\nD. Harmful effect on the abutment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **D** because stress breakers can lead to harmful torque and lateral forces on abutment teeth, which may cause mobility or damage over time.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 172}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_877", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When it is made up of same steel, size 55, which will be more prone to fracture:\n\nOptions: \nA. Triangular reamer\nB. Rhomboid cross section file\nC. Square cross section file\nD. Headstrom file\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Among tools of the same steel and size, a thinner cross-section or more acute shape tends to be more fragile.  \nA triangular reamer has a relatively slender, pointed shape with less material supporting its edges compared to the more robust files.  \nTherefore, the triangular reamer is most prone to fracture.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 178}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1841", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Repeated fracture of a porcelain fused to metal restoration is primarily due to\n\nOptions: \nA. Occlusal trauma\nB. Inadequately designed framework\nC. Improper firing schedule\nD. Failure to use metal conditioner\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Repeated fracture of a porcelain fused to metal restoration is most often caused by an underlying structural issue with the metal framework, such as insufficient support or improper design, which leads to stress concentration in the porcelain. While occlusal trauma can contribute, it is usually not the primary cause if fractures are recurring.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 217}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1446", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sequential arrangement question on JVP. Staing with \"a\" wave. A-First hea sound B-T wave C-R wave D-Rapid ejection phase\n\nOptions: \nA. A,B,C,D\nB. A,C,D,B\nC. C,A,D,B\nD. D,C,B,A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"a\" wave of the jugular venous pulse (JVP) corresponds to atrial contraction, which occurs just before the first heart sound and the R wave on the ECG. The correct sequence is: a wave \u2192 R wave (ECG) \u2192 rapid ejection phase \u2192 T wave. This matches option **B: A, C, D, B**.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 187}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1914", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A properly designed rest on lingual surface of a canine is preferred to a rest on incisal surface because:\n\nOptions: \nA. Less Leverage is exerted against the tooth by Lingual rest\nB. Enamel is thicker on lingual surface\nC. Visibility and access is better on lingual surface\nD. The cingulum of canine produces a naturalsurface for recess\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because the cingulum of the canine provides a natural, rounded prominence that is ideal for preparing a stable rest seat, unlike the incisal edge which is more prone to unfavorable leverage.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 156, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 213}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_777", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a village, despite of health education for oral cancer, people don't follow instructions even after referral with persuasive reminders, people are still reluctant. It best fits under which model:\n\nOptions: \nA. Trans-theoretical model\nB. Health belief model\nC. Social compliance\nD. Public health model\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The scenario describes a failure to adopt recommended health behaviors despite education and reminders, which aligns with the **Health Belief Model** because it focuses on perceived barriers and lack of threat perception influencing behavior change.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 213}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_208", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following does not require 5'capping?\n\nOptions: \nA. tRNA of alanine\nB. mRNA for histone\nC. U6 snRNA\nD. siRNA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The molecule that does not require a 5' cap is **tRNA of alanine** because tRNAs already have a different 5' end structure and function in translation without capping, unlike mRNA or some snRNAs which undergo capping for stability or processing.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_326", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When a dentist says that \" I cannot fix your teeth if you do not open your mouth wide:\" He is employing:\n\nOptions: \nA. Problem ownership.\nB. Voice control\nC. Tolerance.\nD. Flexibility.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The dentist is stating a clear, direct condition for cooperation, which is a form of **voice control**\u2014using tone and clarity to guide behavior.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_298", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is having Maximum buffering capacity\n\nOptions: \nA. Histidine\nB. Cysteine\nC. Tyrosine\nD. Arginine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Histidine has the pKa of its side chain (imidazole group) near physiological pH (around 6.0), allowing it to act as an effective buffer in biological systems. The other amino acids listed have side-chain pKa values farther from physiological pH, making them less effective buffers in that range. Therefore, histidine has the maximum buffering capacity among the options.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 197}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sensitivity in gingival area of class II light cured composite restoration after 2 months is due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Improper cavity preparation at gingival margin\nB. Curing from occlusal area only\nC. Addition of resin in multiple increments\nD. Curing from buccal and lingual aspect\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause is incomplete curing at the gingival margin due to inadequate light exposure, which occurs when curing only from the occlusal aspect. This can leave the gingival portion under-polymerized, leading to post-operative sensitivity.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 142, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 207}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_515", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Thirty-eight children consumed eatables procured from a single source at a picnic party. Twenty children developed abdominal cramps followed by vomiting and watery diarrhea 6-10 hours after the party. The most likely etiology for the outbreak is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Rotavirus infection\nB. Enterotoxigenic E.coli infection\nC. Staphylococcal toxin\nD. Clostridium perfringens infection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The timing of 6\u201310 hours after consumption and symptoms of abdominal cramps, vomiting, and watery diarrhea points toward a bacterial toxin that acts rapidly, such as **Staphylococcal toxin** (often from preformed toxin in food).  \n\nCorrect choice: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 196}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_663", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following structures is not of ectodermal origin:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hunter-schreger bands\nB. Enamel spindles\nC. Enamel tufts\nD. Enamel lamellae\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Enamel lamellae are defects or organic inclusions within enamel that extend from the enamel surface toward the dentin, but they are not formed from ectodermal tissue during tooth development. Hunter-Schreger bands, enamel spindles, and enamel tufts are structural features of enamel itself, which is ectodermally derived.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 181}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_133", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The necrotising pressure areas, undergoing bone resorption and endosteal bone formation\n\nOptions: \nA. Juvenile periodontitis\nB. Occlusal trauma\nC. Chronic suppurative periodontitis\nD. ANUG\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description of necrotizing pressure areas with bone resorption and endosteal bone formation is most characteristic of **occlusal trauma**, as it involves bone remodeling due to excessive occlusal forces.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2223", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A woman comes with postdated pregnancy at 42 weeks. The initial evaluation would be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Induction of labour\nB. Review of previous menstrual history\nC. Cesarean section\nD. USG\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The initial step in managing a postdated pregnancy is to confirm gestational age by reviewing menstrual history and performing an ultrasound. Induction or cesarean would be decided after that confirmation.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_59", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increase in height of mandible with increase in interdental spaces in elderly man\n\nOptions: \nA. Hyperpituitarism\nB. Hyperthyroidism\nC. Hypopituitarism\nD. Hyperparathyroidism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described changes\u2014increased mandibular height and interdental spacing\u2014are characteristic of acromegaly, which is caused by **hyperpituitarism** (specifically excess growth hormone in adulthood).  \nThis eliminates the other endocrine disorders listed.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1179", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new method of measuring Haemoglobin levels has been developed. Ten successive readings of a single sample are as follows: 9.4, 10.4, 9.6, 9.1, 10.8, 12.1, 10.1, 9.8, 9.2, 9.5. But the Haemoglobin measured by standard calorimetry was 10.2. Therefore the given method has\n\nOptions: \nA. Low validity, low reliability\nB. High validity, low reliability\nC. High validity, high reliability\nD. Low validity, high reliability\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The readings vary widely (e.g., 9.1 to 12.1) around the true value of 10.2, so reliability (precision) is low. The mean of the readings is about 10.0, close to 10.2, but the high scatter means validity (accuracy) is also compromised.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 188, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 263}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1716", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mass Drug Administration is not helpful for\n\nOptions: \nA. Lymphatic Filariasis\nB. Vitamin A Deficiency\nC. Worm infestation\nD. Scabies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mass Drug Administration (MDA) is a public health strategy used to treat entire populations for certain infectious diseases, regardless of individual infection status. It is commonly employed for diseases like lymphatic filariasis, worm infestations (e.g., soil-transmitted helminths), and vitamin A supplementation programs, but it is not typically used for scabies, which is usually managed through targeted treatment and infection control measures.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 221}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1431", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The probable reasons for a high incidence of dental caries in the teenage population relates most directly to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Rapid growth\nB. Frequency of sucrose intake\nC. Negligence in visiting the dentist\nD. Carelessness in oral hygiene habits\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most direct reason is the frequent consumption of sugary foods and drinks common in teenage diets, which promotes tooth decay. While negligence and poor oral hygiene contribute, the dietary habit is the primary biological factor.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 197}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2754", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Coefficient of thermal expansion of which of following is most similar to that of tooth?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gold inlay\nB. Acrylic resin\nC. Silicate cement\nD. Gold foil\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C. Silicate cement** because its coefficient of thermal expansion is closest to that of tooth enamel and dentin among the options given. Acrylic resin and metals like gold have much higher or mismatched expansion rates.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1923", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is NOT a socio-economic indicator?\n\nOptions: \nA. Literacy rate\nB. Life expectancy at birth\nC. Housing\nD. Family size\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The family size is a demographic measure rather than a direct indicator of socio-economic development, whereas literacy rate, life expectancy, and housing conditions are commonly used socio-economic indicators.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 136}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2482", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During laparoscopic inguinal hernia repair a tacker was accidently placed below and lateral to the ilio-pubic tract. Postoperatively the patient complained of pain and soreness in the thigh. This is due to the involvement of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Lateral cutaneous nerve of thigh\nB. llioinguinal nerve\nC. Genital branch of genitofemoral nerve\nD. Obturator nerve\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The tacker placed below and lateral to the ilio-pubic tract is likely to have injured the **lateral femoral cutaneous nerve**, which runs in that region and supplies sensation to the thigh.  \nThis matches the symptom of thigh pain and corresponds to option A.  \nThe other nerves listed are either more medial or have different sensory distributions.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 161, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 251}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1186", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following change can be done in insulin structure so that there is least change in the function of insulin:\n\nOptions: \nA. Interchange of A1 & A4\nB. Interchange of B29 and B30\nC. Interchange of A5 & A6\nD. Breaking disulphide linkages\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B** because interchanging B29 and B30 (lysine and threonine) is a known modification in insulin analogs that retains biological activity, while the other options involve more disruptive changes to critical structural elements like disulfide bonds or conserved residues.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_568", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It is likely that cell mediated immune reactions (delayed\nhypersensitivity) occur in periodontitis because subjects with periodontitis have\n\nOptions: \nA. High levels of histamine in involved gingival tissue\nB. IgG antibodies reactive with plaque bacterial antigens\nC. Ttymphocytes sensitized to bacterial plaque antigens\nD. High Levels of collagenase in gingival fluids\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C** because cell-mediated immunity involves T-lymphocytes, and in periodontitis, these can become sensitized to bacterial plaque antigens, leading to delayed hypersensitivity reactions.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 145, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2302", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient complains of looseness of dentures within two to four hours of insertion. The most likely cause is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Psychological\nB. Adaptive unresponsiveness\nC. Deflective occlusion\nD. Unretentive denture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause is **deflective occlusion**, which can cause rapid bone resorption or tissue displacement, leading to quick loosening of the denture after insertion.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_733", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Following bilateral mandibular fracture in the canine region, the following muscles will tend to pull the mandible back:\n\nOptions: \nA. Genioglossus and anterior belly of digastric\nB. Genioglossus and mylohyoid\nC. Genioglossus and thyrohyoid\nD. Genioglossus and masseter\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The genioglossus and anterior belly of digastric are both muscles that pull the mandible backward (or depress and retract it) after a fracture in the canine region.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 181}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2494", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following doesn't occur in 5' to 3' direction?\n\nOptions: \nA. DNA repair\nB. DNA replication\nC. RNA editing\nD. Transcription\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "DNA replication, transcription, and DNA repair all involve synthesis of nucleic acids in the 5'\u21923' direction.  \nRNA editing, however, involves modifying existing RNA bases and is not a template-directed synthesis process, so it doesn't have an inherent 5'\u21923' directionality in the same way.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_459", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Renal osteodystrophy differs from nutritional and genetic form of osteomaLacia in having:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hypocalcemia\nB. Hypercalcemia\nC. Hypophosphatemia\nD. Hyperphosphatemia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Renal osteodystrophy is associated with chronic kidney disease, which leads to phosphate retention and **hyperphosphatemia**, unlike nutritional or genetic osteomalacia where hypophosphatemia is more common.  \n\nThe correct answer is:  \n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1704", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a survey of sleep apnea scores among 10 people, the highest sample of 58 was entered by mistake as 85. This will affect the result as:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased mean, decreased median\nB. Increased mean, increased median\nC. Increased mean. no change in median\nD. No change in mean, increased median.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Since the error replaces a value of 58 with a much larger value of 85, the mean will increase.  \nThe median depends on the middle values in the ordered list; unless the mistaken value changes the position of the middle observations, the median will likely stay the same.  \nThus, the correct choice is **C**.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 147, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 226}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2301", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cell membrane of a cell is freely permeable to three ions X, Y and Z. At resting membrane potential, the respective equilibrium potentials of Xand Y are -30mV and -40 mV.What will happen to the membrane potential if a drug is infused which can block the permeability of Z?\n\nOptions: \nA. Depolarisation\nB. Hyperpolarization\nC. No change\nD. Hyperpolarization following repolarization\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The membrane potential is determined by the ions to which the membrane is permeable. Since the membrane is freely permeable to X, Y, and Z at rest, blocking Z\u2019s permeability means the resting potential will now be determined by the equilibrium potentials of X and Y alone. Given their equilibrium potentials are -30 mV and -40 mV, the new steady potential will likely shift toward a value between them, which is more positive (less negative) than -40 mV if Z was contributing to a more negative potential, so depolarization is the most likely outcome.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 147, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 264}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_477", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On rubber dam application gingiva is seen protruding out of margins, it can be seen due to?\n\nOptions: \nA. Edematous gingival tissues\nB. Holes paced too far apart\nC. Using a light-weight dam\nD. Holes placed too close together\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The gingiva protruding out of the margins is most likely due to **holes placed too close together**, which causes the dam to bunch and push the gingival tissue outward.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_48", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following type of failure may occur, if the coefficient of thermal expansion of ceramic is much lower than that of metal?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cohesive failure of ceramic\nB. Adhesive failure of metal ceramic bond\nC. Cohesive failure of metal\nD. Cohesive failure of metal ceramic bond\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "If the ceramic\u2019s coefficient of thermal expansion is much lower than the metal\u2019s, the metal will contract more upon cooling, putting the ceramic under tensile stress and potentially causing it to crack or separate from the bond interface. This is most likely to result in **adhesive failure at the metal-ceramic bond** or cohesive failure within the ceramic, but given the options, adhesive failure of the bond is the direct expected outcome.  \n\n**Correct choice:**  \n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 144, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 263}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1772", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 3 weeks after insertion of distal extension partial denture, the patient reports to the dental clinic with complaint of sensitivity to chewing pressure. The most probable reason would be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Improper occlusion\nB. Abrasion of tooth by clasp\nC. Wearing off the cement base\nD. Passive retentive arm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause is that the cement base under the denture has worn down, leading to direct pressure on the mucosa and underlying bone during chewing. This is a common issue with distal extension partial dentures shortly after insertion as the tissue settles. The other options are less probable for sensitivity to chewing pressure at this early stage.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 149, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 241}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1029", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In leukemia patient, post extraction bleeding doesn't stop because of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased leukocyte count\nB. Increased Ca+ level in blood\nC. Platelet disorder\nD. Deficiency of clotting factors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In leukemia, bleeding issues often arise from thrombocytopenia (low platelet count) or platelet dysfunction, which impairs clot formation. While clotting factor deficiencies can occur in some leukemias, the most direct and common cause of prolonged post-extraction bleeding is a platelet disorder.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 175}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_248", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Wave patterns of EEF, ECG and EMG are depicted below. The B pattern belongs to (Figure was not provided in the exam):\n\nOptions: \nA. NREM sleep\nB. REM sleep\nC. Wakefulness\nD. Quiet wakefulness\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Without the figure, the most likely answer is **B. REM sleep** because REM sleep is characterized by low-amplitude, high-frequency EEG waves similar to an awake state, while ECG and EMG patterns show increased heart rate variability and muscle atonia.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_53", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is most effective for gluconeogenesis in starvation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Acetyl Co-A stimulation of pyruvate carboxylase\nB. Fructose-1, 6-biphosphate stimulation of phosphofructokinase-1\nC. Citrate stimulation of acetyl carboxylase\nD. Fructose-2, 6-biphosphate stimulation of phosphofructokinase-2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A** because during starvation, acetyl Co-A activates pyruvate carboxylase, a key step in converting pyruvate to oxaloacetate for gluconeogenesis.  \nThe other options either promote glycolysis (B and D) or fatty acid synthesis (C), which are not prioritized in starvation.  \nThus, only A supports glucose production when fasting.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 151, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 241}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1287", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Asymptomatic hep B is common in 2-3% normal population, but there is increased risk of transmission into hepatocellular carcinoma. Why?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inability to induce inflammation to remove the organism\nB. High level of transaminases\nC. High rate of proliferation of virus\nD. Integration of viral DNA with host DNA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D** because integration of hepatitis B viral DNA into the host genome can lead to genomic instability and activation of oncogenes, increasing the risk of hepatocellular carcinoma even in asymptomatic cases.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_511", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A lateral sliding flap done on a tooth with roots denuded for 6 years will show\n\nOptions: \nA. PDL fibres attached to cementum\nB. PDL fibres attached to dentin\nC. Epithelium adjacent to previously denuded root surface\nD. Co adaptation to the remaining fibres\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The roots have been denuded for 6 years, meaning the periodontal ligament (PDL) and cementum will not have regenerated, so epithelium will have migrated next to the previously denuded root surface.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_355", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In examining the edentulous mouth of an aged patient wearing complete maxillary denture against six mandibular teeth, the dentist will see:\n\nOptions: \nA. Cystic degeneration of the foramina of the anterior palatine nerve\nB. Loss of osseous structure in the anterior maxilla\nC. Flabby tissue in the posterior region\nD. Decrease interocclusal distance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In an aged patient with a complete maxillary denture opposing only six remaining mandibular anterior teeth, the excessive occlusal forces on the anterior maxilla often lead to **loss of osseous structure in the anterior maxilla** (resorption), which is a classic clinical finding.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 210}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1816", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Child is Evasive and dawdling, what could be the child's mother behavior:\n\nOptions: \nA. Overprotective mother.\nB. Authoritarian mother.\nC. Rejecting mother.\nD. Underaffectionate mother.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on common behavioral patterns, a child who is evasive and dawdling is often responding to an authoritarian parenting style, where strict control leads to avoidance and stalling behaviors.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: GPCR that does not act through opening of potassium channels is?\n\nOptions: \nA. Muscarinic M2 receptor\nB. Dopamine D2 receptor\nC. Serotonin 5 HT1 receptor\nD. Angiotensin 1 receptor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The angiotensin 1 receptor (AT1) acts primarily through Gq proteins, leading to phospholipase C activation and calcium signaling, not through opening potassium channels.  \nMuscarinic M2, dopamine D2, and serotonin 5\u2011HT1 receptors are Gi/o\u2011coupled and can promote potassium channel opening.  \nTherefore, the GPCR that does not act through opening potassium channels is the angiotensin 1 receptor.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 218}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_720", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 60-year-old has got severe bulla and target lesion which erythema around halo and genital lesions:\n\nOptions: \nA. Stevens Jhonson syndrome\nB. Herpes zoster\nC. Herpes simplex\nD. Herpangina\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The presentation of severe bullae, target lesions with erythematous halos, and genital involvement is classic for **Stevens-Johnson syndrome**, a severe mucocutaneous reaction often triggered by medications.\n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 178}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1610", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Insulin resistance is seen in liver disease because of-\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreased secretion of insulin\nB. Hepatic steatosis\nC. Hepatocytedysfunction\nD. Low 'C'peptide level\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Insulin resistance in liver disease is primarily due to impaired insulin signaling and glucose metabolism in the liver, which results from **hepatocyte dysfunction**. Among the options, hepatic steatosis (B) is often a consequence or associated feature, but the fundamental mechanism is dysfunction of liver cells.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1697", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, elevated triglyceride and VLDL levels are seen due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased activity of lipoprotein lipase and decreased activity of hormone sensitive lipase\nB. Increased activity of hormone sensitive lipase and decreased activity of lipoprotein lipase\nC. Increase in peripheral LDL receptors\nD. Increased activity of hepatic lipase\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The elevated triglycerides and VLDL in uncontrolled diabetes stem from increased hormone-sensitive lipase (driving fatty acid release) and decreased lipoprotein lipase activity (reducing triglyceride clearance).  \n\n**Correct choice: B**  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 227}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1269", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vascular event of inflammation in order-a) delayed prolonged- leukocytes mediated injuryb) immediate transient - mast cell activation lead to release of histamine bradykininc) immediate prolonged- direct endothelial injury by bacterial toxind) Somewhat delayed prolonged- sun exposure /heat stroke lead to mild endothelial injury\n\nOptions: \nA. ABCD\nB. DCBA\nC. ACDB\nD. BDCA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on typical inflammation pathophysiology, the correct ordering matches **B. DCBA**, placing immediate transient first and delayed prolonged last.  \n\n**B** is the correct choice.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2687", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The least effect on the prognosis of a periodontal disease is\n\nOptions: \nA. Suppuration from the pocket\nB. Furcation involvement\nC. Alveolar bone loss\nD. Co-operation and motivation of the patient\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Suppuration is a sign of active infection, but it can be resolved with treatment and does not directly dictate the long-term outcome as strongly as factors like patient cooperation or advanced anatomical destruction. Bone loss and furcation involvement indicate disease severity and complexity, which directly affect prognosis. The patient\u2019s cooperation and motivation are critical for long-term success, making suppuration the least determining factor for prognosis among the options.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 197}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_476", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following event has little or no significance?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mandibular incisor erupting before mandibular molar\nB. Mandibular canine erupting before mandibular premolar\nC. Mandibular 2nd premolar erupting before mandibular 2nd molar\nD. Maxillary premolar and canine erupting before maxillary 2nd molar\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The eruption sequence that is least typical and thus has little or no significance as a common normal pattern is **C. Mandibular 2nd premolar erupting before mandibular 2nd molar**, because in typical development, the mandibular second molar usually erupts before the mandibular second premolar.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 204}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2268", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 3 year old girl having delayed milestones, playing with\nherself, difficulty in learning is likely to be suffering from\n\nOptions: \nA. Mental retardation\nB. Autism\nC. Specific Learning Disorder\nD. ADHD\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description suggests core features of autism, such as delayed milestones, self-stimulation (\u201cplaying with herself\u201d), and impaired social/communication learning.  \nWhile mental retardation (intellectual disability) may co-occur, autism specifically fits the pattern given.  \nThus, **B. Autism** is the most likely answer.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_557", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A G2 P1+0+0 diabetic mother present at 32 weeks pregnancy, there is history of full term fetal demise in last pregnancy. Her vitals are stable, sugar is controlled and fetus is stable. Which among the following will be the most appropriate management?\n\nOptions: \nA. To induce at 38 weeks\nB. To induce at 40 weeks\nC. Cesarean section at 38 weeks\nD. To wait for spontaneous delivery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Given the history of prior full-term fetal demise in a diabetic pregnancy, current diabetes, and the increased risk of stillbirth, induction at 38 weeks is recommended to reduce perinatal mortality while balancing neonatal maturity.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 167, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 233}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_797", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the best management of the case shown?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dapsone plus steroids\nB. Stop smoking and screen for cancer\nC. Vitamin supplements\nD. Antifungals for oral candidiasis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the lack of clinical context or image, the most plausible answer is **B** if the implied condition is a smoking-related oral lesion like leukoplakia, which requires smoking cessation and cancer screening.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1041", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is best method to assess fetal damage in a diabetes mother in 1st trimester is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Blood sugar estimation\nB. Urine ketone assay\nC. Amniocentesis to see level of sugar in amniotic fluid\nD. Glycosylated Hb\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Glycosylated Hb (HbA1c) reflects the average blood glucose level over the previous 2\u20133 months, making it the best indicator of glycemic control during the critical first trimester when fetal organs are forming. The other options are not reliable for assessing the risk of fetal damage early in pregnancy.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 211}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1194", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To assess outcome from labour, cost, time\n\nOptions: \nA. Cost benefit\nB. Cost Effectiveness\nC. Cost utility\nD. Risk Benefit\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks about assessing outcome from labour in terms of cost, time, and outcome, which points to comparing costs with outcomes measured in natural units (like time saved).  \nCost-effectiveness analysis is specifically used to compare costs with outcomes measured in natural units, such as time or labor output.  \nTherefore, the most appropriate choice is cost-effectiveness.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1326", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the best index for burden of disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. Case fatality rate\nB. Morbidity data\nC. Dependency ratio\nD. Disability adjusted life years\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The best index for burden of disease is **Disability Adjusted Life Years (DALYs)**, as it combines years of life lost due to premature mortality and years lived with disability into a single measure. Morbidity data and case fatality rate only capture parts of the burden, while dependency ratio is a demographic measure unrelated to disease burden.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1479", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following drugs is least efficacious in the treatment of temporal lobe epilepsy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Phenobarbitone\nB. Phenytoin sodium\nC. Primidone\nD. Carbamazepine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Primidone is metabolized to phenobarbitone, and both are generally less effective for focal seizures like temporal lobe epilepsy compared to carbamazepine or phenytoin. Among the options, phenobarbitone is considered the least efficacious for this condition due to poorer seizure control and more side effects.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 195}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1514", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 50 year male presented with high BP of 160/100 mm Hg and hea rate of 120/min. CECT is shown below. Which is best management of this condition?\n\nOptions: \nA. Surgical repair\nB. LMW heparin\nC. Beta blocker\nD. Vitamin K inhibitors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The CT shows an abdominal aortic aneurysm with a dissection flap, likely causing secondary hypertension and tachycardia. The best immediate management is to lower heart rate and blood pressure to prevent extension of the dissection, which is achieved with a **beta blocker**.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 206}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1547", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In fracture of atrophic mandible with bone loss, what is the best treatment modality?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bone grafting and load bearing\nB. Bone grafting and load sharing\nC. Semi-rigid fixation\nD. IMF with open reduction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The best treatment for an atrophic mandible fracture with bone loss typically requires both bone grafting to restore continuity and rigid fixation to bear the load due to poor bone stock.  \nAmong the options, **bone grafting and load bearing** (A) most accurately describes this approach, as load-bearing plates provide stability independent of bone contact.  \nSemi-rigid fixation or IMF alone would be insufficient given the lack of bony support.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_1861", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Routine examination of a 17 years old asymptomatic boy reveals sho PR interval, and delta wave on ECG. The least effective measure for the boy would be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hotter monitoring\nB. Treadmill stress test\nC. Beta blocker\nD. Reassurance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ECG findings describe Wolff-Parkinson-White (WPW) syndrome, which is often asymptomatic. In asymptomatic individuals, reassurance and regular follow-up are typically recommended, while treatments like beta blockers are not indicated unless symptoms occur. Among the options, beta blocker would be the least effective measure in this asymptomatic case.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2010", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is the best study to evaluate effect and outcome?\n\nOptions: \nA. Clinical trial\nB. Coho\nC. Case control study\nD. Cross sectional study\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The best study to evaluate effect and outcome is typically a clinical trial, as it can establish causality by prospectively comparing interventions. The other options are observational studies that are less suited for determining direct effects.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2065", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the least important prognostic factor in congenital diaphragmatic hernia ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pulmonary Hypertension\nB. Delay in emergent surgery\nC. Size of defect\nD. Gestational age at diagnosis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The least important prognostic factor among the options is **B. Delay in emergent surgery**, as current management prioritizes medical stabilization before surgery, making surgical timing less critical than the other physiological and anatomical factors listed.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2296", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is the most reliable method for monitoring fluid resuscitation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Urine output\nB. CVP\nC. Pulse rate\nD. Blood pressure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Urine output is the most reliable indicator of adequate organ perfusion and effective fluid resuscitation.  \nWhile CVP, pulse rate, and blood pressure can be useful, they are less direct measures of renal perfusion and fluid status.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 146}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2425", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 29-year-old, 4 months pregnant primigravida has history of juvenile myoclonic epilepsy. She has been regularly taking sodium valproate and now presents requesting for an opinion for a change in her anti-epileptic treatment. What would you sugeets her?\n\nOptions: \nA. Immediately taper off valproate and sta lamotrigine\nB. Switch to carbamazepine\nC. Continue valproate and serial drug monitoring in blood\nD. Add lamotrigine to valproate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The safest approach is to switch from valproate due to its high teratogenic risk, but an abrupt change or adding another drug is not ideal. Lamotrigine is often preferred in pregnancy for focal epilepsy, but juvenile myoclonic epilepsy is generalized, so carbamazepine is not the best choice either. The most appropriate option is to gradually transition to a safer alternative like lamotrigine under close supervision, which aligns with option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 175, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 273}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MedMCQA_2467", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following can be used to delay preterm contractions of uterus with best neurological outcome for the fetus?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mgso4\nB. Nifidipine\nC. Ritodrine\nD. Isoxprine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on current obstetric guidelines, magnesium sulfate is used for neuroprotection to reduce the risk of cerebral palsy in preterm infants, in addition to its tocolytic effect.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_120", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What kind of train was Stepney, a train on the Bluebell Railway notable for his appearance in \"The Railway Series\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. LB&SCR A1X\nB. LB&SCR J1\nC. LB&SCR E2\nD. LB&SCR D1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stepney is a real locomotive preserved on the Bluebell Railway and is known as an LB&SCR A1X class \"Terrier\" tank engine, which also appears in *The Railway Series*. The other options are different classes not matching Stepney\u2019s identity.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 179}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3704", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What nickname was given to Air Canada Flight 143 after it ran out of fuel and glided to safety in 1983?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gimli Glider\nB. Gimli Microlight\nC. Gimli Superb\nD. Gimli Chaser\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct nickname is \u201cGimli Glider,\u201d which refers to the incident where the Boeing 767 ran out of fuel and the pilots glided it to an emergency landing at a former airbase in Gimli, Manitoba.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 172}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1602", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following collision avoidance systems helps airplanes avoid colliding with each other?\n\nOptions: \nA. TCAS\nB. TAWS\nC. GPWS\nD. OCAS\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "TCAS (Traffic Alert and Collision Avoidance System) is specifically designed to help aircraft avoid mid-air collisions with other aircraft. The other systems, such as TAWS (terrain), GPWS (ground), and OCAS (not a standard aviation acronym), serve different purposes. Therefore, the correct choice is TCAS.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 177}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3934", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Japanese Shinkansen beat the French TGV's speed record for fastest electric rail train.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The French TGV holds the world speed record for conventional electric trains at 574.8 km/h, set in 2007, while the Japanese Shinkansen\u2019s top test speed is lower. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3397", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The difference between the lengths of a Boeing 777-300ER and an Airbus A350-1000 is closest to:\n\nOptions: \nA. 10m \nB. 100m\nC. 1m\nD. 0.1m\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A Boeing 777-300ER is about 73.9 m long, and an Airbus A350-1000 is about 73.79 m long. The difference is approximately 0.11 m, which is closest to 0.1 m.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 173}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_4026", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Arriva is owned by the Deutsche Bahn.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Arriva is a British transport company that was acquired by Deutsche Bahn in 2010 and remained under its ownership until its sale in 2023. Therefore, within the context of general knowledge and the time frame before its sale, the statement is considered true.\n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_991", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1993 Swedish car manufacturer Saab experimented with replacing the steering wheel with a joystick in a Saab 9000.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This is true; Saab did test a joystick-controlled prototype called the Saab 9000 Prometheus in the early 1990s.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3396", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2014, over 6 million General Motors vehicles were recalled due to what critical flaw?\n\nOptions: \nA. Faulty brake pads\nB. Faulty ignition switch\nC. Breaking fuel lines\nD. Malfunctioning gas pedal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The recall involved ignition switches that could inadvertently turn off the engine and disable airbags while driving. This flaw was linked to numerous fatalities and injuries.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_645", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What part of an automobile engine uses lobes to open and close intake and exhaust valves, and allows an air/fuel mixture into the engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drive shaft\nB. Piston\nC. Camshaft\nD. Crankshaft\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The camshaft is the component with lobes (cams) that actuate the valves to control intake and exhaust in an engine.  \nThe other options\u2014drive shaft, piston, and crankshaft\u2014do not perform this valve-timing function.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 178}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2541", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What UK Train does NOT go over 125MPH?\n\nOptions: \nA. Javelin\nB. Class 43\nC. Sprinter\nD. Pendolino\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Sprinter is a family of diesel multiple units used primarily on regional and local routes, with a top speed of around 75\u201390 mph, well below 125 mph. The other options (Javelin, Class 43, Pendolino) are all capable of speeds at or above 125 mph. Therefore, the correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 169}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_471", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The snowmobile was invented by Canadian Joseph-Armand Bombardier in 1937.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The snowmobile was indeed invented by Joseph-Armand Bombardier, a Canadian, who patented his first snowmobile design in 1937.  \nTherefore, the statement is true.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 140}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_673", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Chevrolet Corvette has always been made exclusively with V8 engines only.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because the first generation of the Chevrolet Corvette (C1) was initially offered with an inline-six engine before V8s became available. Therefore, the Corvette has not always been made exclusively with V8 engines.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 145}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2597", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the cylinder-like parts that pump up and down within the engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Leaf Springs\nB. Pistons\nC. ABS\nD. Radiators\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Pistons are the cylindrical components that move up and down inside the engine cylinders to generate power.  \n\nThe correct answer is **B**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 131}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2719", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following countries has officially banned the civilian use of dash cams in cars?\n\nOptions: \nA. Austria\nB. United States\nC. South Korea\nD. Czechia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Austria has strict privacy laws that generally prohibit the use of dash cams by civilians without meeting stringent conditions, effectively banning their routine use. The other listed countries either allow dash cams or have more permissive regulations regarding their use.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 183}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3718", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What do the 4 Rings in Audi's Logo represent?\n\nOptions: \nA. Main cities vital to Audi\nB. States in which Audi makes the most sales\nC. Previously independent automobile manufacturers\nD. Countries in which Audi makes the most sales\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The four rings in Audi\u2019s logo symbolize the four founding companies of Auto Union: Audi, DKW, Horch, and Wanderer, which were previously independent automobile manufacturers.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 180}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_601", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The General Motors EV1 was the first street-legal production electric vehicle.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The EV1 was a production electric vehicle, but it was not the first street-legal one; earlier examples like the Baker Electric existed in the early 1900s.  \nTherefore, the statement is false.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_509", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ferrari has never made a V10 engine for any of its cars.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ferrari has produced V10 engines, most notably for their Formula 1 cars in the early 2000s and for the Ferrari F2008 (though that was a V8). They have also used V10s in concept cars like the Ferrari Mythos. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2548", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Volkswagen's legendary VR6 engine has cylinders positioned at what degree angle?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15 Degree\nB. 45 Degree\nC. 90 Degree\nD. 30 Degree\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The VR6 engine uses a narrow-angle V design, with the cylinders set at a 15-degree angle to allow for a more compact size compared to traditional V6 engines.  \nThis unique configuration helps it fit in engine bays designed for inline engines.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_132", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When BMW was established in 1916, it was producing automobiles.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "B. False\n\nBMW was originally founded in 1916 to manufacture aircraft engines, not automobiles; the company began producing cars much later, in 1928.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 118}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3234", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Variable Valve Timing technology is used by BMW?\n\nOptions: \nA. VANOS\nB. MultiAir\nC. VVT-iw\nD. VVEL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "BMW uses VANOS for its Variable Valve Timing system, which is a well-known technology specific to the brand. The other options are associated with different manufacturers: MultiAir (Fiat/Chrysler), VVT-iw (Toyota), and VVEL (Nissan). Therefore, the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2087", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: BMW M GmbH is a subsidiary of BMW AG that focuses on car performance.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "BMW M GmbH (originally BMW Motorsport GmbH) is indeed the subsidiary responsible for high-performance versions of BMW vehicles.  \nThis makes the statement accurate.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1743", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following passenger jets is the longest?\n\nOptions: \nA. Boeing 787-10\nB. Airbus A330-200\nC. Airbus A350-1000\nD. Boeing 747-8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Airbus A350-1000 is the longest among these options at about 73.79 meters, slightly longer than the Boeing 747-8 (76.3 meters is often cited but includes a longer upper deck; overall fuselage length is about 76.25 m for the 747-8, but the A350-1000 is typically considered the longest passenger jet by overall length in direct comparisons). However, reliable aviation sources list the A350-1000 as the longest, followed closely by the 747-8, with the 787-10 and A330-200 being shorter.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 235}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1879", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Audi does not use Haldex based all wheel drive system?\n\nOptions: \nA. Audi TT\nB. Audi S3\nC. Audi A3\nD. Audi A8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Haldex all-wheel drive system is typically used in Audi's transverse-engine models like the TT, S3, and A3. The Audi A8, with its longitudinal engine layout, generally uses the Torsen-based quattro system instead. Therefore, the A8 does not use a Haldex-based system.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3606", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How much horsepower is produced by the SD40-2 Locomotive?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2,190\nB. 2,578\nC. 3,000\nD. 3,200\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The SD40-2 locomotive is a well-known diesel-electric model from EMD, and its rated horsepower is 3,000. Among the options, that corresponds to choice C.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 139}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_279", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When was Cadillac founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1985\nB. 1898\nC. 1964\nD. 1902\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": 