 (inspired by \"Golden Wind\" but also linked to music references generally), and Johnny Joestar is named after the song \"Johnny B. Goode\" (1958). Since Josuke\u2019s reference is to a song from 1986, which is later than 1980, he is the one who does **not** reference a band, artist, or song earlier than 1980.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 162, "total_tokens": 291}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_4061", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does the character Dragowizard, Qinus Axia's from the anime \"Buddyfight\" differ between the Japanese and English dubs?\n\nOptions: \nA. Different Appearance\nB. Different Body Proportions\nC. Different Backstory\nD. Different Gender\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on Buddyfight lore, Dragowizard, Qinus Axia undergoes a significant change in the English dub where his gender is altered from male to female.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1103", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the  Rossini opera, what was the name of 'The Barber of Seville'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Angelo\nB. Fernando\nC. Figaro\nD. Dave\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation o