in 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The British term for a 64th note is \"hemidemisemiquaver.\"  \nA \"semiquaver\" is a 16th note, and a \"demisemiquaver\" is a 32nd note.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1718", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of Rivers Cuomo's wife?\n\nOptions: \nA. Kyoko Ito\nB. Kyary Pamyu Pamyu\nC. LiSA\nD. Yoko Ono\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Rivers Cuomo, the lead singer of Weezer, is married to Kyoko Ito.  \nKyary Pamyu Pamyu, LiSA, and Yoko Ono are other Japanese celebrities but not his wife.  \nTherefore, the correct answer is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3068", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Saxophone is a brass instrument.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A saxophone is made of brass, but it is classified as a woodwind instrument because it uses a reed to produce sound. Therefore, the statement that it is a brass instrument is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 129}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1600", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these Johns was murdered by gunshots outside the Dakota in New York in 1980?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Denver\nB. John Lennon\nC. Johnny Thunders\nD. John Cascella\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Lennon was shot and killed outside the Dakota apartment building in New York City on December 8, 1980. The other individuals listed either died differently or at other times. Therefore, the correct answer is John Lennon.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 172}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3412", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the American rapper Nelly, what should you do when its hot in here?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drink some water\nB. Take a cool shower\nC. Go skinny dipping\nD. Take off all your clothes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D, as Nelly\u2019s 2002 song \u201cHot in Herre\u201d famously includes the lyric \