sted members.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_2223", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many strings are there on a cello?\n\nOptions: \nA. 8\nB. 6\nC. 5\nD. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A standard cello has four strings, which are typically tuned to C, G, D, and A.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 28, "total_tokens": 117}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3818", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: IMAX stands for Image Maximum.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect because IMAX actually stands for \"Image Maximum\" is a common misconception; the official meaning is not an acronym but a brand name derived from \"maximum image.\"  \nTherefore, the correct answer is that the given statement is false.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 154}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3947", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The World Chess Championship in Chess, Act 1 is set in which Italian city?\n\nOptions: \nA. Milan\nB. Merano\nC. Venice\nD. Rome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The World Chess Championship in *Chess, Act 1* is set in Merano, Italy, as depicted in the musical.  \nThis location is part of the storyline involving the chess match between the American and Soviet challengers.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3875", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist's names in 'Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf', George and Martha, were derived from George Washington and his wife.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The names George and Martha in *Who\u2019s Afraid of Virginia Woolf* are indeed an allusion to George and Martha Washington, which is a well-known fact about the play.  \nTherefore, the statement is true.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 163}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3672", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Jeff Wayne's Musical Version of War of the Worlds, the chances of anything coming from Mars are...\n\nOptions: \nA. A trillion to one\nB. A million to one\nC. A hundred to one\nD. A billion to one\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **\"A million to one\"**, as this is the exact lyric from the song \"The Eve of the War\" in Jeff Wayne's musical.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3001", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the play Oedipus Rex, Oedipus kills his father due to jealousy in loving his mother.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because Oedipus kills his father Laius unknowingly during a roadside quarrel, not out of jealousy over his mother. The prophecy and fate drive the tragedy, not deliberate jealousy.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1327", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Macbeth, the eyes of what animals were used in the Witches' cauldron?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sharks\nB. Squids\nC. Humans\nD. Newts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The line from *Macbeth* is \"Eye of newt, and toe of frog,\" so newts are the animal specified.  \nThe other options (sharks, squids, humans) are not mentioned in the Witches' cauldron ingredients.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 154}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1861", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is Jean ValJean's first prisoner number?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1729\nB. 9430\nC. 32769\nD. 24601\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Les Mis\u00e9rables*, Jean Valjean's first prisoner number is 24601.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 25, "total_tokens": 120}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_407", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who played \"Charlie Price\" in the musical \"Kinky Boots\" on Broadway in New York from May 26th - Aug 6th 2017?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dallon Weekes\nB. Tom Cruise\nC. Ed Sheeren\nD. Brendon Urie\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The role of Charlie Price in *Kinky Boots* on Broadway during that period was played by Brendon Urie, who is known as the lead singer of Panic! at the Disco. The other options are not associated with that Broadway role.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 175}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2864", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Les Mis\u00e9rables, who is Prison Code 24601?\n\nOptions: \nA. Javert\nB. Jean Valjean\nC. Jean Claude Van Damme\nD. Marius Pontmercy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jean Valjean is the character identified by the prisoner number 24601 in *Les Mis\u00e9rables*.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 136}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_4088", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the lyrics for Leonard Bernstein's 1957 Brodway musical West Side Story?\n\nOptions: \nA. Oscar Hammerstein\nB. Himself\nC. Stephen Sondheim\nD. Richard Rodgers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stephen Sondheim wrote the lyrics for *West Side Story*, while Leonard Bernstein composed the music. The musical's book was written by Arthur Laurents.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 144}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1925", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Doctor Who\" star David Tennant performed in a rendition of which Shakespearean play?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Taming of the Shrew\nB. Hamlet\nC. Othello\nD. The Tempest\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "David Tennant is well known for playing Hamlet with the Royal Shakespeare Company in 2008, a performance that was also filmed for television. This makes it the most direct and correct association among the options. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2137", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these musicals won the Tony Award for Best Musical?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Color Purple\nB. American Idiot\nC. Rent\nD. Newsies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Tony Award for Best Musical winners among the options are *Rent* (1996) and *Newsies* (2012). *The Color Purple* and *American Idiot* were nominated but did not win. Since only one answer is requested, the most likely intended choice from common knowledge is *Rent*, as it is the more iconic and earlier winner.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 184}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2941", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the award winning musical \"In The Heights\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Phillips Sousa\nB. Lin-Manuel Miranda\nC. Francis Scott Key\nD. Steven Sondheim\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lin-Manuel Miranda is the creator of the musical *In the Heights*, for which he wrote the music and lyrics. The other composers listed are not associated with this award-winning show.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1614", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was George Bizet's last opera?\n\nOptions: \nA. Les p\u00eacheurs de perles\nB. Gris\u00e9lidis\nC. Carmen\nD. Don Rodrigue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Georges Bizet's last opera was *Carmen*, which premiered in 1875, the year of his death.  \nThe other operas were either earlier works or not by Bizet.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 140}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_830", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After England, more Shakespeare plays are set in this present day country than in any other.\n\nOptions: \nA. United States\nB. Greece\nC. Italy\nD. France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shakespeare set many of his plays in Italy, including well-known works like *Romeo and Juliet*, *The Merchant of Venice*, and *Julius Caesar* (set in ancient Rome, part of modern Italy). This makes Italy the correct answer.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_762", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The musical \"Dirty Rotten Scoundrels\" is set in what country?\n\nOptions: \nA. Germany\nB. Sweden\nC. USA\nD. France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\"Dirty Rotten Scoundrels\" is a musical adaptation of the 1988 film, which is set primarily on the French Riviera. The story revolves around con artists operating in a luxurious coastal resort area in southern France. Therefore, the correct country is France.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1269", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Andrew Lloyd Webber musical \"Cats\" is based off a book of poems written by which author?\n\nOptions: \nA. Emily Dickenson\nB. Andrew Lloyd Webber\nC. T.S. Elliot\nD. Robert Frost\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The musical *Cats* is based on T.S. Eliot\u2019s 1939 poetry collection *Old Possum\u2019s Book of Practical Cats*.  \nNone of the other options wrote the source material: Emily Dickinson wrote very different poetry, Andrew Lloyd Webber composed the music, and Robert Frost was an American poet not connected to *Cats*.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 196}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3073", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Shakespeare's play Julius Caesar, Caesar's last words were...\n\nOptions: \nA. Aegri somnia vana.\nB. Et tu, Brute? \nC. Iacta alea est!\nD. Vidi, vini, vici.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most famous and historically cited last words of Caesar in Shakespeare's play are \"Et tu, Brute?\" which translates to \"And you, Brutus?\"  \n\nThis line signifies his shock at seeing his friend Brutus among the assassins.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2132", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which Shakespeare play does the character Marcellus say, \"Something is rotten in the state of Denmark\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Twelfth Night\nB. King Lear\nC. Macbeth\nD. Hamlet\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The line \"Something is rotten in the state of Denmark\" is spoken by Marcellus in **Hamlet**.  \nIt occurs in Act I, Scene 4, as Marcellus, Horatio, and Hamlet encounter the ghost of Hamlet\u2019s father.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is **D**.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 178}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3479", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of following is rude and dishonorable by Klingon standards?\n\nOptions: \nA. Reaching over and taking his meal\nB. Insulting and laughing at him at the dinner table\nC. Punching him and taking his ship station position\nD. Taking his D'k tahg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on Klingon cultural values, the most dishonorable act would be **insulting and laughing at him at the dinner table**, as it is a cowardly attack on honor without facing physical consequences, which Klingons despise.  \nDirect physical challenges like taking a meal, a position, or a weapon through force are more aligned with their aggressive but honorable code.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 233}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_744", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Klingons express emotion in art through opera and poetry.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Klingon culture, as depicted in *Star Trek*, is known for valuing opera and poetry as important artistic expressions, often conveying strong emotions like honor and battle fervor. Therefore, the statement aligns with established lore. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 154}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1666", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Star Trek\", what is the Ferengi's First Rule of Acquisition?\n\nOptions: \nA. Never allow family to stand in the way of opportunity\nB. Greed is Eternal\nC. Never place friendship above profit\nD. Once you have their money, you never give it back. \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**, as the First Rule of Acquisition is famously quoted as \"Once you have their money, you never give it back.\" This rule is explicitly stated in several *Star Trek* episodes, particularly those involving the Ferengi. The other options are also Ferengi rules but are not the first one.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 134, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 214}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_2367", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which British writer wrote for both Doctor Who and Sherlock?\n\nOptions: \nA. Toby Whithouse\nB. Phil Ford\nC. Steven Moffatt\nD. Russell T Davies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Steven Moffat wrote episodes for both *Doctor Who* and *Sherlock*, and he also served as showrunner for both series.  \nThe other writers listed worked on *Doctor Who*, but only Moffat was directly involved with *Sherlock*.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_4094", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Game of Thrones, what continent lies across the Narrow Sea from Westeros?\n\nOptions: \nA. Easteros\nB. Essos\nC. Westereast\nD. Esuntos\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B. Essos**, as it is the continent east of Westeros across the Narrow Sea in the *Game of Thrones* world.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 140}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3308", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Star Trek: The Next Generation\", Data is the only android in existence.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \u201cStar Trek: The Next Generation,\u201d Data is not the only android in existence; other androids appear in various episodes, such as Lore and the androids created by Dr. Soong.  \n**Answer: B. False**  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_2595", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Doctor Who universe, how many times can a time lord normally regenerate?\n\nOptions: \nA. 11\nB. 13\nC. 12\nD. 15\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the classic series of *Doctor Who*, Time Lords were originally limited to 12 regenerations, allowing for 13 incarnations. This was established in the 1976 serial *The Deadly Assassin*.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_99", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Battlestar Galactica (2004), Cylons were created by man as cybernetic workers and soldiers.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**B. False**  \n\nIn the 2004 series, Cylons were created by humans, but they were not originally cybernetic; they were fully mechanical and later evolved into biological forms. The statement is misleading because it omits this key evolution.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 166}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_955", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which state of America was the Fresh Prince of Bel-Air born and raised in?\n\nOptions: \nA. Florida\nB. California\nC. Pennsylvania\nD. New Jersey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Fresh Prince (Will Smith's character) was born and raised in West Philadelphia, which is in Pennsylvania.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3329", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Klingons once had a period of Democracy in their history, they referred to it as the \"Dark Times\".\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because in *Star Trek* lore, Klingons view democracy as a weak and foreign system, and their history does not refer to a democratic period as the \"Dark Times.\"  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_421", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Naruto: Shippuden, which of the following elements is a \"Kekkei T\u014dta?\"\n\nOptions: \nA. Ice Style\nB. Any Doujutsu\nC. Particle Style\nD. Shadow Style\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C. Particle Style** (also known as Dust Release), as it is explicitly identified as a Kekkei T\u014dta in the series, requiring the combination of three nature transformations. The other options are either Kekkei Genkai or not classified as Kekkei T\u014dta.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 179}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1524", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Klingons respect their disabled comrades, and those who are old, injuried, and helpless.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on established *Star Trek* lore, Klingons value strength and combat prowess, often viewing disability or helplessness as dishonorable. Therefore, the statement contradicts typical Klingon cultural values.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_2855", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The fictional movie 'Rochelle, Rochelle' features in which sitcom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Seinfeld\nB. Cheers\nC. Friends\nD. Frasier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The movie *Rochelle, Rochelle* is a recurring fictional film parody in the sitcom *Seinfeld*, often referenced as a melodramatic foreign art film. It does not appear in the other listed sitcoms.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which country does the YouTuber \"SinowBeats\" originate from?\n\nOptions: \nA. England\nB. Scotland\nC. Germany\nD. Sweden\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "SinowBeats is known for creating music primarily in the synthwave/vaporwave genre and has mentioned being from Sweden in his videos and social media.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 135}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1415", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Star Trek universe, what color is Vulcan blood?\n\nOptions: \nA. Green\nB. Purple\nC. Blue\nD. Red\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the Star Trek universe, Vulcan blood is famously depicted as green due to its copper-based composition. This is a well-known trait distinguishing Vulcans from humans. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 142}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3963", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In season one of the US Kitchen Nightmares, Gordan Ramsay tried to save 10 different restaurants. How many ended up closing afterwards?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 0\nC. 9\nD. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on available data, in the first season of the US *Kitchen Nightmares*, 6 of the 10 featured restaurants eventually closed.  \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1799", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: British actor David Morrissey stars as which role in \"The Walking Dead\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rick Grimes\nB. Daryl Dixon\nC. The Governor\nD. Negan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "David Morrissey played the character known as \"The Governor\" in *The Walking Dead*.  \nThis is a well-known fact from the series, distinguishing him from the other main characters listed.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1492", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cesar Romero played which iconic Batman villain from the 1960's TV show?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Riddler\nB. The Penguin\nC. Mr. Freeze\nD. The Joker\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Cesar Romero portrayed The Joker in the 1960s *Batman* television series. He is particularly remembered for refusing to shave his mustache, so it was often visible under the white makeup.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_2345", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Donkey Kong Country\", why does Donkey Kong want to know the secret of the crystal coconut?\n\nOptions: \nA. He's the big kahuna.\nB. Because Diddy Kong forced him.\nC. To find out where all the bananas are.\nD. He wants to punish brutes.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Donkey Kong Country*, Donkey Kong seeks the secret of the crystal coconut because it reveals the location of the banana hoard, which is his primary motivation. The correct answer matches that reason.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2933", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TF2: Sentry rocket damage falloff is calculated based on the distance between the sentry and the enemy, not the engineer and the enemy\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Team Fortress 2*, sentry rocket damage falloff is indeed based on the distance from the sentry gun to the target, not from the Engineer. This is consistent with how sentry guns operate independently of their builder.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3753", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Minecraft, which two items must be combined to craft a torch?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wood and Fire\nB. Wood and Coal\nC. Stick and Coal\nD. Stick and Fire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Minecraft, a torch is crafted by placing a stick above a piece of coal (or charcoal) on the crafting grid.  \nThe correct combination from the options is **Stick and Coal**.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 145}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2195", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By how many minutes are you late to work in \"Half-Life\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. 60\nB. 30\nC. 15\nD. 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Half-Life*, the protagonist Gordon Freeman arrives late to work, and the exact delay is specified as **five minutes** in the opening tram ride sequence.  \nTherefore, the correct answer corresponds to option D.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 151}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1985", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the lore of \"Starbound\", what does the \"Colony Deed\" do when it is placed down?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sends out an advertisement for someone to move in.\nB. Materializes a new being at it's location.\nC. Teleports a random person to the location.\nD. Teleports somebody from somewhere on the planet it is placed.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the game mechanics, the Colony Deed spawns a new NPC tenant at the location where it is placed, which matches the description in option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 175}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_563", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Rust, how many Timed Explosive Charges does it take to destroy a Ladder Hatch?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. 1\nC. 5\nD. 3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A. 2** \u2014 in the game Rust, a ladder hatch requires 2 Timed Explosive Charges to be destroyed.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 132}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_235", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many obsidian blocks are required to build a nether portal in Minecraft?\n\nOptions: \nA. 14\nB. 13\nC. 16\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A standard nether portal frame is 4 blocks tall and 5 blocks wide, requiring 10 obsidian blocks for the corners and edges, but the interior is empty.  \nIf you count only the blocks placed, it\u2019s 10 obsidian (the 4 corners and 6 vertical/horizontal edges).  \nTherefore, the correct answer is **D. 10**.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 187}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2562", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Magicka\", which two elements are combined to cast the spell, \"Nullify\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Arcane + Shield\nB. Arcane + Life\nC. Lightning + Life\nD. Lightning + Shield\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Magicka*, the \"Nullify\" spell is created by combining **Arcane** and **Shield** elements. This combination specifically counters and removes magical effects.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2634", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What ingredients are required to make a cake in Minecraft?\n\nOptions: \nA. Milk, Sugar, and Wheat\nB. Milk, Sugar Cane, Egg, and Wheat\nC. Milk, Sugar, Egg, and Wheat\nD. Milk, Bread, Egg, and Wheat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Minecraft, a cake requires **Milk, Sugar, Egg, and Wheat**, which matches option C.  \nOption B incorrectly lists \u201cSugar Cane\u201d instead of \u201cSugar,\u201d and the others are missing or have incorrect ingredients.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1005", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Terraria, which debuff does the ankh charm not provide immunity to?\n\nOptions: \nA. Venom\nB. Bleeding\nC. Cursed\nD. Slow\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Ankh Charm provides immunity to many debuffs, but **Slow** is not one of them. Immunity to Slow is granted by the Ankh Shield, which is the upgraded form combining the Ankh Charm with the Obsidian Shield.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2445", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Terraria, you can craft the Cell Phone pre-hardmode.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Cell Phone requires components like the Angler's fishing quest rewards and the Tinkerer's Workshop, which are available pre-hardmode, so it can indeed be crafted before entering hardmode.  \n**Answer:** B. True  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 136}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2184", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"The Witness\", how many lasers must be activated to get into the mountain area?\n\nOptions: \nA. 8\nB. 5\nC. 12\nD. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *The Witness*, you need to activate 7 lasers to open the path to the mountain.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 130}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1107", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which U.S. state is Far Cry 5's fictional setting 'Hope County' located?\n\nOptions: \nA. Montana\nB. Wyoming\nC. Idaho\nD. North Carolina\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The fictional Hope County in *Far Cry 5*