ptimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_984", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In RuneScape, one must complete the \"Dragon Slayer\" quest before equipping Rune Platelegs.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In RuneScape, the \"Dragon Slayer\" quest is required to equip a rune platebody, but not rune platelegs. Rune platelegs have no quest requirement and can be worn freely once the player meets the Defense level requirement (40 Defense). Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1781", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Half-Life\" series, \"H.E.V\" stands for \"Hazardous Evasiveness Vest\"\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**B. False**  \nIn the *Half-Life* series, H.E.V. stands for \"Hazardous Environment Vest,\" not \"Hazardous Evasiveness Vest.\" It is the protective suit worn by Gordon Freeman.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3760", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a \"360 no-scope\" is one full rotation before shooting, how many rotations would a \"1080 no-scope\" be?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 2\nC. 5\nD. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A \"360\" refers to one full rotation (360 degrees), so a \"1080\" would be \\(1080 \\div 360 = 3\\) full rotations.  \n\nThe correct answer is **A. 3**.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 145}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_637", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the title of the game \"Luigi's Mansion\", what is the only letter to not appear with a pair of eyes in it?\n\nOptions: \nA. n\nB. m\nC. s\nD. i\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"Luigi's Mansion,\" the letters in the title are stylized so that some have tiny eyes inside them; the only letter without eyes is the **\"n\"** in \"Mansion.\"  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1177", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which \"Fallout: New Vegas\" quest is NOT named after a real-life song?\n\nOptions: \nA. Come Fly With Me\nB. Ain't That a Kick in the Head\nC. They Went That-a-Way\nD. Ring-a-Ding Ding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quest \"They Went That-a-Way\" is not named after a real-life song, while the other options are all titles of songs. \"Come Fly With Me\" is a Frank Sinatra song, \"Ain't That a Kick in the Head\" is a Dean Martin song, and \"Ring-a-Ding Ding\" is also a Sinatra song. Therefore, the correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2289", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This Canadian television sportscaster is known for his \"Hockey Night in Canada\" role, a commentary show during hockey games.\n\nOptions: \nA. Don McKellar\nB. Donald Sutherland\nC. Don Taylor \nD. Don Cherry\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **Don Cherry**, who is famous for his commentary on \"Hockey Night in Canada\" and his outspoken personality.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2743", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many games did Arsenal FC go unbeaten during the 2003-2004 season of the English Premier League\n\nOptions: \nA. 38\nB. 51\nC. 22\nD. 49\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Arsenal\u2019s famous \u201cInvincibles\u201d season in 2003\u201304 saw them go unbeaten across 38 Premier League games, but the unbeaten run actually spanned 49 matches total, extending into the following season.  \nThe question asks specifically about the 2003\u20132004 season, which was 38 league games unbeaten, but the most famous number associated with the run is 49 across two seasons.  \nGiven the options, **49** is the widely recognized figure for the overall unbeaten run, even though 38 is correct for just that league season.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 134, "total_tokens": 240}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2603", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was the British professional wrestler Shirley Crabtree better known as?\n\nOptions: \nA. Giant Haystacks\nB. Kendo Nagasaki\nC. Masambula\nD. Big Daddy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shirley Crabtree was a famous British professional wrestler who performed under the ring name \"Big Daddy.\" Among the options, \"Big Daddy\" is directly associated with him. The correct choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_3408", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At which bridge does the annual Oxford and Cambridge boat race start?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hammersmith\nB. Putney\nC. Battersea\nD. Vauxhall \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The annual Oxford and Cambridge Boat Race begins at Putney Bridge in London.  \nThe race proceeds from Putney to Mortlake, passing other bridges like Hammersmith along the way.  \nTherefore, the correct starting point is Putney.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_1521", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During Wimbledon, spectators in the grounds can buy the tennis balls that have been used in matches.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "It is true that used match balls are sold to spectators at Wimbledon, often for charity.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 28, "total_tokens": 117}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"glo