l goes out of play over the goal line, last touched by a defender, not after a goal is scored.  \nAfter a goal, play restarts with a kick-off.  \nTherefore, the correct answer is **False**.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 161}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_3275", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What tool lends it's name to a last-stone advantage in an end in Curling?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drill\nB. Hammer\nC. Screwdriver\nD. Wrench\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The last-stone advantage in curling is called the **hammer**, named after the tool.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_1998", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why was The Green Monster at Fenway Park was originally built?\n\nOptions: \nA. To make getting home runs harder.\nB. To prevent viewing games from outside the park.\nC. To display advertisements.\nD. To provide extra seating.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Green Monster was originally built to prevent people outside Fenway Park from watching games for free, which matches option B. While it later became known for making home runs harder and displaying advertisements, its initial purpose was to block the view from nearby buildings.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 200}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2177", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A stimpmeter measures the speed of a ball over what surface?\n\nOptions: \nA.  Football Pitch\nB. Pinball Table\nC. Cricket Outfield\nD. Golf Putting Green\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A stimpmeter is specifically used in golf to measure the speed of a putting green by rolling a ball down a ramp and seeing how far it travels. Therefore, the correct surface is a golf putting green. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 161}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_976", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which boxer was banned for taking a bite out of Evander Holyfield's ear in 1997?\n\nOptions: \nA. Roy Jones Jr.\nB. Evander Holyfield\nC. Lennox Lewis\nD. Mike Tyson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is Mike Tyson, who was banned and had his boxing license revoked after biting Evander Holyfield\u2