 "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2992", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Harry Potter\" novels, what must a Hogwarts student do to enter the Ravenclaw Common Room?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rhythmically tap barrels with a wand\nB. Speak a password\nC. Knock in sequence\nD. Answer a riddle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To enter the Ravenclaw Common Room, a student must answer a riddle posed by a bronze door knocker, rather than using a password or tapping barrels.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 169}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2995", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"The Hobbit\", who kills Smaug?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frodo\nB. Bard\nC. Bilbo Baggins\nD. Gandalf the Grey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In J.R.R. Tolkien's *The Hobbit*, the dragon Smaug is killed by Bard the Bowman, who learns of Smaug's weak spot from a thrush that overheard Bilbo.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3000", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"Berenstein Bears\" is the correct spelling of the educational children's book series' name.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct spelling is actually **Berenstain Bears**, named after the authors Stan and Jan Berenstain, so the statement is false.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3056", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Green Eggs And Ham\" is a book by which author?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dr. Seuss\nB. Beatrix Potter\nC. A.A. Milne\nD. Roald Dahl\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\"Green Eggs and Ham\" is a well-known children's book written by Dr. Seuss. The other authors listed wrote different classic children's books but are not associated with this title.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3106", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By what nickname is Jack Dawkins known in the Charles Dickens novel, 'Oliver Twist'?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Artful Dodger\nB. Fagin\nC. Bull\u2019s-eye\nD. Mr. Fang\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Artful Dodger is the nickname for Jack Dawkins, the skilled pickpocket in Fagin's gang.  \nThe correct answer is A.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 142}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3157", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In The Lies of Locke Lamora, what title is Locke known by in the criminal world?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Thorn of the Marrows\nB. The Thorn of Camorr\nC. The Thorn of Emberlain\nD. The Rose of the Marrows\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *The Lies of Locke Lamora*, Locke is famously known as \"the Thorn of Camorr\" within the criminal underworld. This title reflects his reputation as a persistent and troublesome figure in the city of Camorr. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 176}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3339", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The book \"The Little Prince\" was written by...\n\nOptions: \nA. Jane Austen\nB. Ant