 "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1002", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Officials carrying out this European country's policies place an activist on trial in the novel  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel likely refers to *The Trial* by Franz Kafka, where Josef K. is prosecuted by an opaque authority, reflecting the Austro-Hungarian bureaucracy.  \n\n\\boxed{Austria}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 72, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 113}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1189", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: character by this name is shown a photograph of a messenger practicing the high jump by the Bridge Inn's landlady.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a scene from *The Hound of the Baskervilles* where Mrs. Barrymore shows a photograph of her brother to Sir Henry Baskerville. The brother is the escaped convict Selden, who is described as a messenger.  \n\n**Answer:** Sir Henry Baskerville  \n\n\\boxed{Sir Henry Baskerville}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1609", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Supposed \"supplements\" to this text, published by Franc\u0327ois Nodot (noh-doh) and Jose\u0301 Marchena, were later shown to be forgeries.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The text is *The Satyricon* by Petronius.  \n\n\\boxed{The Satyricon}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 16, "total_tokens": 112}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_667", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: While staying in this city, a man hears the story of Curran, a circus manager whose passion was founding a church exclusively for dogs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story of a circus manager named Curran founding a church for dogs is associated with **St. Louis, Missouri**, where such a church was established in the early 20th century.  \n\n\\boxed{St. Louis}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_267", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Denis Diderot revealed his atheism in a letter to a person with this condition.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"