, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 135}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1307", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This essay argues that from the perspective of the intellect, sin has no essence, but is \"diminution or  less ,\" whereas the conscience feels sin \"as essence,\" viewing it as \"pravity or  bad .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{Augustine}, as the description matches his view of sin as a privation of good rather than a positive substance.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1309", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an essay by Sigmund Freud, this state is characterized by a cleavage between the critical ego and the ego altered by identification, which is caused by the withdrawing of free libido from an object into the ego.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The state described is **melancholia** (or depression, as it is closely related to Freud\u2019s concept of mourning and melancholia).  \n\nIn Freud\u2019s 1917 essay \u201cMourning and Melancholia,\u201d melancholia involves the critical ego turning against the ego that has identified with a lost object, due to the withdrawal of libido.  \n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{melancholia}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1727", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem by Richard Brautigan reimagines this event as a rape at the hands of \"an evil  sherman who was dressed in clothes that had no childhood.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem by Richard Brautigan reimagines the **Lewis and Clark Expedition** as a rape by an evil \"sherman\" (likely a misspelling or variant of \"Sharman\" or \"shaman\").  \n\n\\boxed{Lewis and Clark Expedition}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 154}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1798", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Addressing this place, a character calls himself \"one who brings / A mind not to be changed by place or time,\" since \"The mind is its own place.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is Satan in John Milton's *Paradise Lost*, speaking in Hell.  \n**Answer:** \\boxed{Hell}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 117}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_0", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The lines \"Rude, and ungrateful, though my country be,\" in Book 5 of this work alludes to Scipio Africanus as a reference to its author's multiple exiles.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The lines allude to the author\u2019s own exiles and reference Scipio Africanus in Book 5 of *The Tristia* by Ovid.  \n\n\\boxed{Tristia}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 139}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_12", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a novel by this author, a character who thinks he has been poisoned when he is served locally-grown coffee is overthrown in a coup that anticipated a series of real-life coups in this author's home country later the same year.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *Autumn of the Patriarch* by Gabriel Garc\u00eda M\u00e1rquez, and the event matches a scene where the dictator fears poisoning from local coffee. The 1975 novel anticipated coups in the author's home country of Colombia later that year.\n\n\\boxed{Gabriel Garc\u00eda M\u00e1rquez}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_24", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: 