y referring to the fourth watch of the night, and the image of mountains disgorging suggests the moon rising. This matches the opening of the famous Tang dynasty poem \"The Moon at the Fortified Pass\" by Li Bai, which begins with the line \"The bright moon is born from the mountains of heaven.\"  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{the moon}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 166}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_105", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of a novel in this genre entertains fellow passengers on a stalled train by describing frogs being hunted en masse to supply restaurants with legs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The genre is **magic realism**, as the described scene is from Gabriel Garc\u00eda M\u00e1rquez's *Love in the Time of Cholera*, where Florentino Ariza tells this story on a stalled train.  \n\n\\boxed{Magic realism}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_127", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of a novel by this author is too absorbed in thinking about how Keats felt being spurned by Wordsworth to notice that assassins enter the restaurant he's in and gun down a man at the next table.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches a scene from Haruki Murakami\u2019s novel *Kafka on the Shore*, where the character Nakata is in a diner thinking about Keats and Wordsworth just before a violent incident.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{Haruki Murakami}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 155}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_136", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these poems states that the \"burden of a great / sadness\" arises from realizing that \"what one is pursuing now / was / once / nearer, truer, and joined to us / with infinite tenderness.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem described is **\"Archaic Torso of Apollo\" by Rainer Maria Rilke**, which ends with the famous line: \"You must change your life.\" The quoted lines about the \"burden of a great sadness\" and the lost connection appear in that poem.\n\n\\boxed{Archaic Torso of Apollo}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_138", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This play's author wrote that he was resisting the \"bourgeois conception of the immutability of the soul\" by having its characters be \"somewhat lacking in \u2018character.'\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play described is likely *Six Characters in Search of an Author* by Luigi Pirandello, as he critiqued fixed identity and \u201cbourgeois\u201d static conceptions of character.  \n\n\\boxed{Six Characters in Search of an Author}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_161", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Regina Gagnier's (\"GAHN-yay's\") book The Idylls of the Marketplace argues that this author's work functioned as a protest against the commodification of art through notions of utility.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author referenced in Regina Gagnier\u2019s argument about protesting the commodification of art is Oscar Wilde.  \n\n\\boxed{Oscar Wilde}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 142}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_210", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character created by this author stops believing in the supernatural and hears the speech of birds as mere chatter, after which he blots a manuscript and is imprisoned in a crystal bottle.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is from Jorge Luis Borges\u2019s story \u201cThe Aleph,\u201d and the author referenced is **William Shakespeare**.  \nThe story describes a manuscript by Shakespeare in which a character (possibly from *The Tempest*) loses his magical beliefs.  \nThus, the answer is Shakespeare.\n\n\\boxed{William Shakespeare}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_228", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The cover of Sherry Turkle's book Reclaiming Conversation is a reference to an anecdote in this other book, in which the narrator writes that he and his friend \"gradually shoved our chairs farther apart till they touched the wall in opposite corners.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The cover references an anecdote from *Walden* by Henry David Thoreau, where he describes a visit from a visitor with whom he felt a strained, distant connection.\n\n\\boxed{Walden}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_237", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem compares one of these animals to a person who is \"part woman, three parts a child,\" because she scans to ensure \"that nobody looks\" when her \"feet / Practice a tinker shuffle / Picked up on a street.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem describes a **monkey** imitating human behavior, specifically a shy or playful person.  \nThe lines are from Rudyard Kipling\u2019s poem \u201cThe Monkey,\u201d where the creature acts furtive and childlike.  \n\n\\boxed{monkey}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 166}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_300", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A speech in this novel claims that although \"no code\" mattered to a poor woman \"before she broke it,\" it \"came crashing down on her afterwards.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote is from Thomas Hardy's novel *Tess of the d'Urbervilles*, describing the societal judgment Tess faces after her loss of innocence.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{Tess of the d'Urbervilles}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 145}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_321", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of this novel kills a man and then pretends to be him to have sex with his lover, this novel's antagonist.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Silence of the Lambs*, where serial killer Jame Gumb (Buffalo Bill) is the antagonist, but the protagonist Clarice Starling does not commit that act. The scenario actually matches the plot of *Red Dragon*, where Francis Dolarhyde kills a man and impersonates him to be with the man's lover, Reba McClane.  \n\n\\boxed{Red Dragon}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 182}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_337", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At the end of this novel, its protagonist finally begins finishing his dissertation on his ancestor, after he abandoned it during a long period he calls his \"Great Sleep.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Sleepwalkers* by Hermann Broch, whose protagonist Joachim von Pasenow eventually resumes his dissertation on his ancestor after a period of inertia.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{The Sleepwalkers}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_343", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem by a writer of this ethnicity asks \"Why are the senators sitting there without legislating?\" and ends by calling the title group of people \"a kind of solution.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem is by a Puerto Rican writer (Pedro Pietri), and the title group is \"Puerto Ricans.\"  \nThe poem is \"Puerto Rican Obituary,\" which includes the line about senators and ends with \"puerto ricans / a kind of solution.\"  \n\n\\boxed{Puerto Rican}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_403", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A main character of a play named for one of these events takes a garland of orange blossoms from her maid and throws them on the floor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play is *The Cherry Orchard* by Anton Chekhov, and the main character is Madame Ranevskaya, who throws a garland of orange blossoms on the floor.  \n\n\\boxed{The Cherry Orchard}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_408", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character in this novel physically skips from side to side whilst delivering convoluted explanations, and is said to be able to turn black into white.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches the character of **Seth Pecksniff** from Charles Dickens's *Martin Chuzzlewit*, who is a hypocrite known for his sanctimonious speeches and mannerisms.  \n\n\\boxed{Seth Pecksniff}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_412", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one part of this poem, the protagonist has to climb aboard a creature with the wings of a dragon, the tail of a scorpion, and a face of an honest man in order to scale a cliff.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches the creature **Geryon** from Dante\u2019s *Inferno*, which the protagonist rides down a cliff in the eighth circle of Hell.  \n\n\\boxed{Geryon}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 140}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_431", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The main character of this novel persuades her husband to buy a skinny yellow mule by comparing the sale to the Emancipation Proclamation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel is *Their Eyes Were Watching God* by Zora Neale Hurston, in which Janie convinces Joe Starks to buy a yellow mule by likening its purchase to freedom from work, referencing the Emancipation Proclamation.  \n\n\\boxed{Their Eyes Were Watching God}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_445", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an allusion to the Book of Isaiah, this author described a \"cup of trembling\" that glowed and shook as the title character plays the piano at the end of a short story.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author is Flannery O\u2019Connor, who uses the phrase \u201ccup of trembling\u201d in her short story \u201cA Good Man Is Hard to Find\u201d during the final scene with the Misfit.  \n\n\\boxed{Flannery O'Connor}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_451", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by Edmund Wilson asks why people read stories that focus on these kinds of people.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The essay by Edmund Wilson is \u201cWhy Do People Read Detective Stories?\u201d which focuses on detectives and criminals.  \n\n\\boxed{detectives and criminals}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 112}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_479", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This story's protagonist pictures \"a young man under a dripping tree\" and realizes he is imagining shades of the afterlife.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story is \u201cAn Occurrence at Owl Creek Bridge\u201d by Ambrose Bierce.  \n\n\\boxed{An Occurrence at Owl Creek Bridge}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 110}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_491", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The appendix of a book in this genre includes a poem satirizing \"pious priests\" who attack \"Jack and Nell\" in the name of \"heavenly union.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem in the appendix satirizing priests attacking \u201cJack and Nell\u201d is from **William Blake\u2019s *The Marriage of Heaven and Hell***, which is a work of **prophetic poetry** or **Romantic literature**, but the most common genre categorization for this book is **poetry**.\n\n\\boxed{poetry}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_542", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a play, one of these objects gradually loses its resemblance to Pan and becomes more Mephistophelean over the span of 14 years.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The object is a set of wax figures, specifically the waxworks in Oscar Wilde's *The Picture of Dorian Gray*, which Dorian observes changing to reflect his own moral decay.  \n\\boxed{Wax figures}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 131}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_553", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character in this story describes how he always signs everything so he can hold up the crime to the punishment, see if they match, and determine whether he's been treated fairly.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is Edmond Dant\u00e8s from *The Count of Monte Cristo*, who says this as part of his philosophy of vengeance.  \n\n\\boxed{The Count of Monte Cristo}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 129}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_559", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character is subjected to an older woman's interminable conversation about the contents of a new letter from her niece, which this character escapes having read aloud to her.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is **Elizabeth Bennet** from *Pride and Prejudice*, who avoids hearing Mrs. Long's letter read aloud by her mother.\n\n\\boxed{Elizabeth Bennet}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 128}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_567", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one of these works, the title character unwittingly convinces thieving servants of his clairvoyance after he follows sarcastic instructions to buy an alphabet book with a picture of a rooster in it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story described is \"The Master Thief\" by the Brothers Grimm, where the clever protagonist uses the alphabet book with a rooster to trick the thieves.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{The Master Thief}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_590", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An author from this movement contrasted phrases like \"white napkin\" and \"daylight\" or \"the world\" and \"a purse\" in a text that praises the novels of Matthew Lewis.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author is from the **Romantic** movement, specifically Samuel Taylor Coleridge, who used such contrasts in his critique of Matthew Lewis\u2019s novels.  \n\n\\boxed{Romantic}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_605", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After a writer was banned in this country, a fellow poet wrote the lines \"only the trees know the pain as they stand still erect\u2026 their branches dry like wire.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country is **China**, where the poet Liu Xiaobo was banned, and the lines were written by his wife, Liu Xia.  \n\n\\boxed{China}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 123}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_628", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem about one of these animals describes how it \"drops the silver chain of sound\" after it \"rises and begins to round.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The line describes a skylark, which is known for its ascending flight and continuous, cascading song.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{Skylark}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 125}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_659", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Insisting on the centrality of \"intellectual freedom,\" this essay cites at length Arthur Quiller-Couch's argument that \"the poor poet has not in these days, nor has had for two hundred years, a dog's chance.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The essay is referring to F.\u202fR.\u202fLeavis\u2019s \u201cMass Civilization and Minority Culture.\u201d  \n\n\\boxed{F.\u202fR.\u202fLeavis}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_681", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Virginia Woolf highlighted a symbolic passage in this novel in which a plain earthenware pot allows the reader to see into the human soul.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel is *To the Lighthouse* by Virginia Woolf, where the \u201cplain earthenware pot\u201d appears in a key symbolic passage reflecting Mrs. Ramsay\u2019s consciousness.  \n\n\\boxed{To the Lighthouse}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_728", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem dedicated to his mother, this author described a felled chestnut tree as \"a soul ramifying and forever / silent, beyond silence listened for.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem is \u201cThe Chestnut Tree\u201d by **Seamus Heaney**, written in memory of his mother.\n\n\\boxed{Seamus Heaney}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 121}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_763", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this poem, one of the speakers recounts how she was beaten and stripped of her mantle by the \"sentinels of the walls\" making their rounds in the city.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem is \u201cThe Prisoner\u201d by Emily Bront\u00eb, where the female speaker describes being seized by the guards (\u201csentinels of the walls\u201d) during her attempted escape.  \n\n\\boxed{The Prisoner}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 136}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_771", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character fondly recalls \"the triumphant conviction of strength, the heat of life in the handful of dust\" associated with the title attribute in a short story that concludes with his first vision of the East.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is Marlow in Joseph Conrad\u2019s \u201cYouth,\u201d who associates this feeling with the sea.  \n\n\\boxed{Marlow}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 125}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_780", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these people becomes a hero by saving a boy from drowning in a novel in which these people are impressed by a man's ability to shoot pheasants on the wing.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel is *The Great Gatsby*, and the people are the Buchanans (Tom and Daisy). The hero who saves a boy from drowning is Gatsby himself, and the man who impresses the Buchanans with his ability to shoot pheasants on the wing is Tom Buchanan.  \n\n\\boxed{The Buchanans}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_811", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an essay, this author wondered at the pre-modern \"dry truthfulness\" with which Homer recorded the unequal value of the arms exchanged by Diomedes and Glaucus.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author is **Matthew Arnold**, who in his essay \u201cOn Translating Homer\u201d comments on the episode in the *Iliad* where Diomedes and Glaucus exchange armor of unequal value.  \n\n\\boxed{Matthew Arnold}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens":