 is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The scene describes the destruction of the Horcrux diary in *Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets*, which is stabbed with a basilisk fang. The \"candle\" is the magical life of the Horcrux flaring and going out as the memory of Tom Riddle is defeated.\n\n\\boxed{Tom Riddle's Diary}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 161}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1210", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem by this author that opposes the palindromic terms amor and Roma, Tarpeia begs for a retributive \"Rape of the Roman Women.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem is by **Propertius**, specifically Elegy 4.4, which tells the story of Tarpeia\u2019s betrayal of Rome for love of the Sabine leader Tatius.  \n\n\\boxed{Propertius}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1215", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Margaret Ezell challenged the historical assumptions perpetuated by this character's story in her essay on \"The Myth of [this character].\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is **Judith Shakespeare**, from Virginia Woolf's *A Room of One's Own*.  \n\nMargaret Ezell's essay critiques the idea that women writers before the 18th century were exceptionally rare or suppressed into silence.  \n\n\\boxed{Judith Shakespeare}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1225", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem set at this location, the speaker hears \"peals of distant ironical laughter at every word I have written\" and describes himself as \"ba  led, balk'd, bent to the very earth\" in his awareness that \"before all my arrogant poems the real Me stands yet untouch'd, untold, altogether unreach'd.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem is Walt Whitman\u2019s \u201cAs I Ebb\u2019d with the Ocean of Life,\u201d and the location described is the seashore.  \n\n\\boxed{The seashore}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 167}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1235", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character addresses the \"dark Hindoo half of nature\" as he watches an animal turn to \"seek intercedings with yon all-quickening sun\" before it dies.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "gene