rguing against predestination in a speech that repeats his claim to be a racially-pure \"man without a cross.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The protagonist is **John \u201cHandsome\u201d Grand** from *The Grandissimes*.  \n\n\\boxed{The Grandissimes}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 117}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1820", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character says that one of these objects \"irked me... it itched me\" after he and another man find one of them on the ground and silently swap three of them back and forth.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The object is a **hat**, from the hat-swapping scene in Mark Twain\u2019s *A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur\u2019s Court*.  \n\n\\boxed{hat}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 132}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1833", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character conceives of conversation as a \"served dessert\" of ripe fruits to be piled atop a silver plate signifying his wife's mind.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is St. John Rivers in Charlotte Bront\u00eb's *Jane Eyre*, who describes intellectual conversation with Jane as a dessert to be offered to his wife Rosamond.  \n\n\\boxed{St. John Rivers}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1843", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a story titled for a man with this name, the narrator gives a brief outline of the plot, then gives the reader the option of meditating on it individually or reading the fuller account, trusting that there will be a moral \"done up neatly, and condensed into the \u70a4nal sentence.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story is \u201cWakefield\u201d by Nathaniel Hawthorne, so the man\u2019s name is Wakefield.  \n\n\\boxed{Wakefield}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 145}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1856", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this poem, a transition between two radically di\u9d01ferent refrains occurs with the line \"The ant's a centaur in his dragon world.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The line \u201cThe ant\u2019s a centaur in his dragon world\u201d appears in the poem \u201cPity Me Not\u201d by Edna St. Vincent Millay, but the poem does not contain two radically different refrains.  \nThe line actually comes from the poem \u201cwhat if a much of a which of a wind\u201d by E. E. Cummings, where it marks a shift from a chaotic to a more ordered refrain.  \nTherefore, the correct answer is the poem by E. E. Cummings.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{E. E. Cummings}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 201}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1879", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a short story, a young man tasked with picking out one of these beings among a group of maidens playing \"hawk and chickens\" is rewarded with a mysterious letter for his father the mayor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story is \"The Shepherd\u2019s Daughter\" by William Saroyan, where the young man must identify a *fairy* disguised among the maidens.  \n\n\\boxed{fairy}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 137}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1893", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this novel, a professor tells his students to \"let your thought be the wall,\" then \"let your thought be that that thought the wall.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel is *The Glass Bead Game* (also known as *Magister Ludi*) by Hermann Hesse.  \n\n\\boxed{The Glass Bead Game}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 122}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoGraphyData_100k_0", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the capital of France?\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The capital of France is Paris.\n\n\\boxed{Paris}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 71, "output_tokens": 11, "total_tokens": 82}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoGraphyData_100k_3", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which country has the largest population?\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "As of current estimates, India has surpassed China to become the country with the largest population. This change occurred around 2023 based on United Nations data.  \n\n\\boxed{India}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 68, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 107}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoGraphyData_100k_4", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the largest island in the world?\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The largest island in the world is Greenland, as it is defined as a landmass surrounded by water and not considered a continent.  \nAustralia is larger but is classified as a continental landmass, not an island.  \n\n\\boxed{Greenland}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 73, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 130}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoGraphyData_100k_5", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which country is known for its pyramids?\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Egypt is most famous for its ancient pyramids, particularly the Giza pyramid complex near Cairo.  \n\\boxed{Egypt}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 73, "output_tokens": 28, "total_tokens": 101}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoGraphyData_100k_6", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which ocean is the largest in the world?\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Pacific Ocean is the largest and deepest ocean on Earth, covering about one-third of the planet's surface.  \n\n\\boxed{Pacific Ocean}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 64, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 95}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoGraphyData_100k_7", "prompt":