icut, not New Haven.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 27, "total_tokens": 126}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2088", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Broome is a town in which state of Australia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Northern Territory\nB. Tasmania\nC. South Australia\nD. Western Australia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Broome is located in the Kimberley region of **Western Australia**.  \nIt is known for its pearling industry and Cable Beach.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 139}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1608", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the following are classified as Finno-Ugric languages EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hungarian\nB. Finnish\nC. Estonian\nD. Samoyedic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Finno-Ugric language family includes Hungarian, Finnish, and Estonian, but Samoyedic languages belong to a separate branch of the Uralic family. Therefore, Samoyedic is not classified as Finno-Ugric.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_504", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which English county is Stonehenge?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wiltshire\nB. Somerset\nC. Cumbria\nD. Herefordshire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stonehenge is located in Wiltshire, which is a county in southwestern England. The other counties listed are not the site of this prehistoric monument.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3211", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What event led to Liechenstein adding a crown to its flag?\n\nOptions: \nA. The 1936 Olympics\nB. Signing of the 1862 Constitution of Liechtenstein\nC. Charles VI's decree in 1719\nD. Coronation of Prince Johann I Joseph in 1805\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The crown was added to Liechtenstein\u2019s flag in 1937 after it was discovered at the 1936 Olympics that its flag was identical to Haiti\u2019s. This prompted the change to avoid confusion. Therefore, the event that led to the addition was the 1936 Olympics.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 193}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1221", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On a London Underground map, what colour is the Circle Line?\n\nOptions: \nA. Blue\nB. Red\nC. Green\nD. Yellow\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Circle Line on the London Underground map is yellow.  \nAmong the options, yellow corresponds to choice D.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 128}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2468", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many stations does the Central Line have on the London Underground?\n\nOptions: \nA. 43\nB. 49\nC. 47\nD. 51\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Central Line has 49 stations, which matches option B. This count includes all stations served by the line, even those shared with other lines.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1120", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The flag of South Africa features 7 colours.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The South African flag uses six colors: red, blue, green, black, white, and gold (yellow).  \nIt does not have seven colors.  \nTherefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 132}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3880", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following Inuit languages was the FIRST to use a unique writing system not based on the Latin alphabet?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inuktitut\nB. Inupiat\nC. Greenlandic\nD. Inuinnaqtun\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first Inuit language to use a unique non-Latin writing system was Greenlandic, which adopted the **Greenlandic alphabet** (based on the Latin script but with unique additions like Kra) in the 1850s, though the question may refer to the earlier **Syllabics** used for Inuktitut in the 19th century. However, among the options, **Inuktitut** was the first to widely use a writing system not based on the Latin alphabet\u2014specifically, the **Inuktitut syllabics** developed in the 1870s.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 132, "total_tokens": 248}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1953", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where is the fast food chain \"Panda Express\" headquartered?\n\nOptions: \nA. Fresno, California\nB. Rosemead, California\nC. San Diego, California\nD. Sacramento, California\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Panda Express was founded in and is headquartered in Rosemead, California.  \nThis is a well-known fact about the company's origins.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2812", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Liechtenstein does not have an airport.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Liechtenstein does not have its own commercial airport; the nearest airports are in neighboring Switzerland and Austria. Therefore, the statement is true.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 119}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2364", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What national museum will you find in Cooperstown, New York?\n\nOptions: \nA. National Toy Hall of Fame\nB. National Baseball Hall of Fame\nC. Metropolitan Museum of Art\nD. Museum of Modern Art\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The National Baseball Hall of Fame is located in Cooperstown, New York, which matches the question. The other museums are not primarily associated with that town.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 162}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_878", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following European languages is classified as a \"language isolate?\"\n\nOptions: \nA. Maltese\nB. Galician\nC. Hungarian\nD. Basque\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Basque is the only language isolate among the options, meaning it has no known genetic relationship to any other language. The other languages belong to established language families: Maltese (Semitic), Galician (Romance), and Hungarian (Uralic).  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1057", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Japanese district Akihabara is also known by what nickname?\n\nOptions: \nA. Otaku Central \nB. Electric Town\nC. Big Eyes\nD. Moon Walk River\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Akihabara is famously known for its electronics shops and pop culture, which led to the nickname \"Electric Town.\"  \nThis aligns with option **B**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 146}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3368", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What name was historically used for the Turkish city currently known as Istanbul?\n\nOptions: \nA. Adrianople\nB. Constantinople\nC. H\u00fcdavendigar\nD. S\u00f6\u011f\u00fct\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city now called Istanbul was historically known as Constantinople during the Byzantine and early Ottoman periods.  \nAdrianople is the old name for Edirne, while H\u00fcdavendigar and S\u00f6\u011f\u00fct are associated with other Turkish towns.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is Constantinople.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 181}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3087", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The title of the 1969 film \"Krakatoa, East_of Java\" is incorrect, as Krakatoa is in fact west of Java.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is accurate because Krakatoa is indeed west of Java, making the film\u2019s title geographically incorrect.  \nTherefore, the correct answer is that the claim is true.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2480", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which English county will you find the University of East Anglia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Norfolk\nB. Suffolk\nC. Essex\nD. Cambridgeshire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The University of East Anglia (UEA) is located in Norwich, which is in the county of Norfolk.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 26, "total_tokens": 129}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_724", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Into which basin does the Jordan River flow into?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aral Sea\nB. Salton Sea\nC. Dead Sea\nD. Caspian Sea\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Jordan River flows into the Dead Sea, which is a salt lake bordered by Jordan and Israel.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 131}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2466", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gothenburg is the capital of Sweden.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The capital of Sweden is Stockholm, not Gothenburg. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 112}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1511", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The formerly East-Prussian city of K\u00f6nigsberg is known as which Russian City today?\n\nOptions: \nA. Kazan\nB. Krasnodar\nC. Kaliningrad\nD. Kursk\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "K\u00f6nigsberg was renamed after World War II and is now a Russian exclave. The correct present-day name is Kaliningrad. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 139}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2056", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The two largest ethnic groups of Belgium are Flemish and Walloon. \n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is true: the Flemish (Dutch-speaking) and Walloon (French-speaking) communities are indeed the two largest ethnic groups in Belgium.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 135}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Southeast Asian island of Borneo is politically divided among 3 countries.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Borneo is divided among three countries: Malaysia (states of Sabah and Sarawak), Indonesia (Kalimantan), and Brunei.  \nTherefore, the statement is true.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 140}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_776", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If soccer is called football in England, what is American football called in England?\n\nOptions: \nA. Touchdown\nB. Combball\nC. American football\nD. Handball\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In England, the sport known as American football in the U.S. is still typically called \"American football\" to distinguish it from soccer (which they call football). The other terms are not the standard name for the sport there.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1149", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The World Health Organization headquarters is located in which European country?\n\nOptions: \nA. France\nB. Switzerland\nC. Belgium\nD. United Kingdom\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The World Health Organization headquarters is in Geneva, which is in Switzerland.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 23, "total_tokens": 131}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1548", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Israel is 7 hours ahead of New York.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Israel observes daylight saving time, but its schedule does not always align with New York\u2019s, so the time difference can vary between 6 and 7 hours.  \nTherefore, stating it is always 7 hours ahead is not consistently accurate.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2150", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are no deserts in Europe.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement \u201cThere are no deserts in Europe\u201d is false because Europe contains semi-arid regions that qualify as deserts, such as the Tabernas Desert in Spain.  \n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 121}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1942", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the African nation of Zimbabwe formerly known as?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mozambique\nB. Zambia\nC. Rhodesia\nD.  Bulawayo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Zimbabwe was known as Rhodesia before gaining independence in 1980. The other options are either different countries or a city within Zimbabwe. The correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 146}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_171", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of one of the Neo-Aramaic languages spoken by the Jewish population from Northwestern Iraq?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lishan Didan\nB. Hulaul\u00e1\nC. Lishana Deni\nD. Chaldean Neo-Aramaic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Jewish Neo-Aramaic language from Northwestern Iraq is Lishana Deni, which was historically spoken in the region around Zakho and Dohuk. The other options are either spoken by Jewish communities in other regions (like Lishan Didan in Iran and Hulaul\u00e1 in Kurdistan/Iran) or by Christian communities (Chaldean Neo-Aramaic).  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 207}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2220", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There is an island in Japan called \u014ckunoshima, A.K.A. \"Rabbit Island\", so named because of it's huge population of rabbits.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is true; \u014ckunoshima is indeed known as \"Rabbit Island\" due to its large population of feral rabbits.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is A.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usag