e, Italy\nC. Carlisle, England\nD. Dublin, Ireland\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hadrian's Wall is a Roman fortification built across northern England. It runs from the vicinity of Carlisle on the west coast to Wallsend on the east coast.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1131", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tokyo is the capital of Japan.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is factually correct, as Tokyo is indeed the capital of Japan.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 21, "total_tokens": 108}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1664", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nova Scotia is on the east coast of Canada.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nova Scotia is indeed located on the Atlantic coast in eastern Canada.  \nTherefore, the statement is true.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 119}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2346", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the county seat of King County, Washington?\n\nOptions: \nA. Seattle\nB. Skykomish\nC. Bellevue\nD. Enumclaw\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The county seat of King County, Washington, is Seattle, as it houses the county government offices and courthouse.  \nWhile Bellevue is a major city in the county, it is not the county seat.  \nThus, the correct answer is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_473", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Hunua Ranges is located in...\n\nOptions: \nA. China\nB. Nepal\nC. New Zealand\nD. Mexico\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hunua Ranges are a mountain range and regional park situated in the North Island of New Zealand. This makes option C the correct choice.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 132}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1997", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Montreal is in which Canadian province?\n\nOptions: \nA. Quebec\nB. Nova Scotia\nC. Alberta\nD. Ontario\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Montreal is a major city located in the province of Quebec.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 22, "total_tokens": 118}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3155", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The capital of the US State Ohio is the city of Chillicothe.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The capital of Ohio is Columbus, not Chillicothe. Therefore, the statement is false.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 118}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3698", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Sonoran Desert is located in eastern Africa.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Sonoran Desert is located in North America, primarily in the southwestern United States and northwestern Mexico, not in eastern Africa.  \nTherefore, the statement is false.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_514", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these countries is located the FURTHEST away from the South China Sea?\n\nOptions: \nA. Malaysia\nB. Vietnam\nC. Bangladesh\nD. Philippines\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Bangladesh is located on the Bay of Bengal and is not directly adjacent to the South China Sea, while Malaysia, Vietnam, and the Philippines all have coastlines along it. Therefore, Bangladesh is the farthest from the South China Sea geographically.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_792", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these countries is \"doubly landlocked\" (surrounded entirely by one or more landlocked countries)?\n\nOptions: \nA. Uzbekistan\nB. Switzerland\nC. Bolivia\nD. Ethiopia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A doubly landlocked country is one that is landlocked and also surrounded only by other landlocked countries.  \nUzbekistan is landlocked and its neighbors (Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan, Afghanistan, Turkmenistan) are all landlocked as well.  \nThe other options are either not landlocked (Switzerland borders Italy, which has a coastline) or not surrounded solely by landlocked countries.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 218}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1143", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not a megadiverse country - one that harbors a high number of the earth's endemic species?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peru\nB. Thailand\nC. South Africa\nD. Mexico\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Thailand is not among the world's recognized megadiverse countries, while Peru, South Africa, and Mexico are all on the list.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 140}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following Arab countries does NOT have a flag containing only Pan-Arab colours?\n\nOptions: \nA. United Arab Emirates\nB. Jordan\nC. Qatar\nD. Kuwait\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Pan-Arab colors are black, white, green, and red. Qatar\u2019s flag is maroon and white, not using the standard red, so it does not contain only the four Pan-Arab colors.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2099", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following language families is the most controversial amongst modern linguists?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indo-European\nB. Dravidian\nC. Altaic\nD. Sino-Tibetan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Altaic hypothesis, which proposes a genetic relationship between Turkic, Mongolic, and Tungusic languages (and sometimes Japanese and Korean), is widely disputed due to a lack of conclusive evidence for common ancestry. In contrast, the other families listed (Indo-European, Dravidian, Sino-Tibetan) are generally accepted by linguists.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 199}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1967, a magazine published a story about extracting hallucinogenic chemicals from bananas to raise moral questions about banning drugs.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story is a well-known urban legend, and no such article was actually published in a reputable magazine in 1967.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_253", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Fallingwater House, located in Pennsylvania, was designed by which architect?\n\nOptions: \nA. Antoni Gaudi\nB. Frank Lloyd Wright\nC. Frank Gehry\nD. Le Corbusier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Fallingwater House is a famous example of organic architecture designed by Frank Lloyd Wright. The other architects listed are known for different iconic works.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 145}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3563", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you grab the bladed end of a longsword in a specific way, you will not cut yourself.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**B. True**  \n\nIt is possible to grasp the bladed portion of a longsword safely using a technique called \u201chalf-swording,\u201d where the grip is adjusted to hold the blade with a firm, flat-palmed grasp, often used for better control in thrusts or grappling.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2093", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"I disapprove of what you say, but I will defend to the death your right to say it\" is a quote from French philosopher Voltaire.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote is widely attributed to Voltaire, but it was actually written by his biographer Evelyn Beatrice Hall summarizing his views. Therefore, the statement as given is not accurate.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_236", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The fourth funnel of the RMS Titanic was fake designed to make the ship look more powerful and symmetrical.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The fourth funnel of the Titanic was indeed non-functional, used for ventilation and to give the ship a more balanced appearance.  \nThis matches the statement given.  \nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3511", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Las Vegas casino was originally constructed and operated by mobster Bugsy Siegel?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Flamingo\nB. The MGM Grand\nC. The Sahara\nD. The Sands\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Flamingo was famously opened by Bugsy Siegel in 1946 and is historically tied to his involvement in Las Vegas. The other casinos listed were built later or by other figures.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2033", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is NOT classified as a Semetic language?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sumerian\nB. Mandaic\nC. Akkadian\nD. Maltese\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sumerian is a language isolate and not part of the Semitic language family, while Mandaic, Akkadian, and Maltese are all Semitic languages. Therefore, the correct answer is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2185", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The coat of arms of the King of Spain contains the arms from the monarchs of Castille, Leon, Aragon and which other former Iberian kingdom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Catalonia\nB. Granada\nC. Galicia\nD. Navarre\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The coat of arms of the King of Spain includes the arms of the former kingdoms of Castile, Le\u00f3n, Arag\u00f3n, and Navarre, reflecting the historical unification of Spain. Granada is represented separately as a pomegranate at the bottom, not as one of the main quarterings.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 187}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1532", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pianist Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Chopin was a composer of which musical era?\n\nOptions: \nA. Baroque\nB. Romantic\nC. Renaissance\nD. Classic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Chopin was a composer and pianist whose work is most closely associated with the Romantic era of music. The Romantic period emphasized emotion, individualism, and expressive depth, which aligns with Chopin's style. Therefore, the correct choice is Romantic.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 171}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_950", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The M41 Walker Bulldog remains in service in some countries to this day.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The M41 Walker Bulldog is still used by some nations, such as Taiwan and Uruguay, for light reconnaissance and security roles. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 131}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_453", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the aim of the \"Umbrella Revolution\" in Hong Kong in 2014?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lower taxes\nB. Go back under British Rule\nC. Genuine universal suffrage\nD. Gaining Independence\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Umbrella Revolution in 2014 was primarily a pro-democracy movement demanding genuine universal suffrage for Hong Kong, without restrictive pre-screening of candidates by Beijing.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3923", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The original Roman alphabet lacked the following letters EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. J\nB. X\nC. W\nD. U\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The original Roman alphabet (the Latin alphabet as used in the classical period) lacked the letters J, W, and U (using V for both the vowel and consonant sounds), but it did include X.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1092", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When did L. L. Zamenhof first publish \"Unua Libro\", the first publication describing his international language Esperanto?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1887\nB. 1915\nC. 1897\nD. 1905\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "L. L. Zamenhof first published \"Unua Libro\" in 1887, which introduced Esperanto to the world. The other dates correspond to later events in Esperanto's history or unrelated milestones. Therefore, the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 170}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3348", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ancient city of Chich\u00e9n Itz\u00e1 was built by which civilization?\n\nOptions: \nA. Toltecs\nB. Mayans\nC. Incas\nD. Aztecs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Chich\u00e9n Itz\u00e1 was primarily built by the Maya civilization, though it shows later Toltec influences. The other civilizations were located in different regions of the Americas.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1452", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Under which name was Rodrigo Borgia made Pope?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Paul II\nB. Rodrigo I\nC. Pius VII\nD. Alexander VI\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Rodrigo Borgia became Pope Alexander VI in 1492.  \nThe other options are popes from different eras.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_46", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Tiananmen Square protests of 1989 were held in Hong Kong.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Tiananmen Square protests of 1989 occurred in Beijing, not Hong Kong. Therefore, the statement is false.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 124}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_422", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The creator of the Enigma Cypher and Machine was of what nationality?\n\nOptions: \nA. German\nB. British\nC. American\nD. Polish\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Enigma machine was invented by German engineer Arthur Scherbius, making its creator German.  \n**Correct answer: A. German**  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2949", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: King Henry VIII was the second monarch of which European royal house?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stuart\nB. York\nC. Tudor\nD. Lancaster\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "King Henry VIII was the second monarch of the Tudor dynasty, following his father Henry VII. The other houses either preceded the Tudors or came later.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 143}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3603", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sir Issac Newton served as a Member of Parliament, but the only recorded time he spoke was to complain about a draft in the chambers.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This statement is true according to historical records; Newton did serve in Parliament and his only recorded intervention was indeed about a cold draft.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3902", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not in the Indo-European language family?\n\nOptions: \nA. Finnish\nB. Russian\nC. English\nD. Hindi\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Finnish is a Uralic language, while Russian, English, and Hindi are all Indo-European languages.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 132}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1183", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After his loss at the Battle of Waterloo, Napoleon Bonaparte was exiled to which island?\n\nOptions: \nA. Elba\nB. St. Helena\nC. Canary\nD. Corsica\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Napoleon was initially exiled to Elba after his first abdication, but after his defeat at Waterloo, he was sent to St. Helena, where he spent the remainder of his life.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 158}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2888", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who is the creator of the soft drink, Dr. Pepper?\n\nOptions: \nA. James Wellington\nB. Charles Alderton\nC. Boris Heviltik\nD. Johnson Hinsin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The creator of Dr. Pepper was pharmacist Charles Alderton, who first made the drink in the 1880s in Waco, Texas.  \nTherefore, the correct answer corresponds to option B.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 165}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_940", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The minigun was designed in 1960 by which manufacturer.\n\nOptions: \nA. General Electric\nB. Colt Firearms\nC. Sig Sauer\nD. Heckler & Koch\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The minigun was designed by General Electric, which developed the electrically driven Gatling-style gun for the U.S. military in the 1960s.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1865", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In addition to his career as an astrologer and \"prophet\", Nostradamus published a 1555 treatise that included a section on what?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cheating at card games\nB. Making jams and jellies\nC. Teaching parrots to talk\nD. Digging graves\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nostradamus\u2019s 1555 work *Les Proph\u00e9ties* was published alongside an earlier treatise that included a section on making jams, jellies, and cosmetics. This section was part of his 1552 treatise on medical recipes and household preparations. Therefore, the correct answer is the option about preserves.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 132, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 209}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3884", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who is attributed credit for recording the epic poem The Odyssey?\n\nOptions: \nA. Homer\nB. Socrates\nC. Aristotle\nD. Odysseus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Odyssey is traditionally attributed to the ancient Greek poet Homer.  \nNone of the other options are known for recording this epic poem.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1815", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During the Spanish Civil War (1936), Francisco Franco fought for which political faction?\n\nOptions: \nA. Popular Front\nB. Papal State\nC. Nationalist Spain\nD. Republican Spain\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Francisco Franco led the Nationalist faction during the Spanish Civil War, which opposed the Republican government.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 131}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3970", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which English king was married to Eleanor of Aquitaine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Henry V\nB. Richard I\nC. Henry I\nD. Henry II\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Eleanor of Aquitaine was married first to King Louis VII of France and then to King Henry II of England.  \nTherefore, the correct answer is Henry II.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 140}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3985", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With which Greek philosopher would you associate the phrase, \"I know that I know nothing\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aristotle\nB. Pythagoras\nC. Socrates\nD. Plato\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This phrase is attributed to Socrates, reflecting his approach to wisdom through acknowledging one\u2019s own ignorance. It is famously recounted in Plato\u2019s account of Socrates\u2019 defense in the *Apology*.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 146}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_170", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Spain was formed in 1469 with the marriage of Isabella I of Castile and Ferdinand II of what other Iberian kingdom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Navarre\nB. Aragon\nC. Galicia\nD. Le\u00f3n\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The marriage of Isabella I of Castile and Ferdinand II of Aragon in 1469 united the two largest Christian kingdoms in the Iberian Peninsula, leading to the formation of Spain.  \nThe other options were either absorbed earlier or remained separate entities.  \n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1641", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the name of one of the surviving palaces of Henry VIII located near Richmond, London?\n\nOptions: \nA. St James's Palace\nB. Buckingham Palace\nC. Coughton Court\nD. Hampton Court\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hampton Court Palace is indeed one of Henry VIII's surviving palaces and is located near Richmond upon Thames in London. The other options are either not associated with Henry VIII in the same way or are in different locations.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 159}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3667", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Hagia Sophia was commissioned by which emperor of the Byzantine Empire?\n\nOptions: \nA. Theodosius the Great\nB. Justinian I\nC. Constantine IV\nD. Arcadius\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hagia Sophia was commissioned by Emperor Justinian I, who oversaw its construction after the previous church was destroyed during the Nika riots.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1436", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The son of which pope supposedly held a lecherous f\u00eate involving 50 courtesans in the papal palace?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pius III\nB. Urban II\nC. Innocent V\nD. Alexander VI\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D. Alexander VI**, as his son Cesare Borgia was infamous for the \"Banquet of Chestnuts,\" a scandalous event held in the Vatican.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 154}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_332", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Battle of Trafalgar took place on October 23rd, 1805\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Battle of Trafalgar actually took place on **October 21st, 1805**, not October 23rd.  \nTherefore, the statement in the question is incorrect.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 132}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1483", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ontological argument for the proof of God's existence is first attributed to whom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aristotle\nB. Immanuel Kant\nC. Anselm of Canterbury\nD. Ren\u00e9 Descartes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ontological argument is most famously associated with Anselm of Canterbury in the 11th century, though it was later reformulated by others like Descartes.  \nWhile Descartes also developed an ontological argument, the historical origin is credited to Anselm.  \nTherefore, the correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 191}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_541", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what dialogue did Socrates defend himself to the court of Athens?