hol\nD. Post cards\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first vending machines in the early 1880s were invented in London and dispensed post cards, not beverages or cigarettes. This makes option D the correct choice.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what year was the video game company Electronic Arts founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1981\nB. 1999\nC. 2005\nD. 1982\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Electronic Arts was founded in 1982 by Trip Hawkins. The correct option corresponds to that year.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 27, "total_tokens": 126}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2331", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: United States President Ronald Reagan was the first president to appoint a woman to the Supreme Court. \n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "**B. True**  \nRonald Reagan appointed Sandra Day O\u2019Connor in 1981, making her the first woman to serve on the Supreme Court. No previous president had appointed a female justice.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The seed drill was invented by which British inventor?\n\nOptions: \nA. Jethro Tull\nB. Isaac Newton\nC. Charles Babbage\nD. J.J Thomson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jethro Tull invented the seed drill, an important innovation in agricultural technology during the British Agricultural Revolution.  \nThe other individuals are known for contributions to physics, computing, and science, not farming equipment.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_411", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what year was the famous 45 foot tall Hollywood sign first erected?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1933\nB. 1923\nC. 1913\nD. 1903\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hollywood sign was originally erected as \u201cHollywoodland\u201d in 1923 to promote a real estate development. Therefore, the correct answer is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3283", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The pantheon in Rome was used to worship what god?\n\nOptions: \nA. Zeus\nB. Athena\nC. Any god they wanted\nD. Both Athena and Zeus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Pantheon in Rome was originally built as a temple for all the gods of ancient Rome, not a single specific deity.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_523", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first televised presidential debate was between Jimmy Carter and Gerald Ford.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first televised presidential debate was between John F. Kennedy and Richard Nixon in 1960, not between Jimmy Carter and Gerald Ford.  \nCarter and Ford debated in 1976, but it was not the first televised debate.  \nTherefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 164}}, "cost"