lization of weaving?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Kay\nB. Richard Arkwright\nC. James Hargreaves\nD. John Deere\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The flying shuttle was invented by **John Kay** in 1733 (often cited as patented in 1733, with improvements in later years like 1738). This device mechanized the process of weaving and was a key step toward industrial textile manufacturing.\n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The crown of the Empire State Building was originally built for what purpose?\n\nOptions: \nA. Antennae\nB. Flag Pole\nC. Lightning Rod\nD. Airship Dock\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The crown of the Empire State Building was designed as a mooring mast for airships, though this proved impractical and dangerous. Therefore, the correct answer is **D. Airship Dock**.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 157}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_438", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After the 1516 Battle of Marj Dabiq, the Ottoman Empire took control of Jerusalem from which sultanate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mamluk\nB. Ummayyad\nC. Ayyubid\nD. Seljuq\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Battle of Marj Dabiq in 1516 resulted in an Ottoman victory over the **Mamluk Sultanate**, leading to Ottoman control over Jerusalem. The other sultanates listed had lost control of Jerusalem long before this battle.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 168}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_857", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adolf Hitler was accepted into the Vienna Academy of Fine Arts.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Adolf Hitler applied to the Vienna Academy of Fine Arts twice (in 1907 and 1908) and was rejected both times, so he was never accepted.  \nTherefore, the statement is false.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 144}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1162", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"Trail of Tears\" was a result of which United States President's Indian Removal Policy?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Quincy Adams\nB. Andrew Jackson\nC. Harry S. Truman\nD. Martin Van Buren\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Trail of Tears was the forced relocation of Native Americans in the 1830s, primarily resulting from the Indian Removal Act signed by President Andrew Jackson and enforced during his administration.\n\nCorrect answer: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 174}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3273", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In relation to the British Occupation in Ireland, what does the IRA stand for.\n\nOptions: \nA. Irish Reformation Army\nB. Irish-Royal Alliance\nC. Irish Republican Army\nD. Irish Rebel Alliance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The IRA is historically known as the Irish Republican Army, an organization seeking Irish independence from British rule.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1054", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Louis was known as 'The Sun King of France'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Louis XIII\nB. Louis XV\nC. Louis XVI\nD. Louis XIV\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Louis XIV is famously known as the Sun King.  \nHe used the sun as his personal emblem and ruled France for over 70 years.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3509", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The United States Department of Homeland Security was formed in response to the September 11th attacks.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Department of Homeland Security was established in 2002, directly in response to the September 11, 2001, terrorist attacks. This makes the statement true.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3972", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Abolitionist John Brown raided the arsenal in which Virginia Town?\n\nOptions: \nA. Harrisonburg\nB. Richmond\nC. Harper's Ferry\nD. Martinsburg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Brown's famous raid in 1859 targeted the federal arsenal at **Harper's Ferry**, Virginia (now West Virginia), in an attempt to start a slave rebellion.  \n\nThe correct answer is **C**.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 153}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3712", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these 1900s tanks were designed and built BEFORE the others?\n\nOptions: \nA. M4 Sherman\nB. Cromwell \nC. Renault FT\nD.  Panzer IV\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Renault FT was introduced in 1917, while the Panzer IV entered service in the late 1930s, the M4 Sherman in 1942, and the Cromwell in 1944. Therefore, the Renault FT predates all the others by decades.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_924", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following African countries was most successful in resisting colonization?\n\nOptions: \nA. Namibia\nB. C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire\nC. Ethiopia\nD. Congo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ethiopia successfully resisted colonization by defeating Italy at the Battle of Adwa in 1896, maintaining its sovereignty.  \nThe other options were all colonized: Namibia by Germany, C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire by France, and Congo by Belgium.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 156}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2026", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which dictator killed the most people?\n\nOptions: \nA. Joseph Stalin\nB. Kim Il Sung\nC. Adolf Hitler\nD. Mao Zedong\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Estimates vary, but many historical assessments attribute the highest number of deaths to Mao Zedong due to policies like the Great Leap Forward. However, precise figures are debated among scholars. Based on common historical estimates, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_61", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A suburb of a city with this name included an iron mine that lent its name to the daiquiri.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The suburb is Daiquir\u00ed, and the iron mine there gave its name to the cocktail.  \nThe city it is a suburb of is Santiago de Cuba.  \n\n\\boxed{Santiago de Cuba}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 119}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_96", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first recorded use of this river's current name, which may mean \"our boat,\" is by Alvise da Cadamosto (\"all-VEE-say da kah-dah-MOH-stoo\"), who met the damel of Cayor along the coast just to its south.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The river is the **Senegal River**, whose name possibly derives from the Wolof phrase \u201csunu gaal\u201d meaning \u201cour boat.\u201d  \n\\boxed{Senegal River}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 152}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_141", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A uranium-containing submarine that ran aground near a naval base in this body of water was nicknamed \"Whiskey on the Rocks.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The incident involved a Soviet submarine that ran aground in the **Baltic Sea** near the Swedish naval base.  \n\n\\boxed{Baltic Sea}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 127}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_223", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The world's longest railway platform is found in this country.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and th