: {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 131}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1028", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Objects used to interact with this substance are often inscribed with adinkra symbols by the Akan people and are called mrammou.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The objects are likely gold weights, and the substance is gold.  \n\n\\boxed{Gold}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 21, "total_tokens": 104}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_658", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adolph Ochs coined a slogan for a business that he owned in this industry, and moved its headquarters to Longacre Square.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The slogan \u201cAll the News That\u2019s Fit to Print\u201d was coined by Adolph Ochs for *The New York Times*, which he owned, and he moved its headquarters to Longacre Square (now Times Square).  \n\n\\boxed{Newspaper}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 135}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_712", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The second president of this organization was a former comparative literature professor at Columbia University dismissed by school president Nicholas Murray Butler.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The organization is the **National Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP)**. Its second president was Joel Elias Spingarn, who was a comparative literature professor at Columbia University before being dismissed by President Nicholas Murray Butler.  \n\n\\boxed{NAACP}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 134}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1039", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A kingdom of this people constantly moved between their summer capital of Peiting and their winter capital of Qocho.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The people described are the Uyghurs, who historically had a kingdom with these seasonal capitals.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{Uyghurs}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 124}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_470", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of the highest-ranking positions in this party, Gauleiter, commanded an entire regional branch of it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 