s": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_537", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Kenneth Westhues said this event was caused by \"workplace mobbing\" and disputed the conclusions of the Massengill Report.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The event described is the Virginia Tech shooting.  \n\nKenneth Westhues attributed it to \"workplace mobbing\" and contested the official Massengill Report's findings.  \n\n\\boxed{Virginia Tech shooting}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 135}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_612", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A company operating in the valley of the Kings River built a 62-mile structure to transport these things.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The structure described is likely the **Kings River flume**, built to transport **logs** from the Sierra Nevada forests.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{logs}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 118}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_784", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A pope with this name opted to remain home after seeing a locust, which sounds similar to the Latin for \"stay in place.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The pope\u2019s name is **Pius**, because the Latin word \u201cpius\u201d sounds like \u201cpi\u0101\u201d (stay), and the clue refers to a locust (\u201clocusta\u201d) prompting a play on \u201clocus sta\u201d (stay in place).  \n\n\\boxed{Pius}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 149}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_812", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Many historians believe that this event was exacerbated by the incompetence of Dr. Willard Bliss.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The event is the assassination attempt on President James A. Garfield, where Dr. Willard Bliss's unsanitary medical care likely contributed to Garfield's death.\n\n\\boxed{The assassination of President James A. Garfield}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 142}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_864", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The man delivering this speech sarcastically asked \"Are fleets and armies necessary to a work of love and reconciliation?\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote is from Patrick Henry\u2019s \u201cGive me liberty, or give me death!\u201d speech in 1775.  \n\n\\boxed{Patrick Henry}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 27, "total_tokens": 121}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_926", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A writer from this country wrote about the \"Tiger of the Plains\" in a work arguing for civilization over barbarism.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The writer is Domingo Faustino Sarmiento from Argentina, who wrote *Facundo: Civilization and Barbarism*, describing the caudillo Juan Facundo Quiroga as the \u201cTiger of the Plains.\u201d  \n\n\\boxed{Argentina}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 142}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_928", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A violent advocate of this cause interpreted a tornado striking Kansas as God's approval for her first-ever protests in Kiowa in 1900.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **Carrie Nation** (often spelled **Carry Nation**), who was a radical temperance activist known for attacking saloons with a hatchet.\n\n\\boxed{Carrie Nation}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 126}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_978", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: W. C. Handy wrote his first popular blues song for one of these organizations, which was rebuffed by GIs with dynamite charges in the 1946 Battle of Athens.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The organization referenced is a **political machine**, specifically the one in Memphis, Tennessee, which W. C. Handy wrote \u201cThe Memphis Blues\u201d about. The 1946 Battle of Athens involved GIs using dynamite against a corrupt local political machine.  \n\n\\boxed{political machine}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 160}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1058", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Irvine Welsh claimed that one of these things was \"ill-conceived nostalgia\" that was \"wrenched from the rancid prostates of senile, gibbering hippies\".\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote by Irvine Welsh is a criticism of the band **The Beatles**, specifically referring to their later work or the nostalgia surrounding them.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{The Beatles}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 136}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1135", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hans Trobst's article \"Fifteen Gallows\" was one of the only foreign reports on purges undertaken by this leader that were justified the following year in his 36-hour speech delivered over six consecutive days.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The leader referenced is Joseph Stalin, whose 1938 purges were reported on by Hans Trobst, and who justified them in his 1939 speech to the 18th Party Congress.\n\n\\boxed{Joseph Stalin}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 169}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1243", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1966, John Gerassi argued that an oligarchical power play was behind a conspiracy exploiting this attitude during which town hall speeches were given by John L. Butler and future senator Frank Church.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The conspiracy described involves the \"Whitewater\" scandal, but the more specific answer is **the \"Whitewater affair\"** or **Whitewater**.  \n\nJohn Gerassi\u2019s argument about an oligarchical power play refers to the Whitewater controversy, during which John L. Butler and future senator Frank Church gave town hall speeches.  \n\nThus, the most common answer is:  \n\n\\boxed{Whitewater}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 185}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1378", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Carolyn Dean analyzed how the Corpus Christi festival in this modern-day country became a site of resistance as it syncretized with summer solstice celebrations.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The modern-day country is **Peru**, where the Corpus Christi festival syncretized with Inti Raymi (the Inca summer solstice celebration) as a form of cultural resistance.  \n\n\\boxed{Peru}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 150}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1435", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Richard Kohn's article on \"The Inside Story\" of this event argues that it was largely stage-managed to bolster the case for central government.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The event described is the **Newburgh Conspiracy** during the American Revolution.  \n\nRichard Kohn\u2019s article argues that George Washington\u2019s dramatic suppression of the officers\u2019 protest was orchestrated to strengthen support for federal taxation power.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{Newburgh Conspiracy}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 147}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1439", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jonathan Winkler's Nexus explains how the a7termath of this event led to unprecedented integration of private business and government research, while Nicholas Lambert argued that its protagonists were unwilling to threaten their own economic networks.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The event described is **World War I**, as both Winkler's and Lambert's analyses focus on its economic and governmental impacts.\n\n\\boxed{World War I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 138}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1449", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Alan Olmstead and Paul Rhode argued that new varieties of this commodity were responsible for its rise in production, against a controversial book with chapters like \"Feet,\" \"Breath,\" and \"Tongues.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The commodity described is cotton, as Olmstead and Rhode disputed the claims in Edward Baptist\u2019s book *The Half Has Never Been Told*, which includes chapters titled \u201cFeet,\u201d \u201cBreath,\u201d and \u201cTongues.\u201d  \n\n\\boxed{Cotton}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 161}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1528", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Daniel Arasse argued that this event amounted to an inverted baptismal rite.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Daniel Arasse argued that the **beheading of John the Baptist** amounted to an inverted baptismal rite.\n\n\\boxed{the beheading of John the Baptist}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 76, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 111}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1616", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem criticizing this government program declares that \"the millet is scattered over the ground, the leaves of the sweet potato are withered,\" which was used as evidence to \u2734re a defense minister.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem criticizes the **Great Leap Forward** in China, and the incident led to the dismissal of Defense Minister **Peng Dehuai**.\n\n\\boxed{Great Leap Forward}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 133}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1637", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An oil painting of this battle displayed at the British Museum inaccurately shows an empress on horseback wielding a pistol and depicts Saint George throwing a spear at the losing army.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The battle described is the **Battle of Vienna (1683)**, often referenced in connection with the inaccurate painting *\"Sobieski at Vienna\"* that depicts anachronistic elements like Saint George and a horseback empress.  \n\n\\boxed{Battle of Vienna}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 148}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1654", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Richard Slotkin's Gun\u1978ghter Nation contrasts the Turner thesis with this man's theory of frontier history, concluding that this man's \"progressive\" narrative was more in\u1978uential.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is **Frederick Jackson Turner**, as Slotkin contrasts Turner\u2019s \u201cprogressive\u201d frontier thesis with Theodore Roosevelt\u2019s more militant frontier narrative.\n\n\\boxed{Frederick Jackson Turner}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 141}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1664", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A ruler of this dynasty whose lineage was questioned took out his sword, shouted \"here is my pedigree!,\" and threw gold coins into a crowd; that ruler of this dynasty commissioned scientists to invent the world's first fountain pen.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ruler described is Tipu Sultan, who belonged to the **Kingdom of Mysore** (though sometimes referred to as the **Mysore Sultanate** or **Tiger of Mysore**).  \nHe famously drew his sword when his lineage was questioned, declaring it his pedigree, and he commissioned early fountain pen-like devices.  \nThe most common answer is the dynasty he ruled under.\n\n\\boxed{Mysore Sultanate}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 196}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1684", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A city that fought to protect these people built a trebuchet that squared off against a machine called the \"cat,\" inspiring a work by Raimon Escrivan (\"rye-MOAN\" ess-kree-VAHN) in which the two siege engines engage in a mock debate.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city is B\u00e9ziers, known for its historical defense of the Cathars, and the mock debate between the trebuchet and the cat is the Occitan poem \"The Debate of the Trebuchet and the Catapult\" by Raimon Escrivan.  \n\n\\boxed{B\u00e9ziers}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 187}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1721", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a speech given in the year of this election, a woman recounted getting beaten in the Montgomery County jail and said \"I question America.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The woman speaking was Fannie Lou Hamer, and the election year was 1964.  \n\n**Correct answer:** \\boxed{1964}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 114}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1804", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these events came as a surprise to noblemen who fought against supporters of the Constitution of May 3rd.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is the **Ko\u015bciuszko Uprising** (or **Insurrection**), as it was launched by Polish\u2013Lithuanian commoners and peasants, surprising many conservative noblemen who had opposed the progressive Constitution of May 3, 1791.\n\n\\boxed{Ko\u015bciuszko Uprising}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 144}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1871", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Samuel Eliot Morison's history of this document argued that Article III, which provided tax support for \"Protestant teachers of piety,\" slipped through without a valid two-thirds vote.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The document in question is the **Northwest Ordinance of 1787**.\n\n\\boxed{Northwest Ordinance of 1787}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 27, "total_tokens": 118}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1894", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A speech given about this personal attribute cites how \"Fuentes and McCafiferty\" died side by side with \"Bowie and Crockett\" at the Alamo.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The personal attribute is **courage** (or bravery), as the Alamo defenders are often cited as examples of it.  \n\n\\boxed{Courage}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 130}}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}]